{"id":"infra","ord":"a0","title":"Infrastructure","desc":"Build system, CI, workspace plumbing. Norm inherited from the rewrite plan (git history has it): one PR per work item; every PR leaves the repo working and CI green.","changed":"2026-08-16T13:04:57-04:00"}
{"id":"scaffold","parent":"infra","ord":"a0","title":"Scaffold","done":"2026-08-09T13:06:54-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #56 (squash ee09573).\n- flake + npins (kolu@4d8a668, nixpkgs), Bun, drishti-style workspace, bunfig.toml isolated linker\n- @kolu/* hydrate + check-kolu-deps scripts\n- justfile whose `check` recipe IS the CI DAG (`[metadata(\"ci\")]`, odu-only — the planned GHA wrapper was dropped mid-flight at the human's direction)\n- linux + darwin lanes, bun2nix from juspay/bun2nix#2\n- **Effect wired in from day one:** effect + @effect/platform-node at the kolu pin's exact version (4.0.0-beta.106) with single-copy overrides\n- packages/core shipped a real @kolu/surface + Effect Schema cell exercised by bun test\n- **Stale:** that package is gone as of see-outline (PR #58), which split it into format/store/surface/server/web","changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:37-04:00"}
{"id":"hm-module","parent":"infra","ord":"a1","title":"Home Manager module #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-10T09:55:14-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #64 (squash ea85270), authored by Grok, reviewed by Claude.\n- **Fix:** review caught a clean-stop-lands-failed systemd bug (Effect exits 130 on interrupt; SuccessExitStatus now declares it clean)\n- **Fix:** review also caught a README snippet that did not evaluate\n- **From the racket audit (2026-08-09):** the racket flake shipped a home-manager module running serve as a systemd user service (Linux) / launchd agent (macOS) with dataDir/host/port options\n- Port it for `olai web`","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:37-04:00"}
{"id":"logging","parent":"infra","ord":"a2","title":"Proper logging #techdebt","done":"2026-08-10T14:55:28-04:00","desc":"Added 2026-08-10 after the chat-agent notice shipped as a bare console line ('no ACP agent configured … so chat is off').\n- **Fix:** log the way kolu does — Effect's structured logging throughout the server (levels, spans/annotations, one consistent format, quiet-by-default with a verbosity switch), replacing the ad-hoc options.log/console.log seam\n- Study kolu's logging setup at the pin and match its shape\n- **Folded in from the sloppiness audit (2026-08-10), same seam:**\n  - serve.ts's fault path calls process.exit(1) from a bare .catch, bypassing the scope finalizers the file itself documents as load-bearing (deliberately untested)\n  - listener.ts still renders a raw String(cause) one file from the Cause.pretty helper built to prevent it\n  - OLAI_ALLOWED_ORIGINS is read inline with no named constant and no docs mention, unlike OLAI_DIST_DIR's exemplary pattern","changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"bun2nix-fork","parent":"infra","ord":"a4","title":"Drop the bun2nix fork #techdebt #upstream","done":"2026-08-10T12:13:40-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #67 (squash 232e774).\n- Upstream nix-community/bun2nix 2.1.2 turned out consumable without flake-parts; the fork input is gone\n- bun.nix equivalence proven by the bun-nix-fresh lane; darwin fix gained; flake.nix header rewritten to tell the new truth\n- **Filed 2026-08-10, a phase-1 watch item never itemized:** the flake's ONE external input was juspay/bun2nix#2 (the rawflake shape), carried because upstream nix-community/bun2nix's nix layer was flake-parts-shaped and could not be consumed\n- Upstream has since shipped fixes the fork lagged (2.1.2 carried a darwin nixpkgs fix at last check)\n- Re-check upstream's shape; if consumable, re-point and delete the fork dependency — if not, PR upstream the rawflake shape and then re-point","changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"serve-surface-app","parent":"infra","ord":"a3","title":"Upstream: serveSurfaceApp #techdebt #upstream","done":"2026-08-10T16:49:24-04:00","desc":"SHIPPED 2026-08-10 as PR #78 — olai's half, and the debt is paid: pin past kolu #2137 AND #2144.\n- listener.ts shrank from 321 lines to one serveSurfaceApp call\n  - plus the two decisions the primitive leaves: whose port this is (the EADDRINUSE fallback), and what a listener event sounds like (SurfaceAppEvent mapped onto @olai/log: stale tab Info, refused cross-site origin Warn)\n- **Kept outside the primitive:** the frame cap, now `RPC_MAX_FRAME_BYTES` inside the primitive with no option to move it, so #71 cannot recur\n- **Moved the OTHER way:** the surface runtime's lifetime, into serve.ts, which built it\n- listener.test.ts retargeted off the number onto the sink (real sockets, asserting on what the logger heard)\n- **Pin fallout (bunfig-invariant, not feature):** @kolu/url-shape joins the hydrate list; ws moves to the root manifest and leaves @olai/server; check-kolu-deps.sh grew peerDependencies\n- architecture.md's 'Owed upstream' note now reads 'Paid upstream'\n- **Evidence:** shutdown.test.ts caught the primitive's teardown hanging under bun (server.close's callback registered while a socket was open — node never sees it); that diagnosis went into kolu #2144, and the fence passes against the primitive now\n\nDISPATCHED 2026-08-10 → Kolu terminal e500de76 (Claude/Opus).\n- **PARKED same day:** the primitive's teardown hangs under bun (server.close registered while a socket is open — caught by olai's SIGINT fence); fix folded into the human's in-flight kolu listener-migration PR (kolu #2144); a re-pin past that merge unblocks\n\n**Kolu side SHIPPED 2026-08-10** as kolu PR #2137 (merged by the human):\n- serveSurfaceApp in @kolu/surface-app owns origin gate → upgrade → stale-tab → heartbeat → serve\n- payload cap sourced from the framework constant (unspellable to undercut)\n- 15 e2e tests\n\n**OLAI'S PAYBACK, dispatchable now:**\n- bump the kolu pin past #2137 (just update-pins)\n- delete packages/server/src/listener.ts's hand-rolled sequence in favor of one serveSurfaceApp call\n- shrink/retarget listener.test.ts (the #71 cap test may be subsumed by the primitive's own)\n- update architecture.md's debt note, and done-mark this item\n\n**Original filing:** Pay back the debt architecture.md has carried since phase 2: packages/server/src/listener.ts hand-sequences origin gate → upgrade → stale-tab check → heartbeat → serve, copied from kolu's own surface-app example.\n- PR kolu a serveSurfaceApp primitive owning that sequence; at the next pin bump olai deletes its copy and calls one line\n- Kolu-side work, zero olai conflict\n- (Filed 2026-08-10 — the sloppiness audit flagged this as a prose-only 'for now' with no tracking id)","changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"viewing","ord":"a1","title":"Viewing","doing":true,"desc":"Seeing your outlines in the browser, kept current with what is on disk."}
{"id":"see-outline","parent":"viewing","ord":"a0","title":"See your outline","done":"2026-08-09T15:36:34-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #58 (squash ac0cba3).\n- Serve a directory, parse and validate the .jsonl files (format core: unique ids, dangling refs, cycles, stored derived state)\n- Render the tree read-only in the browser via a minimal surface view\n- **Visible:** your outline in a browser tab — or the validation error, with file:line\n\nResolved 2026-08-09:\n- Entrypoint is `olai web <dir> [--port] [--host]` (nix-built binary; just serve and nix run wrap it; loopback default)\n- UI is a sidebar of found outlines + one tree per route\n- Mirrors render the target subtree inline, marked (cycle-safe)\n- Nodes render title with styled #tags, derived done/doing/open status, date badge, and desc as sanitized markdown\n- packages/store is born here in load-once form (revision-tagged snapshot, codec seam; watcher/probe arrive with live-updates — see docs/brainstorming/architecture.live-store.md)\n- An invalid set renders an error view listing ALL errors with file:line, grouped by file, cross-file errors in their own section\n- The tree has client-local collapse/expand\n- e2e is Cucumber + Playwright in kolu's packages/tests shape, features written fresh for this item (nothing ported from the racket branch)\n- Styling is Tailwind v4 exactly as kolu does it (utilities inline; no class-validity scanner — accepted trade-off, decided 2026-08-09)\n- Specs: docs/format.md, docs/architecture.md","after":["scaffold"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"live","parent":"viewing","ord":"a1","title":"Live updates","done":"2026-08-09T16:54:33-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #59 (squash ec5aead).\n- Probe-based staleness over the recursive directory, snapshot stream, error cell\n- **Visible:** edit a file or git pull, the page updates without reload; break a file, its outline degrades in place while the rest stays live; a cross-file break keeps last-good and shows the error banner\n\nResolved 2026-08-09:\n- Error scope is hybrid — a file that fails to decode renders its error in place of that one outline (emanote-style) while other outlines stay live\n- Cross-file validation failures (dangling refs, cycles) hold whole-set last-good with the banner (the codec passes decode failures into validate so the snapshot embeds per-outline failures; store stays generic)\n- Deletion is not special (a probe diff — dangling inbound refs are ordinary validation errors, no grace window)\n- The commit()/optimistic-concurrency write gate is deferred to the chat item, where the ops layer is born\n- The periodic backstop probe stays (~60s) alongside the watcher and refresh()\n- Stamps are mtime+size\n- This item also closes the see-outline test gap: packages/store gets real unit tests\n- Design: docs/brainstorming/architecture.live-store.md","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"navigation","parent":"viewing","ord":"a2","title":"Zoom & navigation","done":"2026-08-09T17:18:29-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #60 (squash e036504), which also carried two server fixes approved mid-flight:\n- a busy port now falls back to an OS-assigned one with both facts logged\n- a listen failure reports as itself (ListenFailed) instead of the [object Object] runtime-fault message\n- Zoom into any node as its own page at /n/<id> — stable set-unique ids make permalinks free, surviving renames and moves across files\n- Breadcrumbs always show the canonical parent chain (stateless, even when you arrived through a mirror)\n- A per-view done-visibility toggle (client-local cell, like collapse)\n- Resolved 2026-08-09 (see brainstorming doc)\n- Depends only on see-outline's tree — can run in parallel with live-updates\n- Brainstorming: docs/brainstorming/viewing-web.md","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"search","parent":"viewing","ord":"a3","title":"Search","desc":"Finding things in the outlines. Grammar and filter-in-place shipped as #149/#168; semantic recall is parked on its own node under Someday/Maybe. Children are the open work, PR-shaped; a child carrying from=168 was deferred out of that PR (find them all with prop:from=168).","after":["navigation"],"changed":"2026-08-16T14:38:57-04:00"}
{"id":"md-docs","parent":"viewing","ord":"a4","title":"Documents #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-10T11:11:13-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #66 (squash ed3ef7f):\n- every .md is a page at /doc/<path> with its own sidebar section\n- doc-carrying nodes preview one line and render the document inline when zoomed\n- document text rides the store snapshot (same codec, same revision — no second read path)\n- /media/* pictures route with a both-ends traversal guard (e2e-tested against ..%2f)\n- GFM footnotes with per-block id minting\n- rehype-highlight bundled, no CDN (e2e asserts nothing fetched off-server)\n- Decisions recorded in docs/brainstorming/viewing-web.md §Documents\n- Render the served .md files as documents and link them from nodes' doc fields\n- Moved out of the old editor-growth bucket — it is viewing, not editing\n- **Racket parity (2026-08-09 audit):** relative images served safely (racket's /media/* with restricted extensions), highlighted code fences without a CDN, footnotes\n- Depends only on see-outline's reader; parallel-safe with everything else in this theme","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"journal","parent":"viewing","ord":"a5","title":"Journal & calendar #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-10T08:48:42-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #62 (squash ccb77a1), including a scope addition: the shipped roadmap nodes carry date fields stamped with their PR merge instants (local -04:00), so this feature's calendar renders the project's own history.\n- **From the racket audit (2026-08-09):** a month calendar in the sidebar (day-with-content dots, today ringed, day-being-read filled) plus a /today view\n- All derived from date fields at view time — no stored year/month hierarchy (rewrite decision 11), no `daily` op\n\nResolved 2026-08-09:\n- The calendar aggregates the WHOLE set's dated nodes (any outline — the journal-is-a-query decision realized; no Daily.jsonl filename magic)\n- Clicking a day (and /today) opens /d/<date>, a day view listing every node dated that day grouped by outline with ancestors for context\n- /today with nothing dated today renders an honest empty state (creation arrives with editing ops)\n- The calendar shows the current month with prev/next paging","after":["navigation"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"theming","parent":"viewing","ord":"a6","title":"Theming #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-10T13:06:09-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #69 (squash 430d572), authored by Claude/Opus.\n- Fifteen named palettes picked in the browser, chalk default\n- localStorage + data-theme, no server round-trip\n- **From the racket audit (2026-08-09):** named palettes selected client-side (racket shipped 15, chalk default with AA contrast), stored in localStorage, applied via data-theme — no server round-trip","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"mobile-pwa","parent":"viewing","ord":"a7","title":"Mobile & PWA #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-10T11:00:12-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #65 (squash 4005580):\n- the original racket icons byte-identical (git hash-object verified)\n- a real manifest as server/src/manifest.ts via kolu's layer\n- one column below 48rem with the sidebar as a capped scrolling header\n- 44px touch targets spelled once (touch.ts)\n- visualViewport published as --visible-h/--visible-bottom (lifting the connection dot; left as the chat sheet's seam)\n- no service worker with a scenario pinning it\n- phone e2e at 390×844 plus a laptop scenario\n- **Stale:** the chat full-sheet remains owed to after #63\n- **From the racket audit (2026-08-09):** installable PWA (manifest + icons, standalone display; no offline mode — the app is live-only), touch target sizing, mobile viewport/keyboard handling (racket's visualViewport tracking), and the chat panel becoming a full sheet on phones\n- **Verified 2026-08-10:** today the server ships kolu's manifest with icons: [] — no logo, no touch icon, no favicon — while master-racket carries the complete ORIGINAL asset set (olai/web/static/: icon.svg, icon-192/512, maskable, apple-touch-icon, manifest.webmanifest)\n- Port those original logo assets verbatim; the connection-health indicator shipped separately with PR #61","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"outlines-collection","parent":"viewing","ord":"a8","title":"Outlines as a collection #techdebt","done":"2026-08-10T18:07:08-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #81 (squash e75f157).\n- The `outlines` member was a STREAM carrying the whole corpus in every frame, with the fine-grained part delegated to a client-side `reconcile` keyed on a Solid default the payload never promised\n- It is now a COLLECTION keyed by root-relative file path — declared in the protocol as `keySchema` — served with the batched `deltas` verb: the whole keyed set on (re)subscribe, then one coalesced {upserts, removes} frame per probe tick\n- Wire cost is O(changed files), so a `git pull` that rewrites forty outlines is still one frame\n\n**@olai/store:**\n- keeps the diff it already computed: a published Snapshot names `changed` and `removed`, so a consumer publishing per file does not re-derive it by comparing two whole snapshots\n- it spans the gap between two PUBLISHED revisions rather than one probe — a probe the codec refuses publishes nothing, so what it found is still owed to the next revision that validates, and a path edited-then-deleted is a remove rather than a change\n- still no olai types in the package: it is path talk\n\n**@olai/surface:**\n- declares OutlineEntry — a file's nodes, its `rev`, and its `broken`, which is the per-entity error scope as DATA: an unreadable file keeps its key and carries its errors\n- plus a `manifest` cell for the set-wide facts, whose `null` is the \"never loaded\" bit a collection cannot express (an empty snapshot means the directory holds no outlines; a first probe still running has to say something else)\n\n**Server/client:**\n- the server cuts one revision into entries and maps the store's changed/removed onto the collection's verbs (server/src/outlines.ts), published by one owned fiber so a revision's entries and manifest are one write\n- the client's read side is one module (web/src/client/outlines.ts): the collection's keys in path order are the sidebar's list, and `derive` over every entry's nodes is the one derivation the whole app reads\n- docs/brainstorming/outlines-as-collection.md moves from brainstorming to BUILT, with its open questions answered\n\n**Original filing:** Re-model the `outlines` stream as a surface collection keyed by file path, with the opt-in deltas verb: snapshot on (re)subscribe, then one coalesced {upserts, removes} frame per probe tick — wire cost O(changed files) instead of O(corpus), keying declared in the protocol (keySchema) rather than inherited from a client-library default, per-entity brokenness as plain entry data.\n- The store's probe already computes the change list; expose it as a per-publish summary so the patch computation stays encapsulated in packages/store\n- **Timing open:** bundle with the kolu writeWrappedValue fix (same client layer), or wait until corpus size makes full-snapshot frames hurt; also pushes the frame-cap horizon out","after":["live"],"see":["live"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"edges-ui","parent":"viewing","ord":"a9","title":"Blocked dependencies & edges in the UI #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-11T10:42:38-04:00","desc":"Re-scoped 2026-08-10: the see half moved to the see-refs item (agents theme); this item keeps BLOCKED derivation and rendering.\n- **Filed 2026-08-10:** the format validates after/blocks/see (acyclic, blocks normalized to after) but nothing RENDERS them — racket derived and showed blockedness\n- Derive blocked at view time and render it distinctly from the marks\n- **THE RULE, corrected 2026-08-11** against this item's own filing text above (\"after-targets are not all done\" is `status !== \"done\"`, the trap docs/format.md writes the rule against): `a after b` holds `a` up while `b` is a TASK that is not done — doing or todo — so a target nobody marked never blocks\n- Racket exempted archived nodes from blocking but not from cycle checks, and that asymmetry is kept\n- No stored state — blockedness is derived from the edges and the marks together","after":["navigation"],"see":["see-refs","checkbox"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"title-markdown","parent":"viewing","ord":"a10","title":"Inline markdown in titles #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-11T06:43:14-04:00","desc":"**CORRECTION 2026-08-11:** this done stamp was FALSE from seconds after the merge.\n- commit a56cb65, mis-titled as this item's roadmap stamp, reverted the entire feature out of master (25 files; exact content-inverse of squash e1ab412, verified by the orchestrator's stamp audit)\n- The third such incident from the same morning session (with dd34849/#87 and 12ea294/#83)\n- Restoration tracked as restore-84; this stamp stands for the original merge instant of #84\n\n**Filed 2026-08-10:** racket rendered titles as INLINE-ONLY markdown (bold, links, code — no block elements); the new olai renders titles verbatim with only #tags styled.\n- Port the inline-only discipline through the existing sanitized pipeline","after":["see-outline"],"see":["md-docs"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"checkbox","parent":"viewing","ord":"a14","title":"Status checkbox #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-10T15:33:37-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #75: status checkbox beside the bullet.\n- ☑ done, ◧ doing, ☐ open — from the same derived status the title already tones with\n- open is a visible EMPTY box, not the absence of one\n- read-only (toggling is keyboard-editing)\n- E2E asserts all three faces including empty on an open node\n- **Racket original:** rendered node status as a CHECKBOX beside the bullet (checked / half / empty for done / doing / open); the rewrite showed only strikethrough/title tone\n- Port the three faces as a read-only affordance from the same derived status the styling already reads — open is a visible EMPTY box, not the absence of one\n- No click handler: toggling belongs to keyboard-editing","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"notes-single","parent":"viewing","ord":"a16","title":"Notes: one state, same line #ui","done":"2026-08-10T17:08:58-04:00","desc":"DISPATCHED 2026-08-10 → Kolu terminal fd21b099 (Grok; reviewer at green: Claude Opus).\n- **Ruled:** human, on sight of the shipped 3-way toggle: delete it — no density states at all\n- **ONE rendering, Workflowy-exact** (screen recording 2026-08-10, frame-verified): the note renders UNDER the title on its own line — smaller, dim — CLAMPED TO ONE LINE with ellipsis\n- CLICKING it expands in place to the full desc plus date and see links, click-away or re-click collapses\n- No hover behavior, tap is the same click\n- (Two earlier shapes retracted same day: the 3-way toggle, then a same-line-hover design)\n- The zoomed page keeps rendering everything, always\n- Supersedes the full/first-line/hidden switch from desc-density (#74/#76); the per-place unfold cell goes away with it","see":["desc-density"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"sidebar-tree","parent":"viewing","ord":"a11","title":"Sidebar file tree #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-11T06:33:55-04:00","desc":"**Filed 2026-08-10:** racket's sidebar was a file TREE; the new sidebar is a flat list where nested outlines render as path strings (Daily/2026-08.jsonl).\n- Group by directory once a served corpus has depth — the ported Dropbox data already does\n- **Scope confirmed & widened by the human 2026-08-10** (screenshot of the deployed sidebar): tree navigation of FOLDERS covering BOTH lists — .jsonl outlines and .md documents — today every brainstorming/*.md renders as a wrapped path string\n- Collapsible directory nodes (collapse state client-local, like the outline tree's)\n- **Resolved 2026-08-10 (human):** a SINGLE unified tree mixing .jsonl and .md — a folder shows everything it holds, as racket had — replacing the two flat sections","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"panels","parent":"viewing","ord":"a12","title":"Panel rework: toggleable & resizable","done":"2026-08-11T18:19:57-04:00","desc":"SHIPPED as PR #104 (squash 407edb2; done carries the merge instant). Final head b42b62f:\n- reviewer's 8 must-fixes addressed (phone drawer/scrim/sheet geometry, viewport clamp, transcript unmount, palette '>' failure surfaced, behavioral e2e) + sheet drag-to-snap + 8 cheap takes\n- two ledger-conflict rounds resolved (branch now carries zero roadmap edits of its own — the file changes only via merge commits taking master's side)\n- 18 required odu checks green both platforms\n\nDISPATCHED 2026-08-11 → Kolu terminal c34ee216 (Grok 4.5 high, always-approve; worktree .worktrees/panels, branch panels; brief at .worktrees/panels-BRIEF.md).\n- **#stage review** — PR #104 (https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/104) open: impl (9d373dd), drawer touch-target fix, hickey/lowy refactor (822589f); 527 unit + 173 e2e green locally\n- ten evidence shots verified by orchestrator (rail, pill, palette shell match the decisions; pill photographed only in empty state — reviewer to verify last-message + pulse)\n- **Review DONE** (Claude Opus, split 620b1deb, 2026-08-11; drove the app desktop+phone with a scripted ACP agent, 21 shots): desktop half solid, phone half broken in ways the suite cannot see\n  - 8 must-fixes: drawer resolves position:relative and renders displaced/clipped; scrim and sheet cover the header making its controls untappable; widths don't clamp against viewport; Minimized keeps a transcript subscription for the page's life; palette '>' swallows failure silently; stale README names; tests assert visibility not effect\n  - 10 nice-to-haves (notably: sheet grab handle must drag, not tap-cycle; hand-roll justified for resize, not for the sheet)\n- **MERGE PRE-APPROVED by the human 2026-08-11** — approval opens the gate, not skips the pipeline: squash lands once all 8 must-fixes are addressed, phone evidence verified by the orchestrator, and odu CI is green both platforms at the synced head\n- **#stage addressing-review:** Grok fixing, then master merge (past #103) + odu CI to green; reviewer: Claude (cross-model default)\n- **RECONCILED with the shipped app-header (#101), human 2026-08-11:** the HEADER KEEPS the connection dot and agent toggle (one home for app chrome); the minimized chat pill is only the chat's collapsed state — last agent message + pulse — bottom-right, no connection dot on it\n\n**Filed 2026-08-10 from the human's UI evaluation session**; ONE item by decision (human, 2026-08-10), operable prototypes at https://claude.ai/code/artifact/e8b0f5ad-f293-4982-a4cc-470565ab320e (evaluation grounded in master@232e774 + live screenshots; the prototype's pop-out floating chat window was explored and DROPPED — human retracted it 2026-08-10, chat stays a docked panel).\n- Every panel gets exactly TWO states — open, or minimized-with-signal; nothing closes to nowhere (resolved 2026-08-10, human — the prototype's third 'closed' state and the chat × are dropped) — and the reader owns the widths\n- **Desktop, all resolved 2026-08-10 (human, on the Prototype 1 shell):**\n  - sidebar collapses to a ~3rem ICON RAIL (expand, outlines/calendar/docs icons, live dot — app chrome never disappears) and drag-resizes\n  - chat dock drag-resizes\n  - minimized chat is a pill carrying the LAST agent message, pulsing while a turn runs (replacing the bare >_ agent pill, whose sidebar-footer/corner homes go away)\n  - the connection dot JOINS that pill — one bottom-right chrome strip answering 'is the app alive' (connection state + last agent message; interacts with no-lifecycle's indicator, which this subsumes on every screen)\n  - keyboard map reserved NOW so keyboard-editing cannot collide: ⌘K palette, ⌘\\ sidebar, ⌘J chat\n  - a ⌘K palette is the summon surface: navigation, panel toggles, and a '>' prefix that sends to the agent — this ships the palette SHELL; the palette roadmap item keeps jump-to-node type-ahead and op actions\n- **Mobile mirrors it translated:** the capped close-on-any-tap burger sheet becomes a real slide-over drawer with scrim; chat becomes a bottom sheet with half/full snap points; its collapsed form is a strip above the thumb with the last message (this discharges mobile-pwa's owed 'chat full sheet')\n- All layout state client-local in localStorage like chatOpen — never sent\n- No open questions remain: dispatchable","after":["chat"],"see":["no-lifecycle","palette"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"solid-utilization","parent":"viewing","ord":"a13","title":"Solid utilization: what the client hand-rolls that the framework does better #techdebt","done":"2026-08-10T14:47:41-04:00","desc":"SHIPPED 2026-08-10 (PR #72): all five seams, one PR, each with a test.\n- **(1) ErrorBoundary:** `<ErrorBoundary>` around the shell in main.tsx drawing errors/Fault.tsx — what threw, verbatim, and TWO ways out: a reload (the framework's reloadForUpdate) for a stale bundle, and `/` for a page that is poison, since a fault is usually deterministic for its route and Reload alone would loop.\n  - The fallback also LOGS it: a boundary swallows, so without that line the fault reaches no console at all and a browser test meets it as a timeout on a missing element\n  - Documented as a FOURTH error surface beside the three that are about the files\n- **(2) createSelector:** in Sidebar.tsx (one selector, both lists: what is active is a file) and calendar/Calendar.tsx (the open day; deliberately NOT today, which moves once a day and is meant to redraw the grid).\n  - Worth more than the comment claims: `page()` mints a new object every wire frame, so the old form re-ran every row's comparison on every frame from the server, not only on navigation\n- **(3) scroll.ts:** client/scroll.ts owns every statement that moves the page — top on push, per-entry restore on popstate, and history.scrollRestoration = manual (the browser's restore runs into a page this client has not drawn).\n  - The router says only WHICH of the two a navigation gets, because a push and a pop are the one thing it knows that scroll.ts does not\n  - Positions are keyed by an entry key in history.state, read at the moment they are written rather than copied, and recorded AS THE READER SCROLLS because popstate fires after the position it was made from is gone\n  - Unthrottled on purpose: a trailing write lands after the navigation and would record the old page against the new entry\n- **(4) preference.ts:** grows preferenceChanged + watchPreference — one storage listener feeding the existing theme and chatOpen signals, both started from main.tsx where this client starts everything document-lifetime, and a cleared storage (event.key null) counts as a change rather than as silence.\n  - @solid-primitives/storage's makePersisted was evaluated and NOT adopted: `<html>` is the theme's state and the shell's boot script writes it before any module exists, and this file's degradation contract (storage may throw, the preference stands) is a promise made here rather than trusted to a dependency\n- **(5) clock.ts:** re-reads on visibilitychange beside the timer, and re-aims the timer from where the clock actually got to — in one place, so the rule the file argues for is written down once.\n- **TESTS:** unit for thrownText, preferenceChanged and the clock's wake (a fake document + setSystemTime); e2e for the fault card, for scroll on zoom/back (verified to FAIL without the fix — the page stayed at 64px), and for a theme picked in a second tab of the same browser, left open on purpose\n- SETTLED_SELECTOR now knows three shapes of the app rather than two and world.open() quotes a fault card, so no scenario meets a client fault as a bare timeout again\n\nFiled 2026-08-10 as the follow-up PR #70 asked for (the client stopped keeping a store above the framework's and adopted @solid-primitives/keyed; this audit hunts the same class — hand-rolled code where a Solid primitive is MORE CORRECT, not dependency swaps). Five verified gaps, each with evidence:\n- **(1) No ErrorBoundary anywhere:** the app has three error surfaces for DATA (errors/Page, Banner, Broken) and none for its own code, so a thrown render fault is a dead white tab; #70's RangeError crashed exactly this way. Wrap the shell in `<ErrorBoundary>` rendering an honest 'this page broke' card with the fault and a reload.\n- **(2) The sidebar marks its active entry O(n):** Sidebar.tsx:120/149 computes current={props.active === file} per Link, re-diffing every row on each navigation — while Picker.tsx:31 (theming, #69) already established createSelector as the house pattern with the rationale written out. Apply it to both sidebar lists and the calendar's open day (calendar/Day.tsx:108); matters more once sidebar-tree lands and the corpus is the Dropbox port.\n- **(3) Navigation ignores scroll:** no scrollTo/scrollRestoration outside the chat transcript — router.go() keeps the old scrollTop so zooming from deep in a long outline lands the new page mid-scroll, and back/forward restores nothing the SPA redraw doesn't accidentally keep. Scroll-to-top on push, per-entry restore on popstate; chat/Transcript.tsx's follow-discipline is the house proof this is done deliberately or not at all.\n- **(4) Preferences never sync across tabs:** preference.ts has no storage-event listener, so a theme picked in one tab leaves a sibling tab stale until reload — against the promise clock.ts argues from ('the one stale thing on the screen'). Either @solid-primitives/storage's makePersisted or one listener in preference.ts feeding the existing signals.\n- **(5) clock.ts's midnight setTimeout does not survive suspend/background-throttle:** a laptop asleep past midnight wakes showing yesterday's ring until the late timer fires — the file's own doc names this exact promise. Re-read on visibilitychange alongside the timer.\n- **Audited and REJECTED, so nobody re-litigates:** a router library (routes.ts is five shapes and the hand-rolled pushState router is documented as deliberate), Portal for the fixed panels (no transformed ancestors exist), Suspense (errors-as-data is the design)\n- One PR: the five are independent seams but each is small and they share the review","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:04:38-04:00"}
{"id":"desc-density","parent":"viewing","ord":"a15","title":"Notes fold to one line","done":"2026-08-10T15:31:46-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #74.\n- **Filed 2026-08-10** (human, from a screenshot: ~3 nodes per screen once every desc renders in full)\n- **Workflowy's answer, adopted:** desc renders as ONE dim truncated plain-text line by default — no markdown blocks in the preview\n- The full desc renders in exactly two places: the node's own zoomed page (it is the page's subject there), and per-node in-place expansion — click the first line to toggle the body open and shut, client-local and keyed by PLACE like collapse\n- A per-view density switch beside the done toggle: full / first-line, first-line the default (the first line toggles the body open and shut), the same client-local cell pattern as doneHidden\n- Same visual grammar as md-docs' one-line doc preview\n- Pairs with title-markdown; independent and parallel-safe","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"agents","ord":"a2","title":"Agents","doing":true,"desc":"Coding agents reading and editing outlines through olai."}
{"id":"chat","parent":"agents","ord":"a0","title":"Chat #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-10T12:12:41-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #63 (squash 66d64ff), the largest PR of the rewrite, through three review rounds plus the human's hands-on rounds:\n- ops layer + store write gate + internal MCP + singleton Claude ACP session with racket session semantics\n- full-parity panel (in-place streaming, persistent folds, live tool progress, dual-source model, append-log transcript with break markers, slash completion + show-all)\n- busy visibility in three places\n- mid-turn messages queue\n- packages/chat extracted from the composition root\n- the sigint-hang fix with a real-process regression test\n- the mobile burger (sidebar and chat one tap away on phones)\n- One PR: the chat panel — an ACP session (@agentclientprotocol/sdk) projected into surface events; send, stream, cancel\n- The ops layer is born here (add, mark, move, archive; fractional-ord insertion; temp-file → re-validate → rename → commit) since chat's agent is the first writer; whole-file agent writes stay rejected\n- **Visible:** ask the agent in the web app to check something off and watch the outline update live; a refused write (derived state) shows its unfinished children in chat\n\n**Decided 2026-08-09:** the former agent-editing and chat items collapse into this one; MCP tools for external coding agents are punted to their own item.\n\n**Resolved 2026-08-09:**\n- Claude first via a claude-code ACP adapter\n- the server owns one singleton ACP session (olai is single-user)\n- agent→ops channel is an internal MCP server passed via session/new; ops tool calls auto-approved (permission UI deferred)\n- agent reads via internal MCP query tools only (likely incl. grep), no fs\n- transcripts persist as Claude Code's own session for the served directory so `claude --resume` works from a terminal\n- errors are never silently ignored — only a succeeding StaleWrite retry is invisible, every genuine failure renders in chat with structured detail\n\n**Resolved 2026-08-09, round two:** racket chat semantics adopted wholesale (boot adopts the most-recent session for the cwd via session/list + session/load; picker; foldable tool frames; slash completion; model display; nix-pinned adapter) — full parity in the one PR; query tools are over parsed nodes with file:line, no raw grep.\n\n**Racket parity to preserve (2026-08-09 audit):** session picker (list/switch/new — racket adopted the most-recently-updated session on boot), slash-command completion in the chat input, foldable tool calls in the transcript; write ops auto-commit with racket's message convention (capture:/done:/doing:/move:/archive: TITLE) when the directory is a git work tree, with an opt-out; the archive op rebuilds the ancestor title-chain in Archive.jsonl and references keep resolving after the move.\n\nBrainstorming: docs/brainstorming/acp.md.","after":["live"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"mcp","parent":"agents","ord":"a1","title":"MCP for external agents","done":"2026-08-10T13:16:40-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #68 (squash 64455f7), authored by Claude/Opus, twice re-based over master moves (theming #69, set-fat #70) with conflicts resolved by the agent on instruction: the ops layer as a command an agent launches.\n- **Punted 2026-08-09:** expose the ops layer as MCP tools so a coding agent outside olai (e.g. in a terminal) can edit outlines\n- Chat's internal agent→ops wiring is expected to produce most of this for free","after":["chat"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"create-outline","parent":"agents","ord":"a2","title":"Create an outline","done":"2026-08-10T16:36:06-04:00","desc":"Agents cannot start a new outline file: add_node's plan refuses any file not already under the served directory, and no create op exists.\n- **Fix:** ship create_outline(file, seed?): a validated relative .jsonl path (traversal-guarded segment-by-segment like /media/*), refuse an already-existing file, optionally seed one first node (same shape add_node mints), ride the store's temp-file → validate → rename → commit write gate, with the capture:/create: git auto-commit convention when the directory is a work tree\n- Expose through both faces of the ops layer (MCP tools list and therefore chat)\n- Unit tests on the plan refusals; e2e that a live tab shows the new outline without reload","after":["mcp"],"see":["mcp"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"see-refs","parent":"agents","ord":"a3","title":"see references: rendered, and writable over MCP","done":"2026-08-10T16:26:44-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #79 (squash c04269c).\n- **Filed 2026-08-10 from the leg-pain conversation:** `see` is the format's free cross-reference — validated, and today invisible and unwritable by agents\n- **(1) RENDER:** a node's see refs draw as links to their targets' /n/<id> pages (target's title as the text), on the zoomed page and on rows carrying them — the see half of edges-ui, moved here; edges-ui keeps blocked-derivation\n- **(2) OPS/MCP:** a set_see-shaped op (add/remove see targets on an existing node) through the standard write gate, validation refusing unknown targets with the usual teaching error; MCP read tools (search_nodes, read_subtree) carry see in their output so an agent can traverse references\n- Backlinks (inbound rendering) remain unfiled — this is the forward direction only","after":["mcp"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"bugs","ord":"zz","title":"Bugs","doing":true,"desc":"Known defects, each carrying its diagnosis; per HACKING.md every fix ships with a test that reproduces it."}
{"id":"live-dead","parent":"bugs","ord":"a0","title":"Live view doesn't work at all — and e2e doesn't catch it","done":"2026-08-09T20:34:19-04:00","desc":"FIXED via kolu PR #2133 (the store merge stops guessing keys) plus PR #61 (pin bump and the failing-shape e2e scenarios: mid-insert, mid-delete, reorder, poisoning — asserting the id multiset).\n- Observed 2026-08-09 in real use: a write to the served directory never reaches the page without a manual reload, while the e2e liveness suite stays green\n\n**DIAGNOSED 2026-08-09** (Grok; DIAGNOSIS.md in the live-dead worktree).\n- Root cause is UPSTREAM in kolu: @kolu/surface's solid writeWrappedValue merges each stream frame with Solid reconcile(next) under the DEFAULT key 'id' — but olai's outline nodes are Located records ({file,line,node:{id,…}}) with no top-level id, so every element keys as undefined and any membership/order change mis-merges the client store: missing nodes, duplicated nodes, scrambled lines, and a poisoned store that stays wrong for all later frames until reload\n- Server, watcher, probe, bind and WS frames are all healthy (verified leg by leg; the correct frame reaches the browser)\n- A/B-verified: reconcile(next,{key:null}) or plain replacement fixes mid-insert/mid-delete/reorder\n\n**Why e2e is green:** every liveness scenario edits in exactly the shapes keyed-reconcile survives — whole-file rewrites at stable indices and end-of-file appends — never a mid-insert, mid-delete, or reorder, and never an assertion on the full id multiset.\n\n**Fix direction:** upstream PR to kolu (writeWrappedValue must not assume key 'id' for arbitrary payloads — caller-supplied key or replace policy from the stream definition), plus e2e scenarios that fail today: mid-insert, mid-delete, reorder, mid-insert-then-append poisoning, asserting the id multiset rather than eventual title text.\n\n**Upstream fix in flight 2026-08-09:** folded into the kolu-side agent's scope (branch surface-typed-lifecycle), pointed at DIAGNOSIS.md.\n- Olai still owes, once the kolu pin moves: the failing-today e2e scenarios and the pin bump","after":["live"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"no-lifecycle","parent":"bugs","ord":"a1","title":"Stale server accepted silently — no connection indicator","done":"2026-08-09T20:34:19-04:00","desc":"Diagnosed 2026-08-09.\n- Surface is designed to address exactly this class of bug and olai doesn't use that part: packages/web/src/client/wire.ts calls connectSurface (the no-lifecycle seam) and keeps only .client, discarding the wire status accessor\n- A tab wired to a replaced/dead server just sits there looking fine: on reconnect the new process closes it with the stale-tab code, the wire retires by design (stops re-dialing, reports status 'retired'), and nothing in the UI says so\n- **Fix:** make full use of the framework — derive createServerLifecycle (or consume the status connectSurface already returns) and render a GREEN CONNECTION INDICATOR in the UI (kolu's header dot is the house pattern), with the retired state auto-reloading or showing 'server restarted — reload'\n- **Regression test (HACKING.md):** restart the scenario-owned server under an open page and assert the page recovers; assert the indicator reflects connected/disconnected/retired\n- Pairs with the connection-health pill under mobile-pwa","after":["live"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"no-lifecycle-fix","parent":"no-lifecycle","ord":"a0","title":"The fix in olai","done":"2026-08-09T20:34:19-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #61 (squash 46b3a70), reworked onto kolu #2133 before merge.\n- connection indicator (corner dot, green only when live)\n- retired-wire recovery ('server restarted — Reload' via reloadForUpdate)\n- createServerLifecycle over the status accessor (whose projection maps retired to down)\n- an identity.info surface member feeding the pid echo — which the agent proved was previously a dead gate\n- same-port server-restart e2e scenarios\n- **Decided 2026-08-09:** this PR will also adopt the upstream kolu API from no-lifecycle-upstream once it exists, in the same PR","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"no-lifecycle-upstream","parent":"no-lifecycle","ord":"a1","title":"Upstream: make the framework prevent this #upstream","done":"2026-08-09T20:31:33-04:00","desc":"Shipped as kolu PR #2133:\n- the framework owns the stale-tab handshake end to end (system/identity carries processId, the socket feeds its own echo, rejectStaleProcess deleted)\n- the retired state is a required option on connectSurface (type-level, as preferred)\n- the store merge stops inferring element keys from field names\n- The agent was briefed on the three shapes with type-level required, the self-feeding pid echo, and the projectStatus retired→down conflation\n- **What to PR:** to @kolu/surface / surface-app so a future app cannot silently ship a lifeless wire. To be fleshed out from the PR that comes out of no-lifecycle-fix (decided 2026-08-09)\n- **Preference (human, 2026-08-09):** type-level is always best — the seam should require a status/onRetired consumer at the type level instead of letting it be discarded\n- Other shapes on the table: connectSurface defaulting a retired-state handler (reloadForUpdate) unless explicitly overridden; the app shell (surfaceAppLayer) owning a built-in connection indicator\n- Context: docs/brainstorming/surface-utilization.md","after":["no-lifecycle-fix"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"live-dead-residual","parent":"bugs","ord":"a4","title":"Live update still duplicates rows — one layer above the fixed merge","done":"2026-08-10T13:11:19-04:00","desc":"FIXED 2026-08-10, shipped as PR #70 (squash 298c30c): the client keeps no store of its own.\n\n**DIAGNOSED 2026-08-10**, and it is olai's, one layer above kolu's merge exactly as suspected — but a CONTRACT violation rather than a keying accident.\n- App.tsx reconciled the day's groups (key `file`) and the outline's rows (key `key`) into stores of its own, and what it handed `reconcile` was BORROWED: `situate`/`rowsFor` mint fresh wrappers, but the records inside them are the served set's own Located objects (derive.ts, dates.ts), and `reconcile` unwraps proxies and mutates the previous objects transitively\n- Read two days in turn and the entries inside a group merge POSITIONALLY (a Situated carries no `file`), while the `shows` records either side of that merge do carry one and it matches — so instead of swapping a reference, reconcile copied one node's id/title/date/desc over another node's record, in the live store, which is the set every other page is read from\n- Those writes then invalidated the very memo they came from (`derived` reads every node), so the effect re-triggered itself until the stack ran out: `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded`, frames alternating runUpdates ⇄ completeUpdates\n- Observed in the browser on opening a second day; the Dropbox-port sighting above (a node drawn twice, a day missing from the calendar) is the same class\n- Reproduced headlessly against docs/roadmap.jsonl before any fix — the first navigation never converges\n\n**THE FIX:** no store above the framework's.\n- The rows are a memo, a day's groups are read straight off the page model, and identity across frames — the only thing the stores were for — is a KEYING question, answered where the rows are drawn by `<Key>` (@solid-primitives/keyed) on `Row.key` and on `file/id` for a day entry\n- Nothing in the client writes to what the wire hands it, which is now the rule architecture.md states\n\n**E2E:**\n- `Two days, read in turn, each still says what it said` fails on the old client (day 06 lists `pack` twice) and passes on the new one\n- `An outline that arrives beside the open one leaves it whole` closes the new-files gap this entry named — it is green on the old client too, so that gap was coverage rather than a second bug","after":["live"],"see":["live-dead","solid-utilization"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"sigint-hang","parent":"bugs","ord":"a3","title":"Ctrl+C doesn't stop `just run`","done":"2026-08-10T12:12:41-04:00","desc":"Done-marked 2026-08-10 (human-confirmed): the fix and its regression test shipped inside chat's PR #63 (squash 66d64ff) — this stamp carries that merge instant.\n- Observed 2026-08-10 on the chat branch; a second wedged instance (a store-only smoke server from the previous night) suggests it predates chat\n- **Investigation so far:** SIGINT is delivered and caught (runMain's handler runs), the listener fully closes (no listening socket, no child processes, no TCP connections remain), yet the process never exits — wedged inside Effect scope teardown after all I/O is gone; repeated Ctrl+C is ignored because the handler already tripped\n- **ROOT CAUSE (fixed in PR #63, with the orchestrator's earlier chat-introduced attribution corrected):** NOT chat-specific — master hangs identically whenever a browser tab is connected (the chat agent reproduced it with a master build; the orchestrator's clean master test was an idle server with no tab, the wrong discriminator)\n- server.close waits for every connection, and a tab holds two that never end on their own — the surface websocket and the page's keep-alive — so a server with a tab attached never finished its listener finalizer\n- **Fix:** the teardown now terminates websockets and destroys idle keep-alives before close\n- **Regression test** packages/server/src/shutdown.test.ts: real child process, real websocket, SIGINT, assert exit within a bound — fails against the old finalizer\n- Fix must include a regression test: start the real server, SIGINT it, assert exit within a bound","after":["live"],"see":["serve-surface-app"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"frame-cap","parent":"bugs","ord":"a2","title":"WS frame cap undercuts the framework's #techdebt","done":"2026-08-10T14:09:23-04:00","desc":"FIXED 2026-08-10, shipped as PR #71 (squash 3822a29): the cap is sourced from the framework.\n- `maxPayload: RPC_MAX_FRAME_BYTES` + the ndjson delimiter (the newline rides the wire but is outside what the decoder measures), so the two layers can no longer disagree whatever either of them is re-pinned to\n- **Correction to the audit's account, measured while fixing it:** under bun — what actually runs this server — `maxPayload` was never enforced at all. Bun's built-in `ws` ignores the option and applies its own 16 MiB ceiling, closing 1006 \"Received too big message\" (16777216 delivered, one byte more killed)\n- So the 8 MiB cap was inert in production and the raw-1009 death was a node host's failure mode; the misconfiguration was real, its symptom was not reachable here\n- That is why the regression fence (`packages/server/src/listener.test.ts`) pins the NUMBER — it fails against the old 8 MiB and against any future drift — beside an end-to-end test that a 9 MiB frame is carried and answered\n- Also newly known: while bun's ceiling stands, the framework's handled INBOUND oversize path is unreachable here at all — a frame the decoder would refuse is already past bun's limit, and even one at exactly the cap arrives a delimiter byte over it and dies at 1006 rather than 1009\n- **Stale:** superseded 2026-08-10 by PR #78, which moved the cap inside serveSurfaceApp as an unspellable framework constant — see serve-surface-app\n\n**Found by the surface-utilization audit (2026-08-09):** listener.ts sets ws maxPayload to 8 MiB while @kolu/surface's frameLimit classifies oversize at 16 MiB — an 8–16 MiB frame (a big outline snapshot) dies at the raw ws layer with close 1009, taking the whole socket down, instead of the framework's handled oversize path.\n- **Fix:** source the cap from the framework's constant, with a test\n- Audit: docs/brainstorming/surface-utilization.md","after":["live"],"see":["serve-surface-app"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"editor","ord":"a3","title":"Editor","desc":"Editing outlines directly in the web UI. Everything goes through the same ops layer as the agent (born in chat); the growth items after keyboard-editing are mutually independent — parallel-safe, one PR each.","changed":"2026-08-17T21:27:03-04:00"}
{"id":"self-edit","parent":"editor","ord":"a0","title":"Keyboard editing","done":"2026-08-12T09:15:56-04:00","desc":"Shipped in PR #109 (squash a1d18f7, merged 2026-08-12T13:13:53Z, human-approved).\n- **The Workflowy editing loop through the ops layer:** Enter (new sibling as draft — never writes a blank record), Tab/Shift+Tab indent/outdent, Alt+Shift+↑↓ move, Ctrl+Enter toggle done, ↑↓ row walking with visible caret, Escape\n- titles edit inline via input overlay, descs edit inline on click (post-review fix)\n- drafts commit on blur/Enter/idle and survive a REFUSED write\n- every structural key is one op through the write gate — no optimistic echo\n- **edit.apply intent seam:** client sends indent/outdent/move intents, server resolves placement against the judged snapshot (mirror-anchor bugs fixed under adversarial review)\n- One keyboard registry joined with #104's map; ⌘K/⌘\\/⌘J pinned by test\n- 18 new e2e + unit coverage; 858 unit / 252 e2e green on the merged tree\n- **Human's post-test fixes folded in:** sibling indent, Shift+Enter inline (no box), desc click-to-edit, visible caret\n- DELETE ABSENT by ruling; split/merge/undo/multi-select/drag-drop deferred\n- **Final leg note:** git rerere silently auto-resolved the roadmap during the master merge — caught and restored byte-for-byte; wariness recorded for future merges","after":["chat"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"split-merge","parent":"editor","ord":"a1","title":"Split & merge","done":"2026-08-14T00:46:59-04:00","desc":"Enter mid-text splits a node in two; Backspace at line start merges into the previous sibling.\n- Compound ops (split_node/merge_node) over the ops layer, both faces calling the same op (deferred 2026-08-09 out of keyboard-editing)\n\n**MERGED 2026-08-14** (night slate, SIMPLE — autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization): PR #157, squashed.\n- **Grok review:** 2 blocking (split-at-a-mirror wrote in the target's home file and lost the caret — now follows the 'Enter on a mirror makes a sibling of the PLACEMENT' rule; Backspace on an uncommitted typed row was swallowed — merge now commits the draft first), 4 nits, all addressed at 43c1bae with fail-then-pass proof\n- **Undo design settled by the reviewer:** split's inverse stays merge-as-inverse (remove + was-guarded title would break redo placement); the residual was-hole is documented in inverseOf's split arm — THE HUMAN MAY OVERRULE\n- Nine scope decisions documented on the PR (merge targets previous sibling, not Workflowy's previous visible row; Enter-at-head stays add; etc.)\n- CI 9/9 required green; 1362 unit tests, 437 e2e scenarios; evidence page on the PR","after":["self-edit"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"undo","parent":"editor","ord":"a2","title":"Undo","done":"2026-08-12T13:23:05-04:00","desc":"Shipped in PR #120 (squash b77f929, merged 2026-08-12T17:22:33Z, human-approved with the un-create framing ratified by that approval).\n- **Undo/redo as an intent-inverse stack:** every web edit — structural AND, after the human's live finding, committed title/desc text — records its server-derived inverse at apply time; ⌘Z replays the inverse through the same edit.apply gate against the current snapshot, ⌘⇧Z symmetric; refusals verbatim over the page\n- **Four review rounds (Grok), each closing a real defect with a regression test proven red:**\n  1. redo pollution — a structural op landing mid-replay repopulated the cleared redo side; fixed by putting ALL stack mutations through one serial queue, making the window unobservable\n  2. ledger purity\n  3. the human's finding — 'drafts excluded' had over-excluded committed text ops; title/desc inverses added with a was guard (undo of a retyped row refuses naming the current text)\n  4. the was guard's TOCTOU across ops.run StaleWrite retries — re-checked on every plan attempt\n- **Un-create:** ⌘Z on a row this session created archives it (childless only, GONE aside, cannot be redone — unarchive is parity-unarchive); NO delete key, deferral stays open and docs say so (docs/editing.md, new under #123's split)\n- **Judgment calls ratified in review:** undo of done re-derives the stamp (no op writes a chosen mark value — consistency); position restored as placement (parent + after neighbour), not byte-identical ord\n- Stack: session-local, depth 100, cleared on outline switch, dead in drafts/forms/palette\n- 920 unit + 279 e2e at merge; CI green both platforms at the SHIP head","after":["self-edit"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"dragdrop-multiselect","parent":"editor","ord":"a3","title":"Drag-drop & multi-select","done":"2026-08-14T09:44:30-04:00","desc":"Drag a node to move it with its subtree; Workflowy's multi-select gestures with bulk complete/move/indent/put-away.\n\n**MERGED 2026-08-14** (PR #159, the human approved, squashed at bbfeec70 after resolving against master's #161/#163/#164):\n- a drop is a gap plus a depth; carried rows leave the candidate set where rows are measured (cross-file rows too — a mirror is not a parent, and reordering inside a mirror lands in its home file)\n- pick-XOR-caret enforced in open/start; the Trash confirm keys on the pick's identity\n- Grok review was 3 blocking + 3 nits, all addressed with fail-then-pass proof\n- **In the master merge** it adopted #164's canonical readers/steps (its own copies deleted), took LAYER.row/LAYER.chrome for its lines, and recorded why the refusal bar does not ride saying.ts (a run-stopper follows UndoSaid's no-fade rule) while gaining the missing aria-live\n- Its own flake caveat was closed by #164: 478/478 under the load that used to drop scenarios\n- CI 9/9 required green at bbfeec70\n- **Deferred** (named on the PR, still open): drag-across marquee, touch drag, edge auto-scroll, a delete key (the human's ruling wanted), tone/role unification across five said surfaces","after":["self-edit"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"input-widgets","parent":"editor","ord":"a4","title":"Input affordances","done":"2026-08-14T10:04:48-04:00","desc":"The Workflowy input widgets: `!` natural-language date list (set_date), `#`/`@` tag autocomplete, `((` mirror-creation search (add_mirror — parity nobody had filed: the surface could retire a placement it had no way to make).\n\n**MERGED 2026-08-14** (PR #160, the human approved, squashed at 5af9f68 after resolving against master's #159/#161/#163/#164):\n- built over the ops layer; the palette's list-cursor machinery grew a third keys.ts layer and absorbed two unmigrated copies\n- a latent blur-swallow bug fixed with a timing-free redraws.test.ts (proved fail-then-pass)\n- feb 29 walks to the next leap year\n- **In the master merge** it adopted #164's readers/steps and taught `answering` the completion-list receipt (theListIsGone — one spelling of \"no list\" for three callers), took LAYER.row for the completion popup (with the argued reason the error line does NOT ride saying.ts — it mirrors a live failure, not a lingering said), and closed two parity entries in the brainstorming inventory\n- Grok review was 1 blocking + 5 nits, all addressed\n- CI 9/9 required green at 5af9f68; 497 e2e scenarios, 1491 unit tests on the merged tree\n- **Deferred** (named on the PR): `!` opens the list only, not the calendar; parity-see/parity-after want this widget family but neither verb is on the wire; unmirror's inverse still empty (reason in the arm)","after":["self-edit"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"palette","parent":"editor","ord":"a5","title":"Command palette #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-14T10:24:50-04:00","desc":"Ctrl+K palette over ops and navigation.\n- **History:** panels shipped the ⌘K shell; jump-to-node type-ahead shipped with it (fact-checked 2026-08-13); this item delivered the remaining command-ACTIONS half\n\n**MERGED 2026-08-14** (PR #162, the human approved, squashed at 5b99551 after resolving against master's #159/#160/#161/#163/#164):\n- the ••• menu's verbs as palette commands on the zoomed context (palette/ops.ts)\n- quick capture with racket `olai add`-to-Inbox parity; the Inbox convention written in docs/format.md and on the MCP tool text\n- Grok review was 1 blocking (capture in-flight guard) + 3 nits, all addressed with fail-then-pass proof\n- The master merge kept both palette features intact (23/23 palette scenarios) on #160's third keys layer, with the argued exception recorded for the one write whose promise is that the reader doesn't move\n- CI 9/9 required green at 5b99551; 520 e2e scenarios, 1263 unit tests on the merged tree\n- Evidence artifact: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/524e3160-f738-4b64-b0e6-eb5300eb3bdf (behaviour current; its shot counts predate the final master merge)\n- **Deferred**, named on the PR: op rows are the zoomed node's only; the residual confirm-shell duplication is a `<p>` and a flex row","after":["navigation","panels"],"see":["search","panels"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-mcp","parent":"agents","ord":"a4","title":"Kolu integration: auto-configure its MCP in the ACP chat","done":"2026-08-10T21:32:52-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-10.\n- If Kolu is running on olai's host, the chat agent's session automatically gets kolu's MCP server — a stdio entry (`command: kolu, args: [\"mcp\"]`, forwarding `PADI_SOCKET`, per juspay/kolu's own `.mcp.json`) added to `session/new`'s `mcpServers` alongside olai's internal tool server (`mcpServersOf`, packages/chat/src/agent.ts — today it only speaks the http shape; this teaches it stdio)\n\nResolved 2026-08-10:\n- **Detection targets padi, not kolu web.** The web server may live on another machine reaching this host as a remote (the motivating topology: kolu web on pureintent, this host runs only the padi daemon — https://kolu.dev/padi/). \"Kolu is running\" = the padi daemon is reachable: `$PADI_SOCKET` when olai was launched inside a kolu terminal, else padi's state-root-keyed default socket; plus `kolu` on PATH to spawn the stdio server.\n- **Per session/new**: detect fresh each time a chat session is created, not once at boot — padi starting after olai still gets picked up.\n- **Automatic, no knob**: no flag/env; a knob can come later if ever wanted.\n- **Kolu-specific**: no generic extra-MCP-servers mechanism until a second server shows up.\n- **Upstream option** (#upstream): the detection logic can live in Kolu itself — e.g. a cheap \"is padi reachable\" probe verb, or `kolu mcp` failing fast when no daemon — so olai's side reduces to spawn-and-fall-back rather than reimplementing socket discovery.\n\n**Hazard found 2026-08-10 while orchestrating**, worth knowing before implementing:\n- `kolu` on PATH is not necessarily the host's kolu. Inside a kolu-spawned terminal the padi daemon prepends its own baked agent-tools bundle, and that bundle's `kolu` was an older build reporting the same version string while missing most verbs — filed as juspay/kolu#2146, fixed by kolu#2147 (the injected binary now resolves to the same build as the host's)\n- The lesson survives the fix: a `kolu` on PATH still SPAWNS when it is the wrong build, so detection should confirm the spawned server answers rather than assume the binary is current\n- The #upstream option above covers this too\n\nRefs: https://kolu.dev/mcp/, https://github.com/juspay/kolu/blob/master/.mcp.json","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"commit-button","parent":"agents","ord":"a5","title":"Commit changes on purpose, not on every write","done":"2026-08-11T06:57:37-04:00","desc":"**CORRECTION 2026-08-11:** this done stamp was FALSE from 23 seconds after the merge.\n- commit 12ea294, mis-titled as this item's roadmap stamp, reverted the entire feature out of master (59 files, +390/−4415; exact content-inverse of squash c5bcbdf outside the roadmap, verified)\n- Second of three such incidents from the same morning session (dd34849/#87, a56cb65/#84)\n- Restoration tracked under mcp-commit-manual (option A: restore-83 PR first, then the MCP-face delta); this stamp stands for the original merge instant of #83\n\n**Filed 2026-08-10.** Today every op commits itself (packages/ops/src/git.ts), so one train of thought becomes a dozen commits — a roadmap gardening session produced eleven, each with a full node title as its subject line.\n- Replace that with a commit someone asks for\n- Design: docs/brainstorming/git-commits.md\n\nResolved 2026-08-10:\n- **The feature earns its place for ONE reason: an audit trail of what the tool wrote.** Chat auto-approves its ops and there is no web editor yet, so every write olai makes is one the human did not type. Not for history (descs carry their own dates), not for sync (olai never pushes), not for undo (the `undo` item plans real op inverses).\n- **Manual, not automatic.** Two doors to the same action: a Commit button in the UI, and a `commit` MCP tool the agent calls when it knows its work is done (and can say why). `--commit=off | manual | auto`, default `manual`; `--no-commit` keeps meaning `off`. Never `--amend`.\n- **Derive from git, store nothing**; **never show a text diff**; **writer intent via X-Olai-Writer trailer**; **messages prefixed `olai`**; **busy-repository check decides manual over automatic**; **one derivation serves the Changes view and per-node history**. (Full resolution detail in git history and docs/brainstorming/git-commits.md.)","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:21-04:00"}
{"id":"paste-image","parent":"agents","ord":"a6","title":"Paste an image into the chat","done":"2026-08-11T06:38:54-04:00","desc":"**CORRECTION 2026-08-11:** this done stamp was FALSE from 19 seconds after the merge.\n- commit dd34849, mis-titled as this item's roadmap stamp, reverted the entire feature out of master (29 files, -1830 lines, tests included; CI stayed green because the tests left with it)\n- Discovered when the human pasted an image and nothing happened\n- Restoration tracked as paste-restore (split from silent-errors 2026-08-11, human's call: separate quick PR, no review); the wider audit tracked as silent-errors; this stamp stands for the original merge instant of #87\n\n**Filed 2026-08-10.** Paste (and drop, and pick on a phone) an image into the chat composer and have the agent see it.\n- Today the whole chat path is `string` end to end and the composer has no paste handler at all\n\n**What hardcodes text, layer by layer:**\n- `packages/surface/src/chat.ts` (`send: { input: { text: Schema.String } }`)\n- `packages/chat/src/chat.ts` (`begin(prompt: string)`, queue is `string[]`)\n- `packages/chat/src/agent.ts:115` (`prompt: (text: string)`) and `:549`, where the ACP call is a hardcoded single block `[{ type: \"text\", text }]`\n- `ChatEntry` (packages/surface/src/chat.ts) has only `text`, so a transcript row has nowhere to name an attachment\n- `Composer.tsx` mentions none of paste/clipboard/File/Blob\n\nResolved 2026-08-10:\n- **The agent receives a PATH, as text.** The prompt carries the tmp path; Claude Code reads the file itself. Kolu's model exactly, and it does not depend on `promptCapabilities.image` — which ACP 1.3 does define (`ContentBlock` has an `image` variant carrying base64 `data` + `mimeType`), and which olai could switch to later without redoing the transport. Inline base64 was rejected for now: the bytes would ride the prompt into the persisted Claude Code session.\n- **Bytes land in a TMP dir, not under the served root.** That keeps screenshots out of the store's probe and out of anything `commit-button` would commit. One dir per chat session, removed when the session ends or the server shuts down (the scope finalizer).\n- **Transport is CHUNKED over an existing surface procedure**, not a new HTTP route — a procedure inherits the origin gate and session `listener.ts` already enforces for the websocket, where an upload route would need its own.\n- **The transcript shows a filename chip.** The tab that pasted previews from the Blob it already has; other tabs and any reload show the chip. `/media/*` cannot help — it is guarded to the served root and the file is in tmp — and a second guarded route was judged not worth a thumbnail.\n\n**Copy kolu's derivation rather than re-deriving it** (packages/padi/src/upload.ts, and `scratch.write` in packages/padi/src/surface.ts, at the pin):\n- Two independent numbers: `MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES` = 50 MiB is a POLICY cap on the file; `UPLOAD_CHUNK_BYTES` = 3 MiB is what one frame carries.\n  - Before chunking they were the same number and a 26 MB drop closed the socket with 1009, taking every other subscription on that tab's multiplexed wire down with it.\n- 3 MiB is chosen, not rounded: it must be a MULTIPLE OF 3 so base64's 3-bytes-to-4-chars grouping divides exactly and every chunk boundary lands on a 4-character group, which is what lets each chunk decode independently (4 MiB fails this — 1048576 is not divisible by 3).\n  - 3 MiB raw is exactly 4 MiB base64; plus a <64 KiB envelope that is 4.06 MiB against the 16 MiB budget, ~3.9x headroom.\n  - Base64's alphabet contains nothing JSON escapes, so there is no third expansion inside the JSON string — the one expansion it is tempting to forget, and it is genuinely absent.\n- First chunk creates the file (no `appendTo`); each later chunk passes back the path it was returned and appends.\n- Three details worth taking with it: ONE policy module consumed by both the client's pre-flight gate and the server's authoritative gate, so the two cannot drift on the rejection threshold; `appendTo` carries no authority, because the server re-derives the scratch dir and refuses any path outside it (\"a continuation token that happens to be readable\"); the dropped filename is sanitized to a safe basename and collision-suffixed.\n\nAlso: a phone has no Ctrl+V, so a file input belongs beside the paste handler (mobile-pwa shipped the viewport work this sits on). Drag-and-drop onto the panel is the same machinery once paste works.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"not-every-node-a-task","parent":"viewing","ord":"aA","title":"A bullet is not a task","done":"2026-08-11T06:29:08-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-10. Today every node is a task: status is derived as done → doing → **otherwise open** (docs/format.md:62), so `open` is what a node gets for carrying no mark, and there is no way to say \"this is only a bullet\".\n- `checkbox` (PR #75) made it visible on every row on purpose — \"open is a visible EMPTY box, not the absence of one\"\n\n**Workflowy's model, which we are adopting:** a bullet is just a bullet, completion is a flag you apply to some of them, and an unticked bullet is plain text rather than an unfinished task.\n\n**No decision ever defended the current model.**\n- Nothing in docs/ argues that every node should have a status\n- The rule arrived in ac0cba3 (PR #58, the first rendering PR) as part of the derived-status rule, and racket did the same before it (`checkbox` is tagged #racket-parity)\n- Two things hid it: the only outline olai has ever served is its own roadmap, which really is all tasks, so \"everything is open\" never looked wrong; and format.md:62 argues carefully about WHERE status lives (\"a stored value that currently agrees with the computed one is still a second copy\") without ever asking WHETHER every node needs one\n\n**Why it matters now:** serving the ported Dropbox notes (see sidebar-tree) renders every paragraph as an unfinished to-do, and `search`'s planned `is:open` operator is useless if it matches the whole corpus.\n\n**The defect stated precisely:** `open` answers two different questions with one value — \"a task nobody has started\" and \"not a task at all\". The same shape the manifest cell exists to fix, where an empty collection could not distinguish \"never loaded\" from \"empty\".\n\n**Three shapes, cheapest first** (the human chose the third; the first is a legitimate first step if the screen should be honest before the format moves):\n1. **View-only**: draw the checkbox only where something in the subtree is actually marked. No format change; the model still says everything is open.\n2. **Opt in**: a `#todo` tag or field makes a node a task. Clear, but adds a concept and migrates the roadmap.\n3. **Drop `open` as the residual**: a node is either marked (`done`/`doing`) or has no status at all. Closest to Workflowy, and the honest fix.\n\n**Known cost of (3), not a free lunch:**\n- the parent rule needs a second case — \"all children done → done\" becomes \"count only the children that are tasks\"\n- `blocked` has to say what \"not done\" means for a bullet that was never a task (probably: a plain bullet never blocks)\n- `edges-ui` has NOT shipped, which is lucky: blocked-derivation can be designed against the new model rather than migrated to it\n- Also touches the query tools and the done-visibility toggle, which both read `open`","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"todo-mark","parent":"viewing","ord":"aB","title":"`todo` — the third mark","done":"2026-08-11T07:45:28-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11, straight out of using what #86 shipped.\n- `not-every-node-a-task` removed `open` because it was the RESIDUAL — the value a node got for carrying nothing, which made every bullet a task. That was the defect and removing it was right.\n- But it also removed the CONCEPT of an unstarted task, and those are two different changes\n\n**`done` and `doing` are explicit stored marks.** A third explicit mark, `todo`, obeys the new model exactly: you have to put it there, so a bullet stays a bullet unless marked.\n- What the model forbids is a DEFAULT, not a third face. Nothing about the Workflowy reading argues against it\n\n**The gap showed** the moment the human tried to say \"this is work I have not started\": there was nothing to say it with.\n- The orchestrator reached for a `#todo` hashtag, which is decoration — no checkbox, no derivation, styled like `#racket-parity`\n- The human called it hacky and is right\n\n**Ship:**\n- `Status = \"done\" | \"doing\" | \"todo\"` (packages/format/src/derive.ts:32), stored like the other two, never derived as a residual. At most one of the three on a node, same rule `done`/`doing` already have.\n- The empty checkbox comes back, for `todo` ONLY — `checkbox` (PR #75) had three faces and #86 cut it to two; this restores the third without restoring the default. A node carrying no mark still draws no box.\n- Parents count a `todo` child as an unfinished task, so a theme of unstarted work derives `doing` rather than nothing. Decide and write down what a parent whose task children are ALL `todo` derives — `todo` is the natural answer, but it must be stated, not inferred.\n- `blocked`, still unshipped (`edges-ui`), inherits it: docs/format.md:49 currently says `b` blocks `a` \"while `b` is `doing`\" — with three marks that becomes `doing` or `todo`, and the trap it warns against (`status !== \"done\"`, which reads every plain bullet as an obstacle) stands unchanged.\n- Migration, authorised by the human for this PR only: the nine `#todo` TAGS the orchestrator put in docs/roadmap.jsonl (search, edges-ui, panels, self-edit, split-merge, undo, dragdrop-multiselect, input-widgets, palette) become the real mark, and the tags come out of those titles.\n\ndocs/format.md's Status section is the text that has to change, and it should argue the three-mark shape as carefully as it currently argues the two — the next reader learns the model from there, and `edges-ui` will be built from it.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"orchestrator-in-chat","parent":"agents","ord":"a8","title":"Orchestrate from the chat, not a terminal #human","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-11. RATIFIED 2026-08-15 as the direction: orchestration's home IS olai, operated from the chat.\n\n**THE SHAPE** (docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md, with the worked DAG example and the two gates the day taught): agents (who — docs/agents.olai, shipped), workflows (how — the template DAG), lanes (what's live — the template cloned, marks flipping).\n\n**RULINGS:**\n- template in ONE shared outline; cross-repo progress recorded there\n- babysitting transport is kolu MCP tool calls\n- the waker is olai itself as ACP client over kolu's subscribable urgency/terminals cells\n- titles say WHAT the PR does; chores get done, not tracked\n- the DEFERRAL GATE — a PR whose report carries deferrals merges only on the human's word, each deferral a node first\n- the charter's canonical home is THE GIST, never a repo copy\n\n**WHAT THE DAY BUILT UNDER THIS PROGRAM:**\n- set_doing refuses on blocked (PR #181)\n- properties landed whole (PR #179 — custom, set_prop, prop: search, drawer, stamps), so workflow-template is UNBLOCKED and is the program's next authoring step\n- then lane-cloning, then olai-subscribes\n- hits-carry-custom filed as the board's one-query PR\n- The chat itself gained the model header (PR #176), token usage (PR #178) and wrapping diffs (PR #185) en route\n\n**Verified working — spawning:** lifecycle_create over kolu's MCP cuts worktrees since kolu #2167.\n- The roadmap edits natively from chat through the ops layer with writer attribution","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"oic-worktree","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a0","title":"MCP `lifecycle_create` cannot cut a worktree #upstream","done":"2026-08-13T21:53:22-04:00","desc":"A missing option on an existing kolu MCP verb — completing the socket so one tool call replaces spawning a terminal to type `kolu create --worktree` (debate item 9, \"fix not vault\").\n- **Shipped as kolu #2167** (merged 2026-08-14, head d983f5d0): `lifecycle_create` takes repo/worktree/run; the worktree→create→sendInput composition carries a typed partial-failure payload (stopped-partway survivor reports pinned by wire tests that fail against the pre-fix pass-through)\n- a bare create still behaves exactly as before (pinned)\n- The author named the honest residue in the PR rather than burying it: this composition now exists in four disagreeing copies across kolu's faces, and the real fix is a padi-side lifecycle.createInWorktree — architecture, deliberately out of a fixes batch\n- Directly enables olai-chat orchestration (see orchestrator-home)","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"oic-doc","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a3","title":"The charter stays at the gist — the repo copy was made and unmade","done":"2026-08-15T11:24:38-04:00","desc":"Was \"the orchestrator doc lives at a URL\".\n- **RESOLVED 2026-08-15 the opposite way it briefly went:** a repo copy at docs/orchestrator.md was made and then DELETED on the human's word — the gist (gist.github.com/srid/af6b4bcccf649fb923e4e207a7b93c51) IS the canonical charter, hand-maintained, never mirrored\n- The chat-agent-can't-read-it concern this node was filed for dissolves differently: the chat has web reach questions of its own, and the charter's future in-olai home is the workflows outline (the DAG), not a prose copy","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"hide-done-scope","parent":"viewing","ord":"aC","title":"Done-hidden hides things that are not done #human","done":"2026-08-11T09:12:52-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11, from the first real use of the #88 model. Two intertwined problems, hit on the same node (`orchestrator-in-chat`).\n\n**1. \"Done-hidden\" does not mean \"done nodes are hidden\".**\n- `withoutDone` (packages/format/src/derive.ts:381) drops a `done` row **with its whole subtree**\n- A parent that *derives* done — because its task children are all done — takes its unmarked-bullet descendants down with it, even though nobody ever marked them done and they may be the very findings you wanted to read\n- Live case: `agents` derives done, so the done toggle hides `orchestrator-in-chat` and the four gap-findings under it\n- The human's position, verbatim: *\"done-hidden should mean done nodes are hidden.\"*\n\n**2. A parent whose children are all bullets cannot be marked at all.**\n- The intended shape was: `orchestrator-in-chat` is `todo` (it IS the work), its four children are findings — plain bullets, correctly unmarked\n- The ops layer refuses it: `docs/format.md:49` forbids any stored mark on a node with counted children, as the price of no-stored-derived-state\n\n**The two compose into an absurdity:** the node tracking the chat-orchestrator work is unmarkable (2), so `agents` derives done, so the done toggle hides that work entirely (1).\n- The escape hatch from (1) — mark the work `todo` so the parent reads doing — is exactly what (2) forbids, so #88's fix was defeated by the model on its first day of real use\n\n**Resolved 2026-08-11 — the root cause is derivation itself, and the fix is to delete it.**\n- Deriving a parent's status from its children treats outline containment (notes under an item) as task decomposition (subtasks)\n- It also violates #86's own creed — \"a node is a task because someone said so, never by default\": derivation makes every parent-of-tasks a task by structure, nobody having said so, which is the `open` defect promoted one level up\n- The no-stored-derived-state rule exists only to defend derivation from contradiction; without derivation it has nothing to defend and dissolves rather than needing an exception\n- Neither candidate patch (vacuous-derivation exception, per-node hiding) was taken: each keeps the conflation and adds cases to it\n\n**The design** (the Workflowy model; org-mode likewise stores status per headline and keeps rollup display-only):\n- **Marks are plain stored facts on any node**, children or not. Status is never derived. `read this book` can be ticked with three notes hanging off it.\n- **Delete the machinery**: the `statuses` walk as status, `fromChildren`/`InTheWay`, both refusal sites (validator load error, ops `derived` refusal), and the format.md:83 rule. Net deletion.\n- **Done-hidden means exactly**: nodes whose stored mark is `done` are hidden, subtree included — a done mark on a parent is a human's claim about the whole branch, so the sweep is now justified rather than inferred.\n- **Rollup survives as display only**: a parent with task children may show derived progress (e.g. `3/5`), never a status — it feeds neither hiding nor blocking. Write-time nudges are policy, not invariants: when the last unfinished task child goes done, suggest marking the parent done; `set_done` over unfinished task children may warn. Never a load invariant — a merged file always loads.\n- **`blocked` (edges-ui) reads stored marks**: `doing` or `todo` blocks, a markless node never does. To block on a branch, mark the branch.\n- **Merge safety improves**: marks merge line-wise with no cross-line invariant a clean merge can break. (Today: mark a leaf in branch A, add a task child under it in branch B — clean textual merge, unloadable set.)\n- **Migration**: stored marks on the roadmap parents that should read as something (e.g. `bugs`/`infra` done, `viewing`/`agents` doing), through the format's own writer, like #88's migration.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"mcp-fail-visible","parent":"bugs","ord":"a5","title":"A failed MCP server is invisible in the UI","done":"2026-08-13T13:51:08-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11, from the kolu-not-detected incident. An MCP server that fails to attach to a chat session must be VISIBLE.\n- **The human's position:** MCP must NOT fail silently\n- **Shipped as PR #140** (squash 1c56f90), 2026-08-13\n  - A strip under the chat panel header — master's three-surface vocabulary, one alarm dot, nothing on a healthy session — states the fact in the server's own words: refused the identity read / closed without answering / did not answer within 5s / could not be started\n  - One probe answers both halves (serverOf / missingFrom); a `servers` event lands on the existing chat cell before every session opens; `MissingServer.where` names the probed binary\n  - \"Never installed\" (no kolu on PATH, no PADI_SOCKET) is deliberately not a failure — but PADI_SOCKET set with kolu absent from the process's PATH is, with its own sentence (the review's crux residual, closed in the delta)\n- **The `/simplify` pass found and fixed a live crash one file over:** a bad OLAI_ACP_AGENT dumped an uncaught ENOENT stack, then blamed `initialize`; the exec-failure axis moved to pipes.ts and both subprocess callers race `unstartable`\n- **Pipeline:** Grok review — zero MUST-FIX; all six NICE-TO-HAVEs taken in the delta (the deadline pin cost 150ms not 5s; the @phone scenario asserts the strip; the NTH#1 test caught the suite reading this machine's ambient PADI_SOCKET)\n- DELTA-OK; CI 10/10 green on kolu-ci-1 at 16b8be5\n- The ci-2/ci-4 ~4m42s e2e walls struck again on two SHAs and were judged host-side by the reviewer — failed logs preserved this time","see":["kolu-detect-primary"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-detect-primary","parent":"agents","ord":"a9","title":"Kolu detection must find the primary padi — delegate detection to kolu #upstream","done":"2026-08-11T09:58:21-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11, from the same incident. Multiple padi daemons on one host are EXPECTED and normal (dev/e2e state roots beside the main one).\n- But olai's probe spawned `kolu mcp` with no `PADI_SOCKET` and `kolu mcp` refuses to choose among daemons — so detection answered \"no kolu\" on a healthy host\n- **The human's position:** selection belongs in kolu; olai deliberately refuses to reimplement discovery\n- Upstream path resolved 2026-08-11 with the human's personal approval; done-stamped then\n\n**The leftover — probe-as-evidence — SHIPPED 2026-08-14, both sides** (debate item 9, filed against this paid item per grok's disposition, no second node):\n- kolu #2168 (merged) ships the zero-dependency leaf `@kolu/detect` — `detect()`/`probe()` answering tagged `Detected`/`ProbeFailure`, reading the live-daemon identity resource, racing exec failure, editorializing nothing (notOnPath deliberately reasonless — the judgement is the consumer's; no env reads, no throws; the review's one MUST-FIX, a PADI_SOCKET inherit leak where probe and returned spawn recipe could disagree, fixed red-first)\n- olai #150 (squash be9dc95c, merged on the human's approval) shrinks packages/chat/src/kolu.ts onto the socket with the hard constraint held end to end: kolu.test.ts byte-for-byte unmodified through authoring, review fix, and repin — mcp-fail-visible's sentences survive verbatim, proven by the untouched pins and the a_failed_mcp_server e2e\n- Pinned to kolu master 39b97df6 (contains #2166+#2168; the next ordinary bump picks up #2167)","see":["mcp-fail-visible","kolu-mcp"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"surface-mcp","parent":"agents","ord":"aA","title":"One surface for browser and agents: project the surface into MCP #upstream","done":"2026-08-14T23:32:06-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11: adopt kolu's surface-MCP so the browser and agents share ONE surface.\n- Largely landed via PR #94 (both MCP faces)\n\n**AUDIT MERGED 2026-08-14** (PR #167, the human approved, squashed at 1fd9457 after resolving the #168 seam — the resolution exercised the PR's own property on #168's fields: SearchRequest gained file/under/operator-prose, SearchAnswer gained refusals, filter.ts's Refusal promoted to Schema, the duplicate SearchRefusal deleted; dropping refusals now fails ops+web+server together where before one side compiled on):\n- docs/brainstorming/surface-mcp-positions.md holds the audit with receipts against master\n- two positions already true (subscribable resources; deps-check by construction)\n- two closed (verbs-drift unrepresentable via format/searching.ts; refusal contract pinned across all four OpFailure kinds on both faces)\n- the bridge priced (418 MB / 2099 fds, method written) and gated upstream\n\n**THE HUMAN'S RULING** (2026-08-14, night slate): reads-on-the-floor implemented tonight; watcher-fd-cost investigated tonight, fixed if the fix is contained; per-face-expose and mcp-bridge MOVED OUT to Agents (kolu ask filed + kolu PR drafted overnight, merge is the human's).\n- This parent closes when its two remaining children do","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"surface-mcp-viewing","parent":"surface-mcp","ord":"a0","title":"Viewing over surface-mcp: agents subscribe the browser's cells","done":"2026-08-11T14:38:08-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11, split out of the parent as the slice adoptable before web editing.\n- **Scope:** adopt `@kolu/surface-mcp` (`serveSurfaceAsMcp`) for olai's READ side — the surface's cells exposed as subscribable MCP resources (default-deny `expose` list), so an agent watches the same live rows the browser draws; the existing query tools ride as bespoke tools unchanged\n- Design: docs/brainstorming/surface-mcp-viewing.md\n\n**Shipped 2026-08-11 as PR #94** (squash), the whole chain in one day:\n- kolu#2155 upstream (ToolFailure/structuredContent/instructions/title), pin bump, then the gated commit\n- ops/mcp.ts (227 lines) and mcp/stdio.ts (83) deleted, both faces flipped onto serveSurfaceAsMcp\n- documents exposed as a resource on #95's shape\n- **Four SDK gaps closed en route:** stdin-end drain, bespoke half-duplex HTTP transport where SSE hung e2e, Schema.Struct({}) anyOf wrapping that broke every no-arg call, plus a same-id waiter collision\n- **Behaviour changes recorded and fenced:** unknown tool → isError, destructiveHint derived from mutates, additionalProperties drift\n- **Acknowledged residual:** a handler that never replies leaves the drain counter stuck — pre-existing class, stated on the PR\n- Write tools stay bespoke until the Editor-theme design settles the parent","after":["edges-ui"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"md-render","parent":"viewing","ord":"aD","title":"Markdown rendering, perfected","done":"2026-08-11T13:08:50-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 on the human's ask. Documents (.md) and notes render through the one remark/rehype pipeline (gfm, sanitize, highlight — bundled); the rendering has never had a polish pass.\n- **Method, set by the human:** the agent screenshots real rendered markdown, the orchestrator gives concrete visual feedback, iterate to done — same evidence loop the orchestrator protocol now requires anyway\n\n**Now** (2026-08-11):\n- Kolu terminal: `7cc6c6da` (Claude Opus, YOLO), worktree `.worktrees/md-render`, branch `md-render`; reviewer split `f26ebf9d` (Grok)\n- Stage: #review — APPROVED by srid; resolving DIRTY vs master, merges on green\n- PR: https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/92","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"run-reload","parent":"infra","ord":"a5","title":"`just run` auto-reloads on source change","done":"2026-08-11T10:45:01-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 on the human's ask. `just serve` watches; `just run` deliberately does not (its comment says so). Wanted: auto-reload on source change for `just run`, with the recipe comment updated to the new truth and the sigint behaviour unregressed. Review waived by the human; evidence is a transcript in the PR description."}
{"id":"load-perf","parent":"bugs","ord":"a6","title":"Roadmap initial load feels very slow","done":"2026-08-12T08:24:51-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 by the human. Symptom: initial load of the roadmap in the web UI is subjectively very slow.\n- Dispatched as measurement + root-cause analysis FIRST — phase breakdown (server load/validate/derive, wire payload, client bundle/render) with hard numbers and a named dominant term; the fix is a separate dispatch after the human reads the RCA\n\n**P0 shipped 2026-08-11:** PR #93 (squash f079b7b).\n- build-time .br/.gz siblings for /assets/*, negotiated by @kolu/surface-app's existing static layer\n- 977 KB → ~253 KB brotli on the wire, browser-verified\n- The RCA and measurement harness were dropped from the PR by the human's own hand (they live in the PR history at 624ffba if ever wanted)\n- P2 shipped separately as snapshot-scale (PR #95)\n- **OPEN:** P1 — code-split markdown/highlight off the critical path (the remaining long-task cost) — undecided, awaiting the human","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"snapshot-scale","parent":"bugs","ord":"a7","title":"First snapshot carries every document body — must scale to 1000s of .md files","done":"2026-08-11T11:50:45-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11, escalated by the human from load-perf P2: the manifest cell in the FIRST websocket snapshot inlines the full text of every .md document in the served set (~124 KB of the ~212 KB snapshot for docs/, measured in LOAD-PERF-RCA.md).\n- **The human's requirement, verbatim intent:** olai must support directories with THOUSANDS of .md files — a wire that ships every body up front is O(corpus) on first paint and therefore not acceptable, regardless of perf feel today\n\n**Shape:** documents become a collection on the surface — the first snapshot carries only what the sidebar draws (path, title); a body travels when a document is opened (lazy fetch or per-document subscription).\n- This is a WIRE change only: the server still loads and validates the whole set (format.md's rule — doc references must be checkable — is untouched)\n\n**Interactions:**\n- dovetails with surface-mcp-viewing — kolu surface-mcp projects collections as templated resources, so the documents-as-collection shape serves browser and agents alike; the viewing-slice design (terminal d5df9f63, in flight at filing) must anticipate this shape rather than exposing today's body-carrying manifest cell\n- At 1000s of files the server-side whole-set revalidation cost also deserves its own measurement before it surprises anyone — noted here, not scoped here","see":["load-perf","surface-mcp-viewing"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"batch-capture","parent":"agents","ord":"aD","title":"Batch capture: a subtree in one MCP call","done":"2026-08-11T19:17:10-04:00","desc":"SHIPPED as PR #106 (squash 839ab6a; done carries the merge instant). Final head 258382f:\n- add_node grows recursive children AND — human's ratification reversing the author's decline — create_outline seeds a whole tree, same capture shape, refused seed leaves NO file\n- One call/plan/validation/atomic write/commit; marks ride through the one stampOf seam (#103 day rules hold)\n- captured names every minted node\n- MCP hosts reject $ref so nesting unrolls three levels with the planner refusing deeper BY NAME (silent leaf-loss guarded)\n- Schema cost measured: +1523B after prose-dedupe mitigation; the further 600B description-strip DECLINED, human endorsed — an agent-facing schema teaches its own field shapes\n- Review (Grok): approve, zero must-fixes, probes independent\n- 577 unit + 183 e2e; 24/24 checks green both platforms\n\nDISPATCHED 2026-08-11 → Kolu terminal d94c7864 (Claude Opus, YOLO; worktree .worktrees/batch-capture; brief at .worktrees/batch-capture-BRIEF.md).\n- **#stage review** — PR #106 (https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/106) open: impl + hickey/lowy + /simplify pushed; 553 unit + 172 e2e green locally; evidence (one call, 15 nodes, 4 levels, 19ms, one commit, ref-free schema) in .worktrees/batch-capture-out/\n- **Notable:** MCP hosts reject $ref so the recursive schema is UNROLLED to three levels, planner refuses deeper by name (a schema-dropped child must never silently lose leaves); nested-schema prose dedupe shrank the tool table 13239→11085 bytes; one declined altitude finding flagged for review\n- **REVIEW DONE** (Grok, split 02207bef, 2026-08-11): APPROVE, zero must-fixes — atomicity, schema unroll, stampOf seam, captured, placement, neighbor round-trip all verified under independent MCP probes; declined altitude finding endorsed. Four nice-to-haves.\n- **#stage extending:** 3 of 4 nice-to-haves taken (neighbor test hardened to byte-identity of untouched lines), CI was fully green at 60b9921 (20 nodes both platforms, 574 unit)\n- then the human RATIFIED THE OTHER WAY on #4 (2026-08-11): create_outline seeds a whole TREE in this PR, same recursive capture shape, refused seed refuses the create (no empty outline); wire-cost doubling to be mitigated or measured\n- Opus building; re-CI; then FIELDED to the human at green — no pre-approval, he decides the merge. Reviewer: Grok (cross-model)\n- **SHAPE decided by the human 2026-08-11:** add_node grows an optional recursive children field (title + optional desc/date/id/mark per child) — no dedicated add_subtree tool, no generic batch envelope. One plan, one validation, one atomic write, one commit.\n\nFiled 2026-08-11 from the human watching a chat agent capture a house outline: every child is its own add_node call, so a subtree is N sequential tool calls (screenshot: ~13), each riding the FULL write gate — whole-set revalidation, temp file, rename — and each costing the agent a round trip.\n- Structural, not incidental: the MCP surface (packages/ops/src/tools.ts) has no batch op at all\n- **The fix is also an atomicity fix:** the write gate is already all-files-or-none, so ONE op planning N records validates once and lands atomically — today a failure mid-sequence leaves a half-captured subtree behind\n- **Shape to decide at dispatch:** (a) add_node grows an optional recursive children field (each child: title + optional note/date/id/mark, ids minted as today); or (b) a dedicated add_subtree tool taking a nested tree. Either keeps one plan → one validation → one write → one commit.\n- Explicitly OUT unless separately wanted: a generic batch envelope mixing arbitrary op kinds in one call — cross-op transactionality is a bigger design than capture needs\n- Also worth a look at dispatch: whether set_desc/set_date on a just-added node can ride the same plan (capture-with-note is the common agent gesture)","see":["mcp"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"precompress-upstream","parent":"upstream-dist-socket","ord":"a0","title":"Upstream: buildSurfaceClient should emit precompressed siblings #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T19:49:20-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 from PR #93's review (this debt had no tracked home; the convention is an #upstream node, not a PR-body note). One half of the parent's ONE dist socket.\n- **The fact:** @kolu/surface-app's freshStaticLayer already NEGOTIATES precompressed assets (.br then .zst then .gz under the immutable prefix; identity when missing; shell never compressed; compressed media refused)\n  - but buildSurfaceClient does not EMIT the sibling files, so every consumer re-derives the post-step; olai's is packages/web/src/precompress.ts (PR #93)\n- **The ask:** a precompress option (or always-on) on buildSurfaceClient, single-sourcing what its own static layer serves\n- **When it lands:** olai deletes precompress.ts","see":["load-perf"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"doc-toc","parent":"viewing","ord":"aE","title":"Documents need a table of contents","done":"2026-08-11T14:31:32-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 by the human while reading his real brainstorming/*.md corpus through the perfected renderer: a long document (architecture notes run hundreds of lines) has no way to survey or jump — \"we need ToC.\"\n\n**Shape settled at dispatch:** heading anchors first (rehype-slug + autolinked headings, sanitize schema admitting the anchor ids deliberately), then the ToC derived from the heading tree at view time — nothing stored.\n- In-page collapsible won over a floating rail; notes never get one (a note is a tree row, not a page)\n\n**Shipped 2026-08-11 as PR #100** (squash cc899c5):\n- platform `<details>` contents, heading self-anchors\n- sanitise.ts asserting against the live default schema\n- six e2e scenarios asserted against the page and mutation-tested by the reviewer\n- single-pipeline-run pinned by identity, ToC keyed on file\n- **Known trade, disclosed hard:** the id namespace hashes the whole body, so ANY edit remints every heading fragment — stable permalinks are a different, future change","see":["md-render"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"keysbus-upstream","parent":"infra","ord":"a7","title":"Upstream: keysBus broadcasts the full key set per new key #upstream","done":"2026-08-13T19:42:25-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 from PR #95 (snapshot-scale); a fix, not a receptacle (both debates).\n- **Shipped as kolu #2166** (merged 2026-08-13): a same-tick bulk add of M keys now costs ONE keys frame and ONE readAll (was O(M·N) full-set rebroadcast per key), with same-tick membership bursts coalesced\n- pinned by tests that fail against pre-fix server.ts (expected 100 frames to be 1), and the six pre-existing membership-contract cases untouched\n- Grok-reviewed clean; complete two-platform durable CI pass\n- olai benefits on its next kolu pin bump (riding olai#150's repin)","see":["snapshot-scale","surface-mcp-viewing"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:12-04:00"}
{"id":"smv-kolu-pr","parent":"surface-mcp-viewing","ord":"a0","title":"kolu: ToolFailure + instructions + title land in surface-mcp #upstream","done":"2026-08-11T13:13:36-04:00","desc":"The upstream gate: structuredContent on error results (ToolFailure), passthrough, and BespokeTool title.\n- Scope: structuredContent on error results (ToolFailure); server-level instructions passthrough; title on BespokeTool; ToolFailure adopted in kolu mcp's own sendInput\n- **Design approved** by srid 2026-08-11\n- In kolu's gauntlet on branch `surface-mcp-structured` (terminal `7be1fc95`)\n- **Done when:** srid merges the kolu PR\n- PR: https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2155 (gauntlet in progress)\n\n**Now** (2026-08-11):\n- Kolu terminal: `7be1fc95` (Claude Opus, YOLO), kolu repo, branch `surface-mcp-structured`\n- Stage: #review — gauntlet reviews posted, evidence posted, CI settling; srid merges the kolu PR personally\n- PR: https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2155\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"smv-pin-bump","parent":"surface-mcp-viewing","ord":"a1","title":"Bump olai's kolu pin to a revision carrying it","done":"2026-08-11T14:38:08-04:00","desc":"olai consumes @kolu/* hydrated from the Nix-pinned kolu revision — an open PR is not consumable.\n- **Fix:** update-pins to a kolu master SHA containing the surface-mcp changes\n- check-kolu-deps.sh and the root dependency list move with the pin\n- Whatever other upstream movement rides the bump comes along (normal)\n- **Optional shortcut (pre-ratified):** once the kolu PR's API is final post-gauntlet, the PR #94 agent may prove the final commit against a temporary pin of that revision\n  - Lands only after the real bump\n","after":["smv-kolu-pr"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"smv-gated-commit","parent":"surface-mcp-viewing","ord":"a2","title":"The gated final commit: dispatch deleted, faces flipped","done":"2026-08-11T14:38:08-04:00","desc":"bespokeFrom(TOOLS, ops) carrying name/title/description; olai mcp (stdio) and the /mcp route flipped onto serveSurfaceAsMcp; ops/src/mcp.ts (227 lines) and mcp/stdio.ts (83 lines) deleted. Then PR #94 leaves draft, CI green per odu, review round, and it is fielded for srid's approval.","after":["smv-pin-bump"]}
{"id":"mirror-status","parent":"bugs","ord":"a8","title":"A mirror does not reflect its target's mark","done":"2026-08-11T13:01:24-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 by the human, seen on the live roadmap.\n- **Bug seen:** a mirror of a node whose target carries doing draws a plain bullet (no checkbox), where the target itself draws the half-filled box\n- Screenshot-confirmed on the \"Markdown rendering, perfected\" pair\n- **Pointer for the fix:** packages/format/src/derive.ts's `Derived.status` doc comment PROMISES mirror coverage (\"a mirror standing for whatever its target stores, since that is what it shows\")\n  - Either the #90 rewrite (stored-only status) dropped the mirror-follows-target hop from the map builder while keeping the comment\n  - Or the row/checkbox path looks the status up under the mirror's own id instead of what it shows\n  - Same question for the blocked index and progressOf: a mirror must ask everything of its TARGET\n- Fix per HACKING.md ships with a test that reproduces: mirror of a doing node shows doing; of a todo node shows todo incl. the empty box; of a done node hides under done-hidden with its subtree ONLY per the done rules; bullet target still shows nothing\n\n**Diagnosed 2026-08-11** (terminal `a1f792c9`, PR #96):\n- NOT a mirror bug — mirrors reflect their target's mark correctly\n- PR #96 (+90/−0, tests+docs) locks that promise at both layers so it cannot silently break: every mark through the rows, both halves of the blocked glyph on a mirror row, done-hidden on a mirror-of-done, and the format.md paragraph (a mirror asks everything of what it shows; a see inherits none of it)\n\n**The screenshot's real cause:**\n- Now entries are regular nodes carrying see (the Now convention dropped real mirrors 2026-08-10 at 849eb9b, because a mirror's four fields cannot hold the terminal/stage/PR prose)\n- A markless node draws a bullet — correct under stored-only status\n- **OPEN, a roadmap-convention call for the human:** should Now entries reflect their item's mark?\n  - (a) back to real mirrors — marks reflect for free, but the prose must live elsewhere\n  - (b) keep see-nodes, status stays a hashtag in the title (today)\n  - (c) mark the Now entries by hand — legal under stored-only, but a second copy to keep in sync\n\n**Shipped 2026-08-11 as PR #96** (squash d4c7df2): the test-lock at both layers plus the format.md paragraph.\n- The Now convention itself was fixed the same day: Now entries are real mirrors again, with the tracking prose on the items\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"log-pretty","parent":"infra","ord":"a8","title":"Pretty logs on a TTY, logfmt everywhere else","done":"2026-08-11T14:31:06-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 from the human's ask (\"improve logging for human-friendliness, retaining agent-friendly format\").\n- Today `@olai/log` emits Effect's logfmt through one logger (`Logger.consoleLogFmt` / `formatLogFmt`, packages/log/src/sinks.ts) on every destination — correct for machines, dense for a human at a terminal\n\n**The design:** split by DESTINATION, not format.\n- When stderr is a TTY: a pretty sink (Effect ships `Logger.consolePretty`: local time, coloured level, message first, key=values dimmed after)\n- When piped / under systemd / in tests: logfmt byte-identical to today — the `@olai/log` testlib decoder and any agent parsing depend on it, so the pretty sink may only exist where no machine reads\n- `OLAI_LOG=logfmt|pretty` forces either way\n- Zero change to `toStdout`/`toStderr` call sites: the TTY check lives inside the sink layer\n\n**Shipped 2026-08-11 in two parts:**\n- PR #97 (squash 87cf89f) landed the split; its review completed post-merge — a process misfire, recorded on the PR itself\n- PR #99 (squash, tip f4ccd3e) carried the findings:\n  - `prettyFor(stream)` reading colour at emit time\n  - Wiring tests for both sinks that mutation-testing proved discriminating (three rounds of \"helper tested, wiring not\" before the lock actually held)\n  - `NO_COLOR`\n  - Per-logger `LogToStderr` scoping\n  - `OLAI_LOG` pinned at every harness spawn site\n  - The knob documented in docs/architecture.md\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"mcp-mirror-op","parent":"agents","ord":"aE","title":"The ops layer cannot place a mirror","done":"2026-08-11T22:13:42-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #117** (squash 7866e08), AUTO-MERGED by the orchestrator 2026-08-12T02:13:25Z under the overnight pre-approval — the second fully autonomous merge.\n- **Gate record:** Grok review (six findings, all taken — teaching referenced-retire refusals, Now enumerable via placed/mirrors reads, query tests, master sync)\n- odu 20/20 both platforms at 4d0dd84, CLEAN, roadmap zero-diff\n- Evidence transcript spot-checked by the orchestrator (containment-cycle refusal naming the loop; did-you-mean; placement-retire leaving the target byte-identical)\n- add_mirror / remove_mirror / set_after ship on both faces; ops are LEDGER-COMPLETE — the orchestrator's scripted-edit era ends when its MCP server reconnects onto this build\n\n**Dispatched 2026-08-11** (overnight slate) -> Kolu terminal `1bb73fb1` (Claude Opus, YOLO; reviewer Grok, split `11d79c7f`)\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-node-context","parent":"agents","ord":"a7","title":"Ask the agent about this node: selection becomes chat context","done":"2026-08-13T14:19:23-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11. **Shipped as PR #141 (squash 80e4d65), 2026-08-13.**\n\n**Direction one — arm from a row:**\n- A row's ••• \"Ask agent\" arms the composer with the shown node (a mirror arms what it is a placement of) and opens the panel\n- On the wire the context is ids only, resolved server-side through the same `Query.foundOf` that answers `read_node`, so a context line and a tool call cannot disagree\n- The agent gets one line under the message — a handle it can act on via MCP, never a copy\n\n**Direction two — transcripts point at rows:**\n- Chips on the sent message\n- The node an olai write was about (`Applied.id` finally crosses the wire)\n- Ids the agent writes in backticks become pressable exactly when the loaded set declares them — marked with the RESOLVED id, so a placement id in prose lands on the node it shows\n- Pressing focuses in place when the node is on the page (the address stays put — pinned in e2e) and navigates when it isn't\n- An armed node that has gone refuses the send in ops' own notFound words and the composer restores\n\n**Pipeline:**\n- Grok review found two MUST-FIX (focus-in-place had no pin — always-navigate kept e2e green; placement ids marked with the wrong id), both fixed red-first\n- All six NICE-TO-HAVEs taken including the gone-node join scenario and the palette's > sending armed context\n- Reviewer endorsed keeping see/after links as links (\"an href is a promise about leaving\")\n- Then #140 landed in packages/chat first: master merged, conflicts resolved preserving both features (384/384 e2e together), two-layer delta-verify DELTA-OK\n- CI 10/10 at b4c72a2 on kolu-ci-1\n- The prototype artifact was unfetchable; interaction built from olai's own idioms instead\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:48-04:00"}
{"id":"app-header","parent":"viewing","ord":"aF","title":"A header bar: the app's chrome above every column","done":"2026-08-11T15:40:03-04:00","desc":"**Design:** the header carries what is about the APP — wordmark, connection, agent toggle, theme; the sidebar carries what is about the DIRECTORY — calendar and the file tree.\n- Collapses the corner-pills special case on the sidebar-less screens: the header is the one home for chrome on every page, error report included (the ErrorBoundary fault card is the noted sole exception)\n- On the phone the burger joins the header's left edge\n- Settled slice of the layout rethink (take 2): https://claude.ai/code/artifact/cfe8c88b-9011-4838-86fb-7ddd412817af\n\n**Shipped 2026-08-11 as PR #101** (squash 875dec7).\n- Mid-flight design ruling from the human: the agent pill is a permanent TOGGLE (aria-pressed while the drawer is open), and the drawer's × went — with permanent chrome, the toggle is the one closer\n- **Review round** (the day's hardest): two measured blockers invisible to CI:\n  - Header clipping its pills at phone widths in three connection states\n  - The grid's `min-h-full` resolving to 0 inside a `min-h-0` flex item, ending the sidebar rule mid-screen\n  - Plus `settle()` weakened on a false premise, popover Escape/focus, ARIA — all fixed, re-measured dead in a real browser\n- Locked with geometry-per-connection-state, short-page height, error-report chrome, and picker-promise scenarios, the connecting one deterministic (holds the socket in CONNECTING or fails)\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:48-04:00"}
{"id":"wf-styling","parent":"viewing","ord":"aG","title":"Workflowy-exact styling: outline, sidebar, everything #ui","done":"2026-08-11T16:50:23-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #102** (squash c2dea45; the done mark carries the merge instant). Final head 8c11745:\n- Review's 5 must-fixes addressed + 8 nice-to-haves\n- 20 required odu checks green on x86_64-linux and aarch64-darwin\n- Six skipped nice-to-haves ratified by the human into wf-gutter-debt\n\n**Dispatched 2026-08-11** -> Kolu terminal `bb7211d5` (Grok 4.5 high, always-approve; worktree .worktrees/workflowy-styling, branch workflowy-styling).\n- #stage review — PR #102 (https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/102) open: impl commit + hickey/lowy refactor pushed\n- Evidence screenshots verified by orchestrator against the Workflowy references (bullets/halo/hover ••• +triangle/checkboxes/tag pills/margins/sidebar match; Open Sans via nixpkgs→woff2 at build, no CDN)\n- **Review DONE** (Claude Opus, split 3c57bd38, 2026-08-11): all builds/tests/fonts reproduced green\n  - Visual metrics measured against Workflowy (row pitch 22.6px vs ~23, indent 33px vs ~32)\n  - 5 must-fixes filed in PR-REVIEW.md: menu Zoom reloads the document instead of router.go; touch.ts gutter table drifted from the DOM (day-view note alignment regression); hover e2e passes with the feature deleted; stale docs; +1 more\n  - 9 nice-to-haves\n- #stage addressing-review: Grok fixing, then master merge + odu CI (Linux+macOS) to green\n- Brief + human's reference screenshots staged at .worktrees/wf-refs/ (BRIEF.md, olai-current-dark.png, workflowy-full.png, workflowy-hover-closeup.png); worker's evidence screenshots land in .worktrees/wf-refs/out/\n\nFiled 2026-08-11 from the human's side-by-side screenshots (olai dark vs Workflowy).\n- **Goal:** make olai's visual language match Workflowy EXACTLY — bullets, checkboxes, spacing, line-height, fonts, tag styling, the outline's left margin/content gutter, and the sidebar tree; hover affordances included\n\n**Decisions (human, 2026-08-11, all resolved):**\n- (1) COLORS ride olai's existing theme system — the WorkFlowy-derived palettes in theme/palettes.ts already mirror Workflowy's themes, so this item changes shapes/metrics/typography, not the token system\n- (2) HOVER: collapse triangle becomes hover-only like Workflowy, AND a new ••• hover menu appears left of the triangle\n  - Orchestrator scope limit: the menu carries only actions the client can already perform (zoom, expand/collapse, copy link) — no write/edit path in this PR, the web client has no write ops yet; structured so future actions slot in\n- (3) BULLETS: exact match — filled round dot, gray circular halo when the node is collapsed (has hidden children), bullet click zooms into the node\n- (4) FONT: Workflowy's ACTUAL font (identify from their shipped CSS), fetched and served through Nix itself — no CDN, no vendored font binary in the repo\n- (5) Tags render as Workflowy does (highlighted pill on the tag text)\n- (6) Sidebar tree matches Workflowy's sidebar styling too\n- Key code: web/src/client/Tree.tsx, Bullet.tsx, Checkbox.tsx, NodeLine.tsx, touch.ts, styles.css @theme, theme/palettes.ts, Sidebar.tsx\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"dates-all-views","parent":"viewing","ord":"aH","title":"Calendar & today derive from ALL dates — dated marks included","done":"2026-08-11T17:47:08-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #103** (squash cbc636e; done carries the merge instant). Final head 58e5e17 after two review rounds and two human rulings folded in:\n- Only `date` + a dated `done` place a node on a day (the any-dated-mark rule retracted as orchestrator extrapolation, pinned negatively)\n- Only `set_done` stamps (local-offset instant, never bare true/day-only; doing/todo store true)\n- Archives keep their days\n- TZ=UTC test gap closed against the reviewer's impostor\n- 20 required odu checks green both platforms\n\n**Dispatched 2026-08-11** -> Kolu terminal `90cd9d21` (Claude Opus, YOLO; worktree .worktrees/dates-from-marks, branch dates-from-marks; brief at .worktrees/dates-from-marks-BRIEF.md).\n- #stage addressing-review — PR #103 (https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/103) open: impl + hickey/lowy + /simplify pushed\n- 525 unit tests, 159 e2e scenarios green locally; evidence in .worktrees/dates-refs-out/\n- Reviewer CLAUDE (human's pick 2026-08-11, overriding the cross-model default) reviewing in a split\n- Author flags for orchestrator: /simplify added './testlib' to @olai/ops exports (mirrors @olai/format)\n- No CI yet, per pipeline\n\nFiled 2026-08-11 by the human, on the heels of the done-datetime migration (49d11d9).\n- format.md says the journal/calendar/today views derive from `date` at view time — but a mark (done/doing/todo) may itself carry an ISO date/datetime, and the roadmap now stores completion instants in `done`, so shipped work vanished from the calendar\n- **Requirement, verbatim intent:** the views must take ALL dates into consideration, including the done date\n  - A node done at an instant appears on that day page and lights that calendar day exactly as a date-scheduled node does\n  - A node carrying both appears on both days\n  - Day pages let the reader tell scheduled-on from completed-on, quietly\n- format.md updated to the new truth\n- **SECOND HALF** (human, 2026-08-11, same agent): the MCP done op auto-stamps the completion datetime\n  - `set_done` stores the current instant with local UTC offset, never bare true, never day-only\n  - Existing true/day-only values in the wild keep loading and rendering (validated as text; the write path must not round-trip other nodes' values)\n  - Whether doing/todo stamp too is the agent's call to justify — the human mandated done\n\n**REVIEW DONE** (Claude, split 3e65a774, 2026-08-11): brief met; reproduced 527 unit / 169 e2e green, zone-portable across 4 TZs, byte-for-byte round-trip via a real olai mcp call.\n- **Two must-fixes:** the branch diff reverts docs/roadmap.jsonl (orchestrator's rebase re-authored master under it — resolve wholesale in master's favor); the never-a-Z stamp promise is unpinned under TZ=UTC\n- Seven nice-to-haves\n- **Human decisions 2026-08-11 on the two escalated:** ONLY done stamps — set_doing/set_todo revert to bare true; ARCHIVED nodes keep their days on calendar/day pages (dim ok), as a decided tested behavior\n- Opus folding in, then master merge + odu CI to green\n\n**RULING** (human, 2026-08-11, on sight of /d/2026-08-11 in the running branch): the any-dated-mark placement rule was the ORCHESTRATOR'S extrapolation in the brief, never ratified — retracted.\n- ONLY the date field and a dated done mark place a node on a day page / light the calendar\n- Dates on doing/todo marks are ignored by the views entirely (no row, no badge) though they remain valid format\n- Occasion reduces to date|done, pinned negatively in tests\n- Correspondingly the stored day-only dates on doing/todo marks in this ledger are scrubbed to bare true (this commit)\n- Opus reworking, then master merge + odu CI\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:48-04:00"}
{"id":"wf-gutter-debt","parent":"viewing","ord":"aI","title":"Workflowy gutter follow-ups #techdebt","done":"2026-08-14T23:44:54-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 at PR #102's merge; the human ratified the reviewer nice-to-haves the author skipped (rationale on the PR conversation).\n- **Decomposed 2026-08-13** (the human approved, for the night slate) into the three child items below\n- Order: Kobalte menu primitive + shared dismiss helper first, then (after edges) the touch affordance and the polish batch — since all three touch NodeMenu\n- This parent is done when the children are\n","see":["wf-styling"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"sidebar-collapsed","parent":"viewing","ord":"aJ","title":"Sidebar tree collapsed by default","done":"2026-08-11T18:01:18-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #105** (squash 163c9b3; done carries the merge instant).\n- The set tracks EXPANDED paths (absent = shut, inverted from the outline tree)\n- Reader toggles client-local and never wiped\n- The open file's chain force-opened without writing into the preference set (pure ancestorDirs helper, unit-tested)\n- e2e pins fresh-collapsed, nested-chain-expanded, and re-collapse when selection leaves\n- 20 odu checks green both platforms; merged under the human's pre-approval, review waived\n\n**Filed & Dispatched 2026-08-11** on the human's ask -> Kolu terminal `5c5481e8` (Grok, always-approve; worktree .worktrees/sidebar-collapsed).\n- Directory nodes in the sidebar file tree start COLLAPSED\n- A reader's stored toggle wins over the default\n- The active file's directory chain auto-expands so the selection is never hidden\n- e2e pins fresh-page-collapsed and nested-selection-expanded\n- **Process, set by the human:** NO review round; squash merge PRE-APPROVED once CI is green (tests + CI are the whole gate)\n","see":["sidebar-tree"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"git-invisible","parent":"bugs","ord":"a6","title":"Git state is invisible in the UI #human","done":"2026-08-11T19:31:05-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #108** (squash 70f21dd; done carries the merge instant). Final head f3d0a53:\n- Review approve zero must-fixes, three nits taken\n- Applied.why + the Ops.git cell + the header readout (quiet/no-repo/error-with-reason)\n- Reconciled past #106\n- 20 odu nodes green both platforms\n\nFiled 2026-08-11 by the human, hit live on his vault instance.\n- **Bug:** writes through the agent reported `committed: false` with NOTHING in the UI saying so, on a directory he knows is a git repo\n- By design (ops/src/git.ts) the auto-commit cannot fail the write and collapses every cause — no work tree, git missing from the service PATH, staging/commit refusal, identity unset — into the same quiet flag, with the reason only in the server log\n- **The human's ruling, verbatim intent:** \"even if git detection fails I'd expect it to surface in UI — even just 'Not a Git repo' or 'Git error'.\" Errors may still be IGNORED (never block or fail the write); they must be VISIBLE\n- **Shape:** the server knows workTree and each write's committed + git's said — surface a git status affordance in the app chrome (header, near the live dot) showing repo/no-repo/git-error, and let a write's committed: false say why where the reader can see it\n\n**Dispatched 2026-08-11** -> Kolu terminal `b0ff13b8` (Claude Opus, YOLO; worktree .worktrees/git-invisible; brief at .worktrees/git-invisible-BRIEF.md).\n- #stage review — PR #108 (https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/108) open: the boolean becomes values\n  - Applied.why (one sentence on any uncommitted write's reply, additive)\n  - An Ops.git cell (off/repo/none/error + git's words, probed once per serve, republished on refusal and recovery), drawn as a header readout beside the connection pill (quiet healthy, calm no-repo, error with tip)\n- Classification honesty: nothing-to-commit is never a fault; broken-git is error unless git itself said not-a-repository (LC_ALL=C)\n- Non-blocking guarantee kept\n- 572 unit + 185 e2e green locally; three-state evidence in .worktrees/git-invisible-out/\n\n**REVIEW DONE** (Grok, split 0c913c2d, 2026-08-11): APPROVE, zero must-fixes.\n- Non-blocking guarantee holds, three UI states reproduced independently, classification honest, purity clean\n- Three nits: dead code field, isolate onGit from write failure, e2e for Applied.why\n- #stage finishing: nits + master merge past #106 + odu CI; then FIELDED to the human — he decides the merge\n- Reviewer: Grok (cross-model)\n- **Also now a HACKING.md rule** (f2bbd28, the human's own edit): errors are never silently ignored — they surface in the UX\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"form-elicitation","parent":"agents","ord":"aC","title":"Form elicitation: the agent's questions render as forms","done":"2026-08-11T20:26:45-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #110** (squash 4a7ad66; merged 2026-08-12T00:26:28Z after the human lifted his hold; this done stamp is the ops instant minutes after).\n- The agent's questions render as answerable forms in the chat (AskUserQuestion works over ACP)\n- A refused answer keeps the typed draft\n- Plan mode reaches the human instead of silent auto-approval\n- Review: approve-with-fixes, all findings addressed; 18/18 required checks green both platforms at 9054de8\n\n- All five scope items delivered, verified against the actually-pinned adapter 0.66.0\n- **Scope-5 tightened:** auto-approval is POSITIVE RECOGNITION of session-handed MCP servers; everything else fails toward asking\n- **Carried forward:** the silent-errors cancel-path collision, on that branch's side\n\n**Filed & Dispatched 2026-08-11** on the human's decision (\"We want that\") -> Kolu terminal `5931d974` (Claude Opus, YOLO; reviewer Grok, split `47b4e8c9`).\n- **Origin:** the adapter presents AskUserQuestion as an ACP form elicitation when the client advertises elicitation.form and disables the tool otherwise — olai advertised nothing\n- agent.ts auto-answered every request_permission with the first allow option, which would have silently approved ExitPlanMode into \"auto\" mode\n- Out of scope: elicitation.url, permission settings UI\n- Pairs with orchestrator-in-chat\n","see":["chat","orchestrator-in-chat"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"silent-errors","parent":"bugs","ord":"a7","title":"Silently ignored errors, inventoried and surfaced #human","done":"2026-08-11T22:34:22-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #112** (squash c5774a7), AUTO-MERGED by the orchestrator 2026-08-12T02:34:04Z under the human's pre-approval (evidence waived by his word; gate: review findings addressed + 18/18 checks at the true head 77c73b6 + roadmap zero-diff).\n- The third autonomous merge of the night\n- The agent held the gate honest itself: it caught that #117's landing staled its earlier green verdict, re-merged, and told the orchestrator NOT to act on the stale green\n\n**The whole swallow inventory surfaced:**\n- Cancels refuse honestly (5-second grace tightened per review)\n- Stream health renders beside the connection pill\n- Store platform failures are DATA with the Banner reading the REASON\n- Kolu failure reasons carried for mcp-fail-visible\n- Unresolvable images name themselves\n- Clipboard denial visible\n- Refused session lists say so\n- Non-text agent chunks render markers\n- `publish?.` is a throw\n- Preferences warn once\n- **Review:** all 12 dimensions passed; findings were hygiene + the cancel-grace question, all addressed\n- /simplify caught two real leaks en route (absolute-path exposure; 60s identical-frame rebroadcast — both regression-tested)\n\n**Filed & Dispatched 2026-08-11** on the human's ask (a paste that did nothing; the audit that followed found the three reverted PRs — see docs/RCA/) -> Kolu terminal `c65479b2` (Claude Opus, YOLO; reviewer Grok, split `b9daf69c`).\n- Part 1 (paste restore) split out and shipped as #111\n","see":["git-invisible","mcp-fail-visible","chat"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"paste-restore","parent":"bugs","ord":"a8","title":"Restore paste-image: revert the mis-titled dd34849","done":"2026-08-11","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #111** (squash 2de0ef5), merged BY THE HUMAN directly at 2026-08-11T19:42:50-04:00 (this done stamp is the ops-layer instant, ~minutes after; review and refactor waived by the human).\n- Grok cherry-picked dc4c078, verified the restored e2e coverage, odu green both platforms\n\n**Filed & Dispatched 2026-08-11** (split from silent-errors at the human's direction: separate quick PR) -> Kolu terminal `b3e45fe0` (Grok, always-approve; worktree .worktrees/paste-restore).\n- Cherry-picks dc4c078 (the completed revert-of-dd34849, authored by the silent-errors Opus)\n- Verifies the RESTORED e2e coverage passes (the tests dd34849 deleted are the regression fence that was missing)\n- odu CI both platforms, PR against master\n- **Process, set by the human:** NO review, NO refactor pass — quick; orchestrator fields the PR at green\n","see":["paste-image","silent-errors"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"mcp-commit-manual","parent":"agents","ord":"aF","title":"The MCP face never got manual commits","done":"2026-08-12T09:34:34-04:00","desc":"**Shipped in PR #116** (squash 324f8b5, merged 2026-08-12T13:33:55Z, human-approved).\n- Discovered mid-work that #83 had been reverted entirely (see the RCA); after #114 restored it, this PR delivered the original scope\n- olai mcp takes the same `--commit=off|manual|auto` tri-state as olai web, manual default, `--no-commit` still meaning off\n- The commit verb joins the MCP tool table (last in TOOLS, after #117's mirror ops) calling the one Ops.commit — message required\n  - Reply reports the swept pending summary\n  - Refuses with reason on a busy repository\n- pending/last/writer-intent readable identically over MCP per the HACKING consistency rule\n- Applied.why under manual mode reads as expected-pending, never as a git error\n- **Byte-identical-faces test:** both faces produce identical commits for the same pending set\n- **CI caught a real startup race:** first pending read accepted the unpublished seed and asserted Off against Ready (darwin-only timing) — fixed by waiting for a published value, README teaches the pattern\n- **Final leg:** merged past #109/#112/#115/#117/#118/#119\n  - Roadmap verified byte-identical to master by blob hash\n  - Noted that origin/master advancing by push mid-merge (shared refs across worktrees) can shortchange a merge — the byte-hash check catches it\n- **NEXT:** reconnect the olai MCP server to activate manual mode — one commit per orchestration beat via the commit verb — and #117's mirror ops\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"restore-84","parent":"bugs","ord":"a9","title":"Restore title-markdown: revert the mis-titled a56cb65","done":"2026-08-11T20:28:17-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #113** (squash ae59f9e), merged BY THE HUMAN directly at 2026-08-12T00:27:53Z (this done stamp is the ops instant just after; review and refactor waived per the quick-restore process).\n- Inline markdown in titles is back on master, reconciled to coexist with #102's tag pills in one title\n- #84's restored tests pass beside #102's\n\n**Filed & Dispatched 2026-08-11** -> Kolu terminal `c7118f67` (Grok, always-approve).\n- **Origin:** the orchestrator's stamp-commit audit found a56cb65 ('roadmap: title-markdown done (#84)', seconds after the #84 merge) to be the exact content-inverse of squash e1ab412 outside docs/roadmap.jsonl\n- The third mass-revert stamp from the same morning session (with dd34849/#87 and 12ea294/#83)\n- Inline title markdown had been absent from master ever since, while the ledger read done\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"sticky-header","parent":"bugs","ord":"aA","title":"Header scrolls away — must be sticky","done":"2026-08-11T21:35:40-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #115** (squash df67730), AUTO-MERGED by the orchestrator 2026-08-12T01:35:17Z under the human's conditional pre-approval.\n- The visual gate passed on inspection (desktop scrolled deep with the header pinned; phone drawer from a scrolled page still meeting the header seam)\n- Review: approve, zero must-fixes (Grok drove both viewports, spot-checked the diagnostic e2e by reverting the fix)\n- 18/18 required checks green at f83a527; one darwin FSEvents flake in an untouched package flagged honestly, rerun, passed\n- 7 diagnostic e2e each proven failing on the pre-change client\n- **Deliberately untouched:** the desktop sidebar still scrolls with the page — filed as sidebar-sticky for the human's ratification\n\n**Filed & Dispatched 2026-08-11** by the human (screen recording; it showed the page at rest, so the author reproduced the scroll-away itself — header at y=-4963 — before fixing) -> Kolu terminal `b2b467d6` (Claude Opus, YOLO).\n- Interacting chrome kept true: #104's drawer/scrim/sheet anchor at `top-[var(--height-header)]`, contents jumps land clear of the bar (scroll-padding)\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"commit-whole-repo","parent":"bugs","ord":"aB","title":"Commit UI is blind to edits outside the ops path — .md edits don't show as pending","done":"2026-08-12T13:26:42-04:00","desc":"**Shipped in PR #122** (squash 518f4af, merged 2026-08-12T17:25:56Z, human-approved and human-merged). Everything the human ratified at dispatch landed:\n\n**PHASE ONE:**\n- git.ts extracted to leaf package @olai/git (one dep: effect)\n- Audit convention as an argument, trailer returned verbatim for ops to classify\n- RepoState/Reason owned by the git package, format re-exporting on a `./state` subpath so the browser never reaches `node:child_process`\n- Every plumbing subtlety preserved\n\n**THE FEATURE:**\n- Pending grew outlines/others/served/unpushed\n- The survey lifted to the repository root (a dirty root README.md shows while serving docs/)\n- Dirty non-outline files are path-level rows with porcelain-derived kind chips, untracked included, .gitignore respected\n- PIECEMEAL commits are a selection of named paths, never the index — hand-staged work untouched, refused-by-name for paths with nothing waiting\n- PUSH arrived on both faces (Ops.push, MCP push tool, panel button, header pill count via one survey), refusals verbatim, Blocked-naming-the-rebase like commit\n- `--commit=auto` unchanged\n\n**Review** (Grok, two passes) caught two real MUST-FIXes:\n- A REFUSED commit leaked the git add into the real index (fixed — index bit-identical after failure, test proven against the reviewer's own gpgsign repro)\n- The stale git README\n- `--no-gpg-sign` deliberately refused (a signature is the owner's statement; gpg's refusal carries verbatim)\n\n**Also fixed from review:**\n- pill/panel fence unified (a reformatted outline with zero node changes counts as waiting)\n- git-status failure surfaces as the Unusable/git-error face\n- docs folded into #123's docs/git.md\n- Side find filed separately: mcp-stdout-pollution\n\n- 914 unit + 261 e2e at review; CI green both platforms\n- **FOLLOW-UP for the orchestrator:** reconnect the olai MCP server to gain the push tool and the paths-arg commit — then the orchestrator's last raw-git verb (git push) retires\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:48-04:00"}
{"id":"one-git-indicator","parent":"bugs","ord":"aC","title":"Two git indicators in the header — there should be one","done":"2026-08-11T22:54:54-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #119** (squash b1ca909), AUTO-MERGED by the orchestrator 2026-08-12T02:54:36Z under the overnight pre-approval — fourth autonomous merge.\n- **Gate record:** the review's DO-NOT-MERGE round did its job (the 390pt shrink order had traded one wrap bug for another — the CONNECTION pill went illegible)\n- The fix round resolved it and the orchestrator's visual gate confirmed on the refreshed 40-image evidence: \"● live\" fully legible at 390pt both themes, the commit pill the graceful truncator (glyph intact), exactly one git indicator in every shot, verified in the pinned bar\n- 22 odu checks green at e045c73 both platforms; roadmap zero-diff; conflicts with #112 resolved keeping both sides\n- The one-indicator claim is now a control-shaped e2e assertion\n\nFiled 2026-08-11 by the human (screenshot: \"● git\" beside \"✓ committed · 3m ago\").\n- **Dispatched** (overnight slate) -> Kolu terminal `7184295a` (Claude Opus, YOLO; reviewer Grok, split `a18ec355`)\n- Bonus: fixed a pre-existing 390pt wordmark-crush bug found while shooting evidence\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"load-perf-p1","parent":"load-perf","ord":"a0","title":"P1: markdown/highlight off the critical path","done":"2026-08-12T08:24:20-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED as PR #118** (squash 59e4192), AUTO-MERGED by the orchestrator 2026-08-12T12:23:45Z under the overnight pre-approval — fifth and final autonomous merge of the slate.\n- **Gate record:** review zero must-fixes with the reviewer running its OWN adversarial network/remount script (outline pages fetch no markdown chunk; markdown-bearing pages fetch once; no remount on a held document)\n- Numbers verified honest and reproducible: document words-on-screen −30.8% (203.7→140.9ms), fully-rendered +0–35ms disclosed as run-variance, main chunk byte-for-byte reproducible at the head\n- 18/18 checks both platforms at f44297e; roadmap zero-diff\n- The upstream ask lives as splitting-upstream (filed by the orchestrator)\n\n**Dispatched 2026-08-11** (overnight slate) -> Kolu terminal `4a78220a` (Claude Opus, YOLO; reviewer Grok, split `43698764`)\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"sidebar-sticky","parent":"bugs","ord":"aD","title":"Desktop sidebar scrolls away with the page — should it pin like the header?","done":"2026-08-12T11:21:36-04:00","desc":"**Shipped in PR #121** (squash 37648ee, merged 2026-08-12T15:20:50Z) — the human's first same-day pre-approved auto-merge.\n- **Full pipeline:** Grok adversarial review: NO must-fix; odu CI 20/20 both platforms at 219d4ae\n- Then the orchestrator's visual gate on the evidence: before — empty column at deep scroll; after — calendar+tree pinned under the header, collapsed rail pinned, column's own scroll independent of the page, phone shots sha256-identical before/after\n- **What shipped:** desktop sidebar (calendar + file tree + icon rail) pins below the #115 header with its own scroll region\n- #105 collapsed-by-default and ⌘\\ survive; mobile drawer untouched; #102 styling not regressed\n- **One non-CSS change:** scroll.ts gained a bounded frame-by-frame clamp-restore retry (1s / takeover / position-holds) because the page-tall column had been quietly propping up document height — regression fence proven failing without it (zoom_and_navigate 1px short)\n- Review corrected a false PR-body claim (3 'pre-existing' bun failures — actually 878/0 green both sides)\n- **Known residuals, recorded as decisions in the PR:** SETTLE_MS=1000 doesn't close the slow-/media/* restore case (predates the pin); the collapse chevron overlays a scrolled tree's foot (#105's control, newly visible)\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"splitting-upstream","parent":"upstream-dist-socket","ord":"a1","title":"Upstream: buildSurfaceClient takes splitting?: boolean #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T19:49:22-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 by the orchestrator on the load-perf-p1 author's flag (an #upstream ask with no tracked home is debt-in-prose). One half of the parent's ONE dist socket.\n\n- **The ask:** buildSurfaceClient accepts `splitting?: boolean` (today hardcoded false in its Bun.build call), so the code-split of markdown/highlight off the critical path (PR #118) stops needing a second hand-rolled Bun.build + shell rewrite (packages/web/src/markdown.ts).\n- **When it lands:** olai deletes most of markdown.ts. Details in PR #118's body."}
{"id":"daily-notes","parent":"viewing","ord":"aL","title":"Daily notes: a date-named document IS the day's note — detected, composed into the day view","done":"2026-08-12T17:48:09-04:00","desc":"**Shipped as PR #127**, squash f3fb7dd (2026-08-12). View-only v1, all four ratified decisions intact:\n\n**(1) Detection by convention:**\n- A document whose basename is exactly an ISO date is THE daily note for that date wherever it lives (the vault's Daily/YYYY/MM/ layout matches automatically; 2026-08-10-recap.md, 2026-8-12.md, 20260812.md do not)\n- Two claimants list in path order, no conflict rule invented\n- ONE derivation beside datedDays in format/src/dates.ts (a grep found no second basename date-parse, and loosening the regex turns two tests red)\n\n**(2) Composition:**\n- /d/\\<date\\> and /today render the note FIRST through the existing sanitising pipeline (XSS probe verified)\n- Dated DayGroups below unchanged; empty days stay inert\n\n**(3) Calendar:**\n- Four cell states (nothing/nodes/note/both)\n- The note fold shape-distinct from the node dot in both themes\n- Note-days clickable, aria-labels carry the two facts (reviewer NICE-TO-HAVE taken)\n\n**(4) Relative links:**\n- .md→.md routes to /doc in-app resolved against the note's own directory even on the day page\n- ../ climbs verified\n- A missing target gets the honest nothing\n- Fragments degrade to plain navigation (the non-taking's stated reason verified true)\n\n- The journal-is-a-query doctrine amended in architecture.md: the note JOINS the query's answer, never replaces it\n- **Reviewer:** no MUST-FIX; all four NICE-TO-HAVEs taken (a11y labels, stale Calendar.tsx header line, two-claimants e2e, the two brief-named non-ISO refusals)\n- **CI saga:** the Linux e2e failures were CI POOL HEALTH — kolu-ci-3/4 run ~30% slower and flake timing-sensitive scenarios on master too (author proved it with branch-vs-master runs on the boxes themselves)\n  - Green on a healthy runner, 20/20 both platforms, plus one final run after a post-report master merge reset the checks (that waste is what the CLAUDE.md master-merge-only-on-conflicts rule now retires)\n- Human approved 2026-08-12\n- **FLAGGED, awaiting the human:** the ci-pool health itself (slow boxes fail unrelated PRs)\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:48-04:00"}
{"id":"md-editing","parent":"editor","ord":"a6","title":"Documents become writable: create and edit .md from olai","done":"2026-08-13T19:26:25-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-12 on the human's word. **Shipped as PR #148 (squash 10fd1fbf), 2026-08-13.**\n- Documents are writable end to end through the one ops path on both faces: `write_document`/`create_document` on MCP and the web editor drive the same planner → store.commit → audit trail (X-Olai-Writer)\n- The was-guard refuses an external edit (vim mid-session) in words with an explicit \"Overwrite what is there\" (which clobbers the CURRENT disk, verified)\n- A bare calendar day mints that day's note per the vault's own convention (path inferred from the newest daily note)\n- Dirty .md files ride the existing commit flow\n- **The review's MUST-FIX:** document→document navigation reused the Solid page instance (mint hand-off broken, cross-file draft possible)\n  - Fixed by construction (keyed identity) with three scenarios, measured against pre-fix code (the cross-file draft was the deterministic red; the creation doors had been green by frame-ordering luck)\n- Seven+ sabotage-verified pins; CI green at merge head e14e0800 on kolu-ci-1; 1249 unit, 396 e2e\n- **Recorded, not fixed (pre-existing):** fs.watch only sees a brand-new subdirectory on the next probe — the store's 60s backstop covers it\n- Follow-up filed: md-rich-editing\n","see":["daily-notes","commit-whole-repo"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"precompress-dev-tax","parent":"bugs","ord":"aE","title":"Precompression taxes every dev-server start ~20s — recompresses a never-pruned dist","done":"2026-08-12T21:28:58-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-12 from the human hitting it live (\"this compress stuff is slowing down the dev server like 20 seconds\").\n- **CLOSED 2026-08-13** by PR #129's pin bump — the taxed file no longer exists, and the filed symptom is unreachable\n- Measured on the merged path (buildSurfaceClient → pruneAssets → precompressAssets): cold 3.87s · no-op rebuild 0.96s · changed-entry rebuild 2.18s\n- dist/assets stable at 19 files over four consecutive builds\n\n- **Leg (a) prune — paid upstream** (kolu#2159 names this downstream case in its own body): the hashed dir is reduced to what this build produced before anything is compressed.\n- **Leg (b) skip — paid upstream**: an identically-hashed sibling is left alone; the skip keys on emitted bytes, not source mtime (a minified-away comment does not re-pay).\n- **Leg (c) dev-skip flag — overtaken by ruling**: kolu#2159 refused the precompress knob BY NAME (\"the switch would only ever select between 'the layer works' and 'the layer has nothing to serve'\"). Not implementable in olai; re-opening it is a NEW upstream ask against that ruling, not this node.\n- **Residual, intended**: a build whose emitted bytes changed pays ~1.2s compressing the changed files (slightly up per-file — .zst is a third encoding now — while the total collapsed). Bounded, not growing.\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"editor-op-parity","parent":"bugs","ord":"aF","title":"Web editor expresses less than MCP — a standing HACKING consistency violation","done":"2026-08-14T12:33:42-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-12 from the human's Editor-subtree review.\n- HACKING.md says \"MCP and Web ops must be consistent; never deviate\" — they deviated, so this was a BUG\n\n**PIPELINE COMPLETE 2026-08-14**, PR #166 AWAITS THE HUMAN'S APPROVAL (lane `b9cc35e3` alive; reviewer splits idle).\n- see-edges and after-edges writable from the web (widget-family creation via the `((` machinery, × removal, acyclicity refusals verbatim and sabotage-pinned)\n- The sidebar mints outlines (op's validation verbatim) — all through the intent seam, three arms on the union, three in the resolver, no side channels\n- **Panel review** (grok 0+2, opencode 0+2, independently CONVERGENT on the same two nits; both confirm the deviation closed): union addressed at 9cbb779\n  - The one-verb prose is three verbs in four places\n  - Feature pins added for both new exclusions\n  - SeeRefs.tsx reference corrected\n  - Edge-undo e2e'd for after and × removal (the append-order residual asserted as documented behavior)\n  - The edge-search step keys its wait on the query\n- Five sabotages on the evidence page, each red on its claimed pin\n- CI 9/9 required at 9cbb779, MERGEABLE/CLEAN; 539 e2e scenarios, 1519 unit tests\n- Evidence: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/2581c0b9-099a-4b44-bb6a-060669ec9d70\n\n- **Children closed by this PR at merge:** parity-see, parity-after, parity-create-outline (stamps land with the merge)\n- **Deferred, named on the PR:** the append-order residual itself (a set_see change, not an undo change), per-row createEdgeEditing signals, edgesOf's algorithmic coupling to the planner\n","see":["undo","input-widgets","silent-errors"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"parity-archive","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a0","title":"archive: MCP archive_node vs no web affordance at all","done":"2026-08-18T02:55:00-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED for the mouse in PR #124** (`menu-verbs`, squash 60631fe, 2026-08-12); this stamp is the bookkeeping that never landed.\n- The human's ruling that day was SUBTREE WITH A CONFIRM, and that is what the `•••` menu's `Move to Trash` sends\n- One `archive` edit through the same gate `archive_node` goes through, behind a question naming how many rows go\n- Counted over the SET rather than over the rows on screen (done-hiding drops finished branches from a reading, and a count that read the page would understate what the write moves)\n- **NO KEY, deliberately:** there is still no delete key in this app, and the roadmap's own \"key only if the human wants one\" was never answered yes\n- Three doors reach the op now, all asking the same catalog (`web/src/client/menu/verbs.ts`): the row's `•••`, the multi-selection bar, and the ⌘K palette on a zoomed node — the one node no pointer could put away, since a heading has no `•••`\n- A MIRROR ROW IS NOT OFFERED IT (see `parity-remove-mirror`)\n- What the write did is on the Trash: `parity-unarchive` gave the archive its way out, and #226 took what is put away off every other page\n- Pinned by `menu_verbs.feature` (offers, asks, the count, cancel, confirm) and `trash.feature`; the verbs and the confirm are unit-tested beside them\n- **Stamped 2026-08-18** by the `web-archive-unmirror` lane, dispatched on this node's own stale desc — it still read \"the web has NO archive verb, key, or menu entry\", false since 2026-08-12\n  - Committed the evidence sections `move-to-trash-from-the-menu` and `retire-a-placement` (`packages/tests/evidence.ts`) so the pair is photographed rather than only asserted\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"parity-date","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a1","title":"date: MCP set_date (set AND clear) vs no web date editing","done":"2026-08-13T00:38:39-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #133 (95c3a8b), squash-merged 2026-08-13. The web sets and changes a date on the row — the picker, reachable from the date badge and the ••• menu (Set date… / Change date…), sending the same `date` edit #124's Clear already put on the wire.\n\n- **Dates stay text**: `input type=\"date\"` chosen because it cannot mint an instant — the ten picked characters are the ten written; the only reading is @olai/format's dayOf. Sabotage via toISOString went red.\n- **One spelling of clear**: the picker absorbs #124's verb — emptying the box flips the button to Clear date and both doors emit ONE constructor's edit, with a two-door divergence test (review MUST-FIX; sabotage-verified so the split cannot silently return).\n- **The agenda is the consumer, proven**: a past date on a todo moves it into Overdue live, no reload — pinned in e2e (isOverdue sabotage turned 9 cases red).\n- **Evidence caught two bugs pre-review** (empty said-box under the menu; Clear date offered undated) — both fixed and pinned; the author also caught its OWN first e2e pin passing under sabotage (absence-wait always succeeds) and rewrote it read-once.\n- **Recorded, not lost**: touch door for undated rows (the ••• menu is pointer-only below md — the checkbox's same gap) and three /simplify skips, in the PR body.\n- **CI**: 10/10 Linux at c186fca; the sick-pool file is now three-for-three (mid-suite kill ~4½min, truncated log, committing.feature untouched by the PR — kolu-ci-2 and ci-3 implicated, ci-1 green throughout; table in the PR comment).\n- **Evidence** (verified by the orchestrator): picker from badge, picker from menu, the before/after Overdue move, the absorbed clear — archived to the session scratchpad."}
{"id":"parity-marks","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a2","title":"todo/doing marks: MCP set_todo + set_doing vs web toggles done only","done":"2026-08-12T22:52:22-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #132 (f5d130d), squash-merged 2026-08-13. The web writes all three marks without inventing a second writer: ⌘⇧Enter is an INTENT (`walk`) — the server reads the stored mark and emits exactly the ops request an agent would send.\n\n- **The ring**: unmarked → todo → doing → unmarked; unmarked is a stop (the field leaves the record), `done` is deliberately OFF the ring (walking through it would stamp an instant, fire the nudge, and hide the row en route to somewhere else — Ctrl+Enter stays done's own verb).\n- **The refusal is met, not absorbed**: on a finished row the walk asks todo outright and ops' verbatim sentence renders under the row, naming the way through (undo first — two ops, the second the person's).\n- **Bug found and fixed on the way**: `inverseOf` applied two-edit undo whenever a mark displaced another; the rule is only for writes that leave a node done — undo of the menu's Clear-mark was already broken by this. Regression pinned.\n- **Review**: NO MUST-FIX, six hunts held, three sabotages red on their claimed pins. NTHs: mirror-disk tautology assertion dropped + ring-inverse coverage widened; the data-tone markup-for-a-test declined (the sentence is the contract via its testid). Menu verbs and Archive pre-exist from #124 — this PR is keyboard + refusal + inverse only.\n- **CI**: 10/10 Linux at the resolved head; the sick-host file grew hard data (base commit fails identically on kolu-ci-3/4 with none of this PR's changes; green on a free pool).\n- **Evidence** (verified by the orchestrator): all four faces in one glance, the walk stepwise, the refusal verbatim, the two-step through it, menu verbs, keys written down in docs/editing.md — archived to the session scratchpad."}
{"id":"parity-see","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a3","title":"see edges: MCP set_see add/remove vs web renders but cannot write","done":"2026-08-14T12:33:37-04:00","desc":"MCP adds and removes see references; the web RENDERS them (edges-ui, done) but has no affordance to create or remove one. Creation wants a node search (the same widget family as input-widgets' `((` mirror search); removal wants an x on the rendered reference or a ••• verb."}
{"id":"parity-after","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a4","title":"after edges: MCP set_after vs web shows blocked state but cannot change it","done":"2026-08-14T12:33:38-04:00","desc":"MCP adds and removes after dependencies (#117 completed the set); the web draws blockedness (edges-ui) but a person cannot declare or lift a dependency. Same widget family as parity-see; acyclicity refusals must surface verbatim per HACKING."}
{"id":"parity-remove-mirror","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a5","title":"mirror removal: MCP remove_mirror vs no web way to retire a placement","done":"2026-08-18T02:55:00-04:00","desc":"**SHIPPED for the mouse in PR #124** (`menu-verbs`, squash 60631fe, 2026-08-12); this stamp is the bookkeeping that never landed.\n- The `•••` menu on a MIRROR row offers `Remove this placement` and does not offer `Move to Trash` — the split this verb exists for\n- What the reader is looking at is a line standing for a node that lives somewhere else, and archiving from there would file a subtree out of sight on a click that reads as being about this line\n- The question is asked of the row's OWN RECORD rather than of what it managed to draw (`web/src/client/menu/verbs.ts`), so the two degenerate placements — a chain that died, one that closed a loop — are covered by construction rather than by a fence\n- **THE OP'S FENCE REACHES THE CLICK VERBATIM:** a placement something else still names is refused naming what to re-point first, exactly as `remove_mirror` refuses it\n- Pinned by `menu_verbs.feature` (\"Retiring a placement takes the line and leaves the node\", \"A placement something else still names is refused, naming what\")\n- The creation half is `input-widgets`' `((`, whose ⌘Z is an `unmirror`\n- The retire itself is the one write on this surface with no inverse, said by recording nothing rather than by a ⌘Z that would mint a different id in a slot it cannot name (`server/src/edit.ts`)\n- **Stamped 2026-08-18** by the `web-archive-unmirror` lane, dispatched on this node's own stale desc — \"the web has no affordance on a mirror row\", false since 2026-08-12\n  - Also documented the verb in docs/editing.md (it was the one menu WRITE that doc never named)\n  - Committed the `retire-a-placement` evidence section\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"parity-create-outline","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a6","title":"create outline: MCP create_outline vs no web new-file affordance","done":"2026-08-14T12:33:38-04:00","desc":"MCP mints a new .jsonl outline (optionally seeded with a tree); the web sidebar lists files but cannot create one. A \"new outline\" affordance in the sidebar; naming/path validation is the op's, surfaced verbatim."}
{"id":"parity-unarchive","parent":"editor-op-parity","ord":"a7","title":"unarchive: missing on BOTH faces — the trash cannot be taken out of","done":"2026-08-13T19:05:02-04:00","desc":"The equal absence the 2026-08-12 review exposed: UNARCHIVE existed on NO face. **Shipped as PR #147 (squash 7457d9ab), 2026-08-13**, under the human's shape ruling.\n- The archive got a real web view named **Trash** (file and MCP vocabulary unchanged): sidebar entry, read-only rows, \"Put back\" per row\n- The ops verb born once, exposed on both faces\n- ⌘⇧Z genuinely brings a row back out (pinned, including a retitled-parent scenario added when the review's own suggestion stayed green under sabotage)\n- **The review's MUST-FIX** (Put back on a minted ancestor husk minted live duplicates — proven by planner runs) fixed red-first at the ops layer: the notASignpost fence (bare + a live twin at the landing) refuses on both faces identically\n- Put back deliberately NOT hidden client-side, to avoid recreating the faces split\n- Archive/remove-mirror menu verbs were #124's (verified, not rebuilt; archive relabeled \"Move to Trash\")\n- **Escalated to the human, still open:** does the set freeze archived work, or stay editable on both faces (today: editable, symmetric — recorded in editing-web.md's Open)\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"menu-verbs","parent":"editor","ord":"a7","title":"The ••• menu learns to write: marks, clear-date, remove-placement, archive, copy-as-text","done":"2026-08-12T14:24:01-04:00","desc":"**Shipped as PR #124**, squash 60631fe (2026-08-12). The mouse's first write path: the ••• menu gained five verbs.\n- Contextual mark section (todo/doing/complete/clear, current mark hidden, ops refusals verbatim in the said line)\n- Clear-date (dated rows only)\n- Remove-placement (mirror rows only, op's own fence)\n- Archive (subtree, inline confirm naming DERIVED descendant count — the author's own /simplify pass caught the count reading rendered rows under done-hidden — honest restore sentence since unarchive does not exist)\n- Copy-as-text (tab-indented plain text, target's subtree on a mirror)\n- **Closed four editor-op-parity children for the mouse:** parity-archive, parity-date (removal half), parity-marks (menu half), parity-remove-mirror\n- The menu moved to web/src/client/menu/ (NodeMenu + verbs/actions/writes/subtree, unit-tested)\n- **Reconciled with #120 at merge:**\n  - Mark collapsed to ONE arm and one resolver spoken by both callers\n  - Archive vs remove stay two verbs with different fences\n  - inverseOf extended so a cleared date is restored as the date it cleared\n  - Menu writes record onto the same ⌘Z stack\n- Survived a 10-point adversarial review and two master syncs (#120's 40-file, #122's 49-file)\n- **CI saga:** two red x86_64-linux e2e legs turned out to be the author's own harness error (odu client wrapped in timeout 600, killing the lane mid-suite)\n  - Proven by a controlled experiment on the CI host itself: master control 7/7 clean, branch equally clean once the timeout wrapper was removed\n  - Final gate 21/21 contexts green both platforms\n- Human approved 2026-08-12\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"website","ord":"zzV","title":"Website: GitHub Pages at olai.kolu.dev","done":"2026-08-12T12:16:16-04:00","desc":"**Shipped in PR #123** (squash a8a0105, merged 2026-08-12T16:14:32Z) — authored and merged by the human directly, recorded here by the orchestrator after the fact.\n- A static landing page in the app's chalk palette (website/index.html, no build step)\n- CNAME olai.kolu.dev\n- Pages workflow deploying website/ on master pushes touching it\n\n**THE DOCS CONVENTION IT ESTABLISHES** (binding on all future PRs; relayed to the three in-flight agents at merge):\n- README.md is a POINTER (site + docs/index.md + HACKING.md) — future user-facing copy changes go to website/index.html\n- docs/ split into index.md, running.md, git.md, chat.md beside architecture.md and format.md\n- docs/git.md owns the git-integration story\n\n**One-time settings the human owns:**\n- Repo Pages source = GitHub Actions with the custom domain\n- Cloudflare CNAME olai → juspay.github.io\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-drop-files","parent":"agents","ord":"aG","title":"Drag and drop files into the chat","done":"2026-08-12T17:42:12-04:00","desc":"**Shipped as PR #126**, squash 4851ad5 (2026-08-12). Drop lands on the existing attachment machinery — nothing new below the gesture.\n- The panel body (header excluded) is the drop target with a visible affordance\n- enter/leave COUNTED (not flagged — crossing transcript rows is one drag; sabotaging the counter to a boolean fails the e2e)\n- dragend clears a cancelled drag's overlay (both endings asserted)\n- Text drags left alone\n- Multi-file drops attach in order all the way to the order the agent reads them\n- **Refusals survive each other:** the batch sorts through the ONE shared gate, Chat.attach answers (stored/refused/gone) instead of drawing, and holding.take says every refusal once on the panel's one line\n  - Closes a real silent-loss path (file 3 used to rub out file 2's reason; the reviewer proved nothing went red without its test, so the fix is pinned by a take unit test with type+size reasons)\n- **MID-FLIGHT HUMAN RULING** (the human hit it driving the build): the gate widened beyond pictures\n  - attachmentRejection now takes DOCUMENT_EXTENSIONS (.pdf .txt .md .csv .json) with honest name+size chips\n  - The picker's accept= matches the gate\n  - .svg keeps its scriptable-document refusal\n  - The 50 MB cap stays\n  - Loosening the gate to accept .svg turns four tests red\n- **Two reviewer rounds:** initial — one MUST-FIX + the dragend bug upgraded by the orchestrator; re-verify 1 and 2 both \"the PR stands clean\", every fix sabotage-verified\n- CI green both platforms at each head\n- Human approved 2026-08-12\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:48-04:00"}
{"id":"adapter-interpret","parent":"agents","ord":"aH","title":"Adapter interpretation out of agent.ts: one testable module #techdebt","done":"2026-08-12T15:25:48-04:00","desc":"**Shipped as PR #125**, squash e7fc004 (2026-08-12) — same day the kitchen-sinks debate ratified it (debates/kitchen-sinks/conclusion.md item 4; filed and dispatched on the human's word).\n- packages/chat/src/interpret.ts now owns the adapter's interpretation as pure functions:\n  - `allowedWithoutAsking` (the debate's shouldBypass, renamed because it answers with WHICH option, never a boolean — positive recognition of `mcp__<server>__` against the given names, never the first allow-flavoured option, so plan mode's \"Ready to code?\" cannot silently flip the session to auto)\n  - `toolNameIn` (`_meta.claudeCode.toolName`)\n  - `liveModelIn`/`modelPickerIn`/`labelsOf` (the forwarded CLI init on `_claude/sdkMessage` + the free-form \"model\" config select)\n  - Plus `NEW_SESSION_META`/`SDK_MESSAGE`/`BYPASS_MODE`\n  - Two strays (`id===\"model\"`, `bypassPermissions`) the author proved are adapter vocabulary, not protocol (SessionConfigId and SessionModeId are free-form strings; bypassPermissions appears nowhere in the SDK)\n- 22 unit tests, no subprocess — the safety rule is unit-testable for the first time\n- `onPermission` is four lines\n- agent.ts 1119→1033 with all closure state (session lifecycle, toolNames map, model debounce) unmoved\n- interpret.ts deliberately NOT on the package's export socket\n- **The reviewer passed it with zero MUST-FIX** after two sabotage probes (dropping the ours gate and weakening the prefix match both went red) and arm-by-arm equivalence against the old inline logic\n- Zero behavior change; e2e green throughout\n- Human pre-approved on the green gate\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:48-04:00"}
{"id":"upstream-dist-socket","parent":"infra","ord":"aA","title":"Upstream: buildSurfaceClient completed as ONE dist socket #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T19:49:24-04:00","desc":"Ratified from the lowy-electricity debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-12.md entry 1; all three stances signed). Shipped as kolu PR #2159, squash-merged 2026-08-12, with drishti pair PR #138 green.\n\n- **The receptacle:** \"what a surface-app dist is.\" Both children landed TOGETHER as one socket — precompressed siblings (.br/.gz/.zst) and `splitting` opened, shell never compressed, sibling-skip/prune in.\n- **The proof on the far side:** drishti's repin alone turned its identity-only dist into one carrying every sibling (main-*.js 640,266 B → 173,165 B brotli) — no drishti source change, exactly the socket thesis.\n- **Review:** independent reviewer; one MUST-FIX (the named .zst test was vacuous — deleting the zstd table row left the suite green), fixed and sabotage-verified; review also flushed a real gap (the extra-asset fixture sat under the 1024 B threshold, so sibling growth was never exercised). ts-pattern dep refusal accepted (Record keyed by the union; keeps the pair PR a pure repin). A late ci::e2e-governance red was an allowlist row for httpDrive.testlib.ts (Effect run-edge scan), delta-verified governance-only.\n- **Follow-up flagged, not taken:** kolu's own vite.config.ts emits .br/.gz but no .zst while its server prefers zstd — tracked in the PR body.\n- **Olai's side is NOT this item:** on the kolu pin bump, olai deletes precompress.ts and markdown.ts — the deletion is the installation. Stays in olai forever: Solid transform, Tailwind, fonts, icons."}
{"id":"upstream-readout","parent":"infra","ord":"aB","title":"Upstream: the connectSurface readout that cannot lie #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T19:50:37-04:00","desc":"Ratified from the lowy-electricity debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-12.md entry 2). Shipped as kolu PR #2160, squash-merged 2026-08-12, with drishti pair PR #139 green (Linux-only per the macOS rule; drishti has no branch protection at all).\n\n- **The defect paid for:** `connectSurface(...).status` could say `live` while a subscription over the socket had errored — olai shipped the bug this permits (a dead documents.keys rendering as an empty directory under a green light).\n- **The payment:** the conjunction folded into the readout (degraded state naming the stopped subscriptions); `pending does not degrade` as the universal default; `needsReload` travels. Event-folded, not walk-per-read.\n- **The cut held:** kolu owns the five states' TRUTH; the app keeps its LOOK. Notable deviation, reviewer-adjudicated sound: kolu's own client deliberately ignores conn.health (per-member onError policy, documented in wire.ts), so the in-repo proof is the surface-app example rail + seam tests, not a HostStatusPip migration.\n- **Review:** no code MUST-FIX; the vacuous dispose test was required fixed anyway (one standard across the batch) and sabotage-verified; two lying doc lines corrected; sibling-prefix readout assertion added. The rail-needsReload suggestion was declined as unreachable dead-path UI (its wire passes retired: reloadForUpdate).\n- **Olai's migration rides the later pin bump, not this item:** connection/status.ts shrinks to chrome (\"the files on disk reach this page\" stays this house's sentence)."}
{"id":"upstream-chunking","parent":"infra","ord":"aC","title":"Upstream: frame-limit chunking beside RPC_MAX_FRAME_BYTES #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T19:25:21-04:00","desc":"Ratified from the lowy-electricity debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-12.md entry 3). Shipped as kolu PR #2158, squash-merged 2026-08-12.\n\n- **Why:** an oversized frame is not a failed call — the ndjson decoder closes the socket (1009) and takes every subscription on that tab with it. Every surface-app that uploads must chunk, and the arithmetic has been derived twice in kolu's orbit: padi's upload.ts, then olai's surface/src/attach.ts, which copied it \"because re-deriving it is how the same incident happens twice.\"\n- **The payment:** `chunkBase64` + the envelope/budget helpers landed beside RPC_MAX_FRAME_BYTES (the cap's own home). The arithmetic: base64 4/3, JSON envelope, no third expansion, chunk size a multiple of 3 so every 4-character group decodes alone. padi's upload.ts migrated in the same PR — the first copy is gone.\n- **The seam held (grok's cut, all three signed):** content policy stayed in olai — attachmentRejection, the allowlists, MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES, the tmp-directory rule.\n- **Review:** independent reviewer, one MUST-FIX — `frameBytesFor` was never exercised, so sabotage there left all 56 properties green; fixed and sabotage-verified both ways. The review also caught the old 26 MB fixture's expected value was not legal base64 (misplaced ceil). Drishti pair adjudicated unnecessary: purely additive export. CI: 48/48 required contexts green, both platforms.\n- **Still owed here:** olai's attach.ts shrinks onto the shared helpers on the next kolu pin bump — a separate beat."}
{"id":"chat-edit-diffs","parent":"agents","ord":"aI","title":"Chat shows the agent's file-edit diffs, trimmed, expand on click","done":"2026-08-12T22:05:05-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #130 (c7f8fdb), squash-merged 2026-08-13. Two previews, two vocabularies, one fold idiom — as ratified.\n\n- **Direct file edits**: ACP's diff block travels STRUCTURED (FileDiff: path + oldText/newText); the panel renders Claude-Code-style — trimmed to 6 rows, unchanged runs collapsed into gaps first, expanded in place on click. The line diff is a hand-rolled prefix/suffix-strip + suffix-table LCS (~100-line walk; the diff micro-deps bring character algorithms and patch application for one function — same trade as @olai/git over simple-git). Bounded: over budget says \"rewritten whole\" rather than a wrong diff.\n- **Olai MCP writes**: never a text diff — the node-level story (marked done / note rewritten / moved) via Applied.sort on the ops reply, derived by the same changesOf that classifies commit-panel rows; SAID/GLYPH moved to changes.ts, ONE table for both panels. The never-rule is true of the FILE, not just the ops path: a direct Edit on a .jsonl routes to the story row (fileKind → OutlineDiff).\n- **Review**: 1 MUST-FIX (no reconstruction property — a diagonal-index sabotage left all ten tests green; the reviewer property-checked the implementation itself over 22 cases first) + 6 NICE-TO-HAVEs, ALL taken including two upgraded (the .jsonl file-rule; docs/chat.md's now-false \"no filesystem\" paragraph). DELTA-OK. /simplify caught a literal NUL byte that made folds.ts git-binary.\n- **Conflict round**: #129 moved master; resolved keeping both docs truths (+2/−2), full suite on the merged head, CI 10/10 at 6d8fafd.\n- **Evidence** (verified by the orchestrator): trimmed card, in-place expansion, set_done story row with the outline agreeing beside it, and the .jsonl fallback — archived to the session scratchpad."}
{"id":"preferences-panel","parent":"viewing","ord":"aM","title":"Preferences panel: themes, done-visible, and friends in one place","done":"2026-08-12T22:49:23-04:00","desc":"**Shipped as PR #131** (999dcec), squash-merged 2026-08-13.\n- One place for the client's preferences, kolu's SettingsPopover shape over olai's deliberately client-local preference.ts\n- localStorage, storage-event carry across tabs, never sent to the server (the doctrine is in the panel's own footer copy)\n\n- **Contents v1**:\n  - Theme (the fifteen palettes as self-colored chips — the old standalone picker deleted, Picker.tsx gone)\n  - Done-visible (the DEFAULT; any page's own toggle still wins — precedence pinned in e2e)\n  - Home: the app header, fourth control\n- **Review**:\n  - 1 MUST-FIX — a real keyboard regression: the portal left focus on the trigger, Tab never entered the panel; fixed with focus-move + e2e, sabotage-verified (deleting the queueMicrotask focus leaves the caret on the trigger and the assertion fails)\n  - 3 NICE-TO-HAVEs taken (Done second-tab scenario — sabotage-checked as the real hole; chip focus ring on the accent; two stale comments)\n  - Two skipped on doctrine, reviewer-accepted: muted-hint AA is the app's existing muted contract, and contrast.test.ts widening to fifteen palettes would be a NEW promise (architecture.md pins AA on one) — both palette-wide calls, not panel fixes\n  - DELTA-OK\n- **Conflict round**: #130 moved master; one import-block conflict resolved keeping both truths; 345/345 e2e, CI 10/10.\n- **Follow-up filed**: preference-receptacle (six spellings of read→signal→write→watch want one createPreference).\n- **Evidence** (verified by the orchestrator): panel in header, theme flip chalk→pitch, Done row both hints, phone at 390pt, keyboard Tab-into-first-chip with accent ring — archived to the session scratchpad.\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"agenda","parent":"viewing","ord":"aN","title":"Agenda: due dates as a reading — one overdue predicate, one /agenda page","done":"2026-08-12T20:11:56-04:00","desc":"Due dates got their UX: a derived `overdue` predicate and an `/agenda` page — the forward half of the journal the day pages serve backward. Shipped as PR #128 (ffc1cdf), squash-merged 2026-08-13.\n\n- **The fix as ratified**: no new field — `date` + mark is the reading (`date` alone = occurrence, never late; `date` + `todo`/`doing` = due work). `overdue(n) ⇔ (todo ∨ doing) ∧ day(date) < today`, spelled once in packages/format/src/agenda.ts, string-compared on the first ten characters. `/agenda`: Overdue (oldest first) / Today (minus done) / Upcoming (only days that have anything, headings link to day pages), grouped by outline. DateBadge takes the attention tone wherever the predicate holds.\n- **Rulings honoured** (human, 2026-08-12): `doing` IS overdue-capable; occurrences never in Overdue and never amber; `done` nowhere on the page; undated tasks absent; empty state writes nothing; no snooze/recurrence. One reviewer-noted extension consistent with \"one predicate\": an archived `todo` with a past date is overdue — the archive exemption belongs to blockedness, not to lateness.\n- **Review**: no MUST-FIX across five hunts; both predicate sabotages red; all six NICE-TO-HAVEs taken (isOverdue now slices `today` — the datetime-today hazard — plus five doc/prose truths), DELTA-OK. CI: Linux green; macOS skipped under the standing rule (platform-neutral PR) — which surfaced that olai's ruleset hard-required nine darwin contexts; they are no longer required (ruleset 20608873 edited 2026-08-13).\n- **Design**: docs/brainstorming/agenda.md."}
{"id":"kolu-pin-sockets","parent":"infra","ord":"aD","title":"Install the three sockets: kolu pin bump — the deletion is the installation #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T21:28:58-04:00","desc":"The olai-side halves of the three lowy-electricity payments, all on ONE pin bump. Shipped as PR #129 (d5b302c), squash-merged 2026-08-13. 30 files, net −563.\n\n- **Dist socket in:** precompress.ts and markdown.ts DELETED; build.ts composes buildSurfaceClient's own precompress + splitting; .zst finally emitted (br 189kB / zstd 199kB / gzip 225kB for the 700kB entry); the markdown chunk is one literal import() and first paint still never fetches it.\n- **Readout in:** status.ts shrank to the LOOK; the client.health() walk, unhealthy, readoutOf, needsReload all left; olai reads conn.readout itself (kolu's client deliberately doesn't auto-adopt).\n- **Chunking in:** attach.ts's derived-constants header replaced by kolu's frame-chunking helpers, imported at call sites; the content gate stayed whole.\n- **Review:** one MUST-FIX (the orchestrator's — a roadmap node naming the deleted file; resolved in this beat) + three NICE-TO-HAVEs taken, DELTA-OK; both sabotage hunts red. Beyond-brief: encoding.test.ts now drives every row of kolu's PRECOMPRESSED_ENCODINGS, .zst-arm sabotage-checked.\n- **Flags filed as nodes:** modulepreload-upstream (the 1.5kB unpreloaded shared chunk). The pipeline-<hash>.js naming right (was markdown-[hash].js) is pinned loudly by e2e.\n- **CI:** nine Linux contexts green at final head, GitHub CLEAN; macOS skipped per standing rule."}
{"id":"depth-pass","parent":"viewing","ord":"aO","title":"Depth pass: three altitudes — elevation replaces borders across the app","done":"2026-08-13T11:22:17-04:00","desc":"Ratified 2026-08-12 from the design artifact (https://claude.ai/code/artifact/c22b5168-ecf5-43f3-876e-d32e54c4f344).\n- **The flatness diagnosis:** everything at altitude zero\n- **The five moves:** three altitudes; elevation replaces borders; accent spent not sprinkled; interactive lifts; the paper is the hero\n\n**Shipped 2026-08-13 by the human's own hand: PR #136** (branch surfaces, squash befa8dd) — \"The chrome sits on a desk: three surfaces, and a type of our own\" — authored and merged by the human directly, superseding both orchestrated attempts.\n- Attempt 1: PR #134 (branch depth), closed — right tokens, failed the human's visual review on real data (nine findings)\n- Attempt 2: PR #135 (branch depth2, Grok), closed — addressed all nine, orchestrator-verified, rejected in favor of the human's own take\n- Both branches remain on origin as prior art\n- Follow-up still filed: quiet-pill-unify\n- The website depth touch-up idea was DISCARDED by the human 2026-08-13 — no website restyle follows #136\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:48-04:00"}
{"id":"modulepreload-upstream","parent":"infra","ord":"aE","title":"Upstream: buildSurfaceClient emits modulepreload for the entry's static chunks #upstream","done":"2026-08-13T11:25:26-04:00","desc":"**Shipped as kolu PR #2163** (squash e7f0391, admin-merged past the darwin gate on the human's approval 2026-08-13).\n- buildSurfaceClient walks the Bun metafile's import-statement edges transitively and splices modulepreload links into the shell; dynamic edges never followed; no-split entry byte-identical\n- Measured on Slow 3G: JS critical path 6110 ms → 4095 ms\n- Grok review APPROVE; all three NICE-TO-HAVEs taken\n\n- **olai collected it: PR #139 (squash d7cf177)** — the built shell now carries the modulepreload for the entry's shared chunk, verified in dist before merge. The loop #129 opened is closed.\n- **drishti pair: PR #140 (srid/drishti, squash dfcb26e)** — same repin, 12/12 CI green on the re-run (first run's typecheck miss was a workspace hydration hiccup: @kolu/solid-pwa-install invisible on the box, clean locally and on re-run).\n\nAll three repos now on kolu e7f0391.\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:13:49-04:00"}
{"id":"preference-receptacle","parent":"viewing","ord":"aP","title":"createPreference: one receptacle for the read→signal→write→watch preference spelling","done":"2026-08-13T14:29:06-04:00","desc":"Flagged by PR #131 (preferences panel); ratified as the headline of the 2026-08-13 lowy-electricity debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-13.md item 1). **Shipped as PR #142 (squash a66154a), 2026-08-13.**\n- One factory `createPreference` in web/src/client/preference.ts: codec per key, one option (`persist: false` — the drag handles keep the live/commit split), `stored()` as the escape hatch fold memory's union-merge reads through\n- Eight circuits migrated (sidebar open/width, chat open/width/snap, folds, sidebar folders, done default)\n- Theme stays OFF per the debate — the boot script owns the first paint read, theme/state.ts keeps the primitives\n- Claim test grips the call: `/\\b(read|watch)Preference\\s*\\(/` in no client file outside preference.ts, its test, theme/state.ts\n- #138's fold semantics survive verbatim — and are now LOCKED: the review's one MUST-FIX was that deleting the write-side union-merge left all 24 tests green; the fix round added the setFolded-against-real-storage test that reds under exactly that sabotage\n\n**Pipeline:**\n- Grok review (verified the inert resize-nudge claim against master's own Solid, hunted flattening, found only the missing lock)\n- Fix round red-first\n- NTHs: per-setter opts-hop tests + claim regex + architecture.md taken; resize re-fit declined as a behavior change under binding parity\n- DELTA-OK\n- Then #141 landed: master merged (one docs hunk, both sides preserved), CI 10/10 at dc5128d on kolu-ci-1\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"quiet-pill-unify","parent":"viewing","ord":"aQ","title":"One quiet-pill: the button class string spelled five times across five modules","done":"2026-08-13T17:09:18-04:00","desc":"Flagged by PR #134 (the depth pass); debate 2026-08-13 reclassified it plain cleanup (a class string is not an axis). **Shipped as PR #146 (squash 5c591e6), 2026-08-13**, under the human's pixel-parity-binding ruling.\n- One definition (`web/src/client/pill.ts` QUIET_PILL) worn by the three sites that render identically: chat Header, git Unpushed's dismiss sibling, menu confirm's Cancel — whose bg-transparent dropped only because Tailwind preflight already paints it, verified in built CSS\n- The two sites with a geometry of their own stay divergent with comments saying why: AskForm's h-8 dismiss paired to the accent answer; Unpushed's py-0.5 Push inside a text-xs line\n- Claim test: only pill.ts spells the string (sabotage-verified naming both files)\n- Evidence: all 12 before/after shots byte-identical (cmp clean), chalk+pitch, desktop+phone\n- CI 10/10 on kolu-ci-1\n- Review skipped on the human's word; merged on their approval\n","changed":"2026-08-19T19:14:56-04:00"}
{"id":"fold-memory","parent":"viewing","ord":"aR","title":"Fold memory: the outline remembers how you left it #ui","done":"2026-08-13T11:23:14-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #138 (squash 8098561, merged 2026-08-13).\n- Folds are a preference of this browser: `olai.folds` via `preference.ts`.\n  - Collapsed node ids grouped by defining file, keyed by NODE ID so folds survive reload, zoom round-trips, and moves.\n  - Mirrors fold together per the ratified ruling (one fold vocabulary, `fold/rows.ts`).\n- Sidebar folders get the same memory (`olai.sidebar.folders`, inverted — folders start shut).\n- **Grok review:** one real MUST-FIX — pruning treated a MOVE (archive) as deletion — fixed red-first at both levels plus a write-side twin.\n- Cross-tab writes upgraded from LWW to union-merge so a sibling tab's unrelated fold survives.\n- Delta-verified; CI 10/10 Linux green at head.\n- Docs corrected where they encoded the bug's premise.\n- **Note for preference-receptacle:** the `createPreference` factory was deliberately declined here as out of scope — it remains that node's job.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"website-refresh","parent":"website","ord":"a0","title":"Website refresh: six shipped PRs the site never heard about","done":"2026-08-13T11:13:42-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #137 (squash df23fe3, merged 2026-08-13).\n- The site caught up with #128–#133:\n  - A new Agenda section (predicate byte-for-byte with `agenda.ts`, the row picker, occurrences).\n  - Preferences with all fifteen palettes hex-for-hex as chips wearing their own colors.\n  - The mark walk as shipped (the ring corrected against `server/src/edit.ts` — done is not a stop; the author caught the brief's error).\n  - Chat file diffs.\n  - A swept `#format`/hero/daily.\n- **Grok review:** no MUST-FIX, accuracy verified against packages, both judgment calls accepted.\n  - Two NICE-TO-HAVEs taken in a final round (the daily-notes mock now shows scheduled and finished side by side — a day-page fact the site never had).\n- CI 10/10 Linux green at ddf0dea.\n- **Ruling honored:** the site describes MASTER; a depth touch-up follows only if/when depth merges.\n- HACKING.md's website/ checklist line keeps it current from here.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"owed-moves","parent":"infra","ord":"aF","title":"Owed moves: GitState home, scale.ts home, wire.ts plugs into surfaceWsUrl #techdebt","done":"2026-08-13T14:33:36-04:00","desc":"Three small debts ratified by the 2026-08-13 lowy-electricity debate (items 3, 5, 6). **Shipped as PR #143 (squash 9bd7048), 2026-08-13.**\n- **(1) GitState** declared once in `format/src/committing.ts` beside RepoState.\n  - The reviewer diffed the deleted mirrors field-by-field against the new declaration.\n  - Surface re-exports, zero consumer churn; GIT_OFF traveled.\n  - ops' zero-importer public export (verified zero ON MASTER) dropped.\n- **(2) scale.ts → theme/** with every path reference followed (build, CSS banner, tests, fixtures, README).\n- **(3) wire.ts:36-39 deleted** — the dial calls the pin's `surfaceWsUrl(location.origin)` as a thunk.\n  - Laziness verified (import reads no location; URL parity checked across real origins).\n- **Claim tests:** `/connectSurface\\s*\\(/` equality with `[\"wire.ts\"]` (vacuity-probed both directions), and no client file outside `connection/status.ts` spells the readout's raw states.\n- **Pipeline:**\n  - Grok review — zero MUST-FIX, the zero-behavior-change claim held.\n  - NTHs taken (three READMEs follow the restory; regex widened). DELTA-OK twice.\n  - Then #141 and #142 landed: master merged (one real conflict in `chat/Entry.tsx`, both sides preserved; claims sweep extended over #141's new files).\n  - CI 10/10 at dba732a on kolu-ci-1.\n  - The author also caught and discarded a phantom-green first CI attempt (stream events with no durable artifacts) — re-ran and verified against per-node logs.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"fault-root-upstream","parent":"infra","ord":"aG","title":"Upstream: a throw must not be a white tab — kolu takes a required `fault` #upstream","done":"2026-08-13T16:36:24-04:00","desc":"Debate-ratified 2026-08-13 (item 4; human approved every PR). **Fully shipped, both sides.**\n- **kolu #2164:**\n  - Composition root takes required `fault` like `retired`.\n  - `thrownText` printer upstreamed with the review-hardened lost-message rule (`firstLine === named` — the Grok review caught `includes` dropping short messages behind Safari frames, fixed red-first).\n  - The boundary records to console before the LOOK.\n- **kolu #2165:** `connectSurface.url` optional, defaulting via `surfaceWsUrl`, named error before allocation without a `location` (a fix, per Position C).\n- drishti paired at the master repin.\n- **olai #145 (squash 120904b):** kolu pin → dad81604.\n  - `main.tsx`'s hand ErrorBoundary + record + `thrown.ts` all deleted — the shell rides the standalone `SurfaceFaultBoundary` with `fault={(text) => <Fault text={text}/>}`.\n  - `Fault.tsx` keeps only the LOOK (pixel-identical, verified chalk+pitch with a real injected fault in the packaged binary).\n  - `wire.ts` drops its `url` line for #2165's default.\n  - Riders: `undoing.ts` takes Apply as an argument; bun-test gets a stub location.\n  - Missing `fault` is a compile error (sabotage: TS2322).\n  - The white-tab e2e now pins the heading olai owns and names its failure instead of a bare timeout.\n- **Pipeline:**\n  - Grok review (one MUST-FIX: README described the deleted wiring; three NTHs all taken).\n  - Delta-verify caught one more stale comment.\n  - Final sweep verified zero present-tense mentions of the old seam.\n  - CI green at 030b85b on kolu-ci-1.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"ask-vocabulary","parent":"agents","ord":"aJ","title":"@olai/acp: the ask vocabulary moves to the wall that speaks ACP","done":"2026-08-13T15:25:45-04:00","desc":"Debate-ratified 2026-08-13 (item 2); Position A resolved by the human to fable's wall. **Shipped as PR #144 (squash fbbc15a), 2026-08-13.**\n- New workspace package `@olai/acp` owns the protocol's words:\n  - AskField/AskChoice/AskAnswer/AskOutcome/YES_NO on `./wire` (surface re-exports — no consumer moved an import).\n  - FileDiff judged same-tenant with the argument written at the declaration.\n  - asks/diffs projections + Form/Refused on the main entry.\n- **UsageFailure** translated at the seam, not moved: `Refused` (a plain value, never on a wire or Effect channel) is minted into UsageFailure in exactly one place (`questions.ts`) and read in one (`agent.ts`).\n- **The boundary is machine-checked:** a six-claim manifest test over one tree scan (position-based specifiers + `Bun.Transpiler.scanImports`).\n  - No `@olai/*` import may appear inside acp.\n  - SDK runtime imports only in the subprocess files; matcher covers SDK subpaths.\n- **Pipeline:**\n  - Grok review — zero MUST-FIX; the boundary judgment verified file-by-file against Position A (and the losing floor position used to sharpen the cut).\n  - All four NTHs taken red-first (subpath matcher via the reviewer's own sabotage). DELTA-OK twice.\n  - Parity: 1224 unit, 384 e2e twice (local + CI), packaged-binary smoke; CI green at 8afbc08 on kolu-ci-1.\n  - One test-lane flake (pre-existing kolu fixture's SDK parse noise) judged unrelated and green on rerun.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"store-graduation","parent":"infra","ord":"aH","title":"Leave @olai/store alone until it has proven stable — then decide whether it moves out","desc":"A watch item, not work.\n- The 2026-08-13 design debate noticed `@olai/store`'s source did not change at all during the busiest thirteen-PR week, suggesting it is finished enough to one day live outside this repo.\n- No move now.\n- **Open:** the trigger for revisiting.\n  - Two of the debaters said \"untouched across two consecutive releases, or 180 days without edits from 2026-08-12\" is enough.\n  - The third wanted 90 quiet days AND a second consumer of `Store.make`.\n- The human has not picked a wording.\n- When the trigger fires, decide then whether the package graduates.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00","custom":{"clock":"interrupted — debate #3 (2026-08-19) verified 8 commits into store/src since 08-13, the face (index.ts) twice; stillness counts from the LAST src edit, not 2026-08-12; and whether the socket absorbing volatility resets or reinforces the clock is the same wording question this node parks (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md, corrections)"}}
{"id":"chat-subjects","parent":"agents","ord":"aK","title":"Associations: things that belong to things — chats, nodes, notes #needs-brainstorm","desc":"The human's want, 2026-08-13, reframed meta-level at their direction: one association mechanism for \"this is about that\" across olai's three kinds of things.\n- **chat ↔ node** (the original chat-subjects idea): session named `olai/<node-id>` via claude's named conversations, ••• resumes-or-starts, icon on the node.\n- **node ↔ note**: wanted regardless; likely an outline edge like see/after.\n- **chat ↔ note**: collapses to the other two — a chat about a note is the chat of its home node.\n- Brainstorm: `docs/brainstorming/associations.md`.\n- Awaits ratification.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"hindsight-comparison","parent":"agents","ord":"aL","title":"Olai vs Hindsight: address every con in olai's own grammar #needs-brainstorm","desc":"The human's request, 2026-08-13: thorough comparison against hindsight.vectorize.io (agent-memory: LLM retain/recall/reflect over Postgres) with recommendations to address every olai con.\n- Brainstorm: `docs/brainstorming/hindsight.md`.\n- Six recommendations, all keeping files-as-the-single-truth (smarter things are derived readings):\n  1. Semantic search as a gitignored derived index off the live store's change stream.\n  2. Temporal+graph recall as Query clauses (the graph and dates already exist).\n  3. Capture-as-proposal at conversation end via the chat-diffs surface.\n  4. Consolidation as an agent-assisted stale/duplicates reading, evidence = git blame.\n  5. Multi-agent scoping via per-connection outline/tag subsets + lifting the singleton ACP session.\n  6. Cross-machine sync stays git, auto pull/rebase with conflicts surfaced per silent-errors doctrine.\n- **Deliberately not copied:** LLM normalization of the user's words, memory-bank identity config, hosted memory.\n- Awaits the human's picks.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-model-pin","parent":"infra","ord":"aI","title":"Each repo should pin which model its agents run — written by apm, not by hand #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"Root cause 2026-08-13: every dispatched lane ran bare `claude`, whose machine default was Fable — burning the human's Fable limit all day.\n- Nothing pinned the model and Claude Code's footer never shows it.\n- **What was proven** (scratch-repo tests, valid):\n  - A repo `.claude/settings.json` with `\"model\"` + `\"permissions\": {\"defaultMode\": \"bypassPermissions\"}` makes a bare `claude` boot the pinned model with bypass on.\n  - The repo file beats the machine default.\n- **What was wrongly shipped and REVERTED:**\n  - The orchestrator hand-committed that file to olai and drishti WITHOUT authorization.\n  - `.claude/settings.json` is apm-generated output; hand-writing a generated surface was wrong twice over.\n  - olai: file removed (this commit); drishti: reverted (e987edc).\n- **The real fix must be apm-based** (the human's direction): these repos will adopt apm.\n  - The model/permissions pin gets AUTHORED in apm's source of truth and COMPILED into `.claude/settings.json`.\n  - Solution being designed — see apm-adoption.\n- **Interim, in force now:**\n  - Every spawn passes `--model opus --dangerously-skip-permissions` explicitly.\n  - The orchestrator verifies via /status before chartering.\n  - The machine default is also saved as Opus.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"apm-adoption","parent":"infra","ord":"aJ","title":"Adopt apm so agent briefs, skills and settings become versioned packages instead of per-lane rewrites #needs-brainstorm","desc":"Raised by the human 2026-08-13 while fixing the model-pin failure.\n- apm (Agent Package Manager) is a dependency manager for agent CONFIGURATION — skills, `.agent.md` definitions, prompts, MCP wiring — declared in `apm.yml`, compiled per-runtime.\n  - odu already ships its CI skill via `.apm/skills/`.\n  - drishti already carries `.claude/apm-hooks.json`.\n- **The prospect:** the orchestrator's hand-written per-lane BRIEF.md files, the Grok reviewer checklist, and the sabotage-verify discipline become versioned `.apm` packages.\n  - Portable across the claude/grok/opencode cast and installable into kolu/drishti instead of re-spelled per lane.\n- **Caveats found in its tracker:**\n  - Claude Code is a first-class deploy TARGET (settings.json, hooks, skills, marketplace) but not a runtime apm can launch.\n  - Grok target support merged experimental (#2420).\n- **Watch item:** if apm gains Claude Code as a launchable runtime with model config, it could absorb the launch layer that `.claude/settings.json` (see agent-model-pin) covers today.\n- Awaits the human's word on a design pass.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"done-pref","parent":"viewing","ord":"aS","title":"The Done pill belongs to Prefs","done":"2026-08-13T20:53:53-04:00","desc":"The human's call, 2026-08-13, from a screenshot of the floating \"Done: Hidden\" pill. **Shipped as PR #151 (squash 8ae7ed87), merged 2026-08-14.**\n- #131 had already put the Visible/Hidden control in Prefs; this PR makes Prefs the ONE home.\n  - The floating pill retires entirely, and the per-page override dies with it (\"a default for a switch nobody can press is a lie\").\n  - The empty-state copy on an all-done zoomed node stays, now the honest explanation rather than duplicate chrome.\n- Rides `olai.done.hidden` on the `createPreference` factory — persisted like theme (the human's requirement).\n  - Cross-tab follow and reload both pinned (reload pin sabotaged red-first: drop the write, reload forgets).\n- **Authored by GROK, reviewed by Claude Opus** (the alternation's other direction).\n  - The review verified the #131 claim, re-ran the author's sabotages.\n  - Demanded the master merge (five files from #147/#148/#152, resolved with the font PR's prefs work preserved).\n- All 15 checks green at c77cd395 including e2e 6m27s.\n  - An earlier local readout claiming five undo reds was a load-era artifact contradicted by the posted statuses.\n- Merged on the human's approval.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"orchestrator-home","parent":"infra","ord":"aK","title":"The orchestrator gets a real home inside olai — formalize what the prototype proved #needs-brainstorm","desc":"Opened 2026-08-13 after the Fable-limit burn and the compaction-memory problem.\n- Brainstorm at `docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md`.\n- **UPDATE 2026-08-16** — much of this is no longer hypothetical.\n  - Since 08-15 the orchestration runs as a live prototype in `docs/orchestrator/`.\n    - `agents.olai` (who can be hired and how).\n    - `dag.olai` (the pipeline template a PR walks).\n    - `lanes.olai` (the live board, one lane per PR, every step a node with after-edges).\n  - All written only through olai's own ops, with a terminal orchestrator driving kolu terminals and the human ruling at #human gates.\n  - Ten-plus PRs have shipped through it.\n- **What this item still owes:** turning that proven shape into olai proper — agents as nodes, lanes as nodes, approvals as verbs, launch via kolu — instead of a charter file plus one long-running chat.\n- **Open questions from the brainstorm:**\n  - Where the launch layer lives (command-in-node vs kolu structured spec vs apm as launcher).\n  - What of the prototype's conventions become product.\n- Awaits the human's picks.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"font-pick","parent":"viewing","ord":"aT","title":"The typeface is a pick: Atkinson by default, a catalog in prefs #human","done":"2026-08-13T19:25:10-04:00","desc":"Authored and merged personally by the human (PR #152, squash a112993f, 2026-08-13, via their own Grok terminal).\n- Atkinson Hyperlegible becomes the default typeface.\n- Font catalog in the Prefs panel: `theme/fonts.ts` + FontSelect, `fontCss` with its own tests, `nix/fonts.nix` packaging, e2e `fonts.feature`.\n- Rides the `createPreference` factory.\n- **Known ripple at merge time:** #151 (done-pref) went DIRTY on the shared Prefs panel and `preferences.feature` — resolved in that lane's round.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"e2e-parallel","parent":"infra","ord":"aL","title":"The e2e suite runs parallel by default, sized to the machine #techdebt","done":"2026-08-13T20:56:00-04:00","desc":"The human's dispatch, 2026-08-13, from the observation that the ~400-scenario suite ran serial everywhere. **Shipped as PR #153 (squash 823a679f), merged 2026-08-14 on the human's direct order.**\n- \"Just squash merge\" — review and remote CI skipped; the kolu-ci network was down and the change is test-infra.\n- Authored by GROK: parallel by default sized to CPU cores, `CUCUMBER_PARALLEL` stays the override (=1 serial).\n- All active lanes were told to merge master so their local CI e2e legs speed up immediately.\n- **Residual to watch:** the write-path 15s-wait scenario family that flaked under box load today.\n  - If parallelism surfaces it in normal runs, deflaking at the root becomes its own item.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"agenda-fire","parent":"viewing","ord":"aU","title":"The Agenda entry burns when work is overdue","done":"2026-08-13T21:19:50-04:00","desc":"The human's dispatch, 2026-08-13, from a sidebar screenshot. **Shipped as PR #154 (squash 78052f04), merged 2026-08-14.**\n- The Agenda entry now burns for overdue work (alarm ink + a count badge) and nudges for today (quiet count), nothing otherwise.\n  - The louder face wins when both hold (face order pinned: 3 unit cases).\n- Derived from the SAME reading the Agenda page computes (one situater — the sabotage that froze the reading froze the page too, the claim proving itself).\n- Live to marks/dates across 4 liveness pins, on the phone sheet (burger-tap scenario).\n- `/simplify` caught a real paint bug pre-merge: text-alarm losing to text-ink on Tailwind emission order.\n- 18 evidence PNGs (3 states × 2 themes × desktop/phone/close-up), archived.\n- Local CI 10/10 at 7e72a68 under the flock (e2e 1m50s on the new parallel suite); no background processes left behind.\n- Authored by Claude Opus (model verified at spawn), merged on the human's approval.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-restore-wrong","parent":"bugs","ord":"aH","title":"Restart restores the wrong chat: newest-in-directory is an identity guess","done":"2026-08-13T23:12:05-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-14 on the human's report: after olai restarts, the panel restored some OTHER session.\n- Boot adopted the newest-by-updatedAt session in the served directory, an identity guess anything fresher could steal.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-13** (night slate, SIMPLE — autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization): PR #156, squashed at master.\n  - The panel's session id is now olai's own note (chat `memory.ts`, under `$XDG_STATE_HOME`): written when the panel enters a conversation, read back at boot.\n  - Newest-in-directory demoted to first-boot/gone fallback.\n  - Picker rows carry honest local timestamps.\n  - CodeQL's polynomial-redos finding on the trailing-slash regex fixed by counting slashes.\n- **Evidence:** e2e scenario fails on the old `stored[0]` behavior, 50/50 scenarios pass with the fix.\n- **Grok review:** 1 blocking + 2 nits (all doc staleness), addressed at 935d5705; 9/9 required Linux checks green.\n- The superseded-by-hint dead end moved to its own node under Bugs (#upstream #human).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"fonts-in-store","parent":"infra","ord":"aM","title":"Fonts convert once, in the Nix store — not on every build #techdebt","done":"2026-08-13T23:03:47-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-14 on the human's report.\n- PR #152 had put the seam in the wrong place: `nix/fonts.nix` copied raw TTFs and `build.ts` converted all faces to woff2 on every client build.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-13** (night slate; the human pre-approved the merge): PR #155, squashed at master 9f1e1761.\n  - `woff2_compress` now runs in `@olai/fonts`' package-local `default.nix` (store outputs .woff2 directly, 70 faces).\n  - The client build only copies by name.\n  - `@olai/fonts` owns the catalog (`typefaces.ts`), the sheet (`css.ts`), `hosted.json` and the derivation; `nix/fonts.nix` deleted.\n- **Grok review:** 0 blocking, 1 nit (~40→70 docs figure, fixed in 5f113a3).\n- **Evidence** verified independently by the reviewer: store-vs-dist hashes identical, an independent reconversion byte-identical, a clean `just build-client` runs 0 conversions.\n- CI: 9/9 required Linux checks green at 5f113a3.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"gutter-menu-primitive","parent":"wf-gutter-debt","ord":"a0","title":"Menu primitive: Kobalte adoption + shared dismiss helper","done":"2026-08-14T00:51:21-04:00","desc":"Split out 2026-08-13 from the gutter bundle. **MERGED 2026-08-14** (night slate, SIMPLE — autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization): PR #158, squashed.\n- The ••• menu now rides Kobalte's DropdownMenu (lazy Dots mount).\n- `dismiss.ts` is the shared outside-click/Escape helper for `popover.ts` and `note/expand.ts`.\n- **Grok review:** 1 blocking + nits, addressed at ffc7d70.\n  - Blocking: Escape did not restore focus to the ••• — Kobalte's `onCloseAutoFocus` effect never re-runs under the `<Show>` mount shape.\n  - Fixed with an explicit restore plus a keyboard-reopen scenario, the previously unwalked path.\n  - Nits: focus rationale rewritten after browser-verified cause.\n- **Evidence re-shot:** byte-identical or 0-px shots except the intentional caret band (1.765%) and the new 0.075% Escape focus ring.\n- CI 9/9 required green.\n- Unblocked the two sibling items (touch affordance, menu polish).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"gutter-touch-menu","parent":"wf-gutter-debt","ord":"a1","title":"Phones reach the ••• menu: long-press (or another touch affordance)","done":"2026-08-14T03:02:35-04:00","desc":"Split out 2026-08-13 from the gutter bundle. **MERGED 2026-08-14** (night slate, SIMPLE — autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization): PR #161, squashed at 2a4a1665.\n- Long-press on a row opens the ••• menu on phones (previously hidden entirely).\n  - Driven through Chromium's own gesture recogniser in five @phone CDP scenarios.\n  - `door.ts`'s one signal hands out both doors.\n- `/simplify` caught `{...menu.hold}` putting the hottest element on Solid's runtime spread path (classList diffed per row per frame).\n- **Grok review:** 0 blocking, 3 nits — all addressed.\n  - The page-still-scrolls claim became a mutation-proven scenario (touch-none on the row fails it, on scrollY 0, and nothing else).\n  - The reviewer's preventDefault-on-pointerdown example corrected on the record — touch-action/captured-pointer/prevented-touchmove are what claim a gesture.\n  - The title-collision half of `swallowGhost()` asserted.\n  - Three doc leftovers fixed.\n- **Deferrals accepted by the reviewer:** no on-screen discoverability (Workflowy's price), iOS unverified (`-webkit-touch-callout` in the sheet, no real Safari in CI).\n- **Evidence:** byte-identical laptop shots, only the held-phone shot differs.\n- CI 9/9 required green at 2a4a1665.","after":["gutter-menu-primitive"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"gutter-menu-polish","parent":"wf-gutter-debt","ord":"a2","title":"Menu polish: copy-link toast, z-index plan, NodeMenu file split","done":"2026-08-14T04:11:18-04:00","desc":"Split out 2026-08-13 from the gutter bundle. **MERGED 2026-08-14** (night slate, SIMPLE — autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization; the last of the nine): PR #163, squashed at b317637.\n- **Delivered:**\n  - The copy-link/copy-text toast rides `src/client/saying.ts`, one SAID_MS countdown shared with the Trash remark.\n  - A real two-band z-index scale (page stack kept, sealed numbers remapped) with the no-other-file-spells-a-z-* sweep in `claims.test.ts`.\n  - NodeMenu split along the seams the Kobalte adoption exposed (`MenuSaid.tsx` named like `UndoSaid.tsx`).\n- **Grok review:** 0 blocking, 2 nits (stale doc pointers after the sweeps moved) — author fixed three spots, verifying pointers against reality.\n- **Evidence:** 5 byte-identical layered-chrome scenes vs master; 2 sub-pixel diffs proven run-to-run flake by identical signatures on the same build.\n- CI 9/9 required green at b317637.\n- The sibling debts menu-bundle-cost and dismiss-layer-stack remain recorded, untouched.","after":["gutter-menu-primitive"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"superseded-hint-upstream","parent":"bugs","ord":"aI","title":"Superseded-by hint has no protocol source #upstream #human","todo":true,"desc":"Measured during PR #156 (2026-08-13).\n- The pinned Claude Code adapter's `listSessions` answers `{sessionId, cwd, title, updatedAt}` and sets no `_meta` at all.\n- ACP's SessionInfo carries no message count.\n- So the roadmap's \"adapter-supplied superseded hint, only where an adapter offers it\" has nothing to read today, and per-row counts have no protocol source.\n- Any fix is upstream (adapter `_meta`, or ACP SessionInfo).\n- AWAITS THE HUMAN'S RATIFICATION before anything is filed on another repo.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"menu-bundle-cost","parent":"wf-gutter-debt","ord":"a3","title":"Kobalte DropdownMenu rides the first-paint chunk (~24 kB brotli) #techdebt","done":"2026-08-14T21:31:30-04:00","desc":"Surfaced by PR #158 (2026-08-13): adopting Kobalte's DropdownMenu added ~80 kB raw / ~23 kB brotli to the first-paint chunk (the node's ~85/24 title figures were the pre-remeasure numbers).\n- **MERGED 2026-08-14** (night slate, autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization): PR #171, squashed at head 3ae28cd.\n  - `menu/chunk.ts` is the entry-`import()` split (`markdown/chunk.ts`'s pattern).\n  - `Panel.tsx` and `Confirm.tsx` follow the primitive into the chunk.\n  - `src/client/arriving.ts` (`createArrival`) is the shared arrival receptacle for both chunk files.\n  - `features/menu_arrives.feature` pins WHEN the bytes are fetched over the network (`tests/support/chunks.ts` shared with the markdown steps).\n- **Review:** Grok 4 nits + opencode 3 nits, zero blocking, all addressed as docstring/test-only commits.\n  - Emitted client byte-identical, so the bundle table, six byte-identical screenshots and network trace held without re-shooting.\n- CI 9/9 required green at 3ae28cd.\n- **Residue recorded, deliberately not taken:**\n  - `dismiss.ts:53` keeps ~10 kB raw / ~3 kB brotli of Kobalte on first paint (20+ first-paint panels import it — reviewer-verified not removable).\n  - No hover prefetch (a second ask on a different trigger; `menu/Dots.tsx` is where it would go).\n  - Chunk-failure sentence has no countdown (matches `Markdown.tsx`'s decision).\n- The stray e2e flake grok attributed to `input_widgets.feature:209` got its own bug node.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:52-04:00"}
{"id":"dismiss-layer-stack","parent":"wf-gutter-debt","ord":"a4","title":"Dismiss is not one layer stack: Escape with popover + menu up shuts both #techdebt","done":"2026-08-14T23:44:50-04:00","desc":"Surfaced by PR #158 (2026-08-13).\n- `dismiss.ts`'s two callers were not on Kobalte's DismissableLayer stack, so Escape with both a popover and the menu open closed both instead of the topmost.\n- `chat/Sessions.tsx` had no dismissal at all.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-14** (night slate, autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization): PR #172, squashed at efe934b5.\n  - `topmost.ts` is the one stack — popover, menu, Sessions AND the ⌘K palette (found off-discipline by the author's own altitude pass: `whileEditing:true` opened it over popovers and one Escape took both).\n  - The un-enforceable rule written where the stack lives: a layer answers a dismissal from the document or later, never from its own box.\n- **Review:** Grok + opencode, zero blocking.\n  - opencode walked pairs the e2e doesn't (triples, phone viewport).\n  - All five nits fixed as isolated commits including the reverse-order `dismiss_stack` scenario.\n- CI 9/9 required green at efe934b5. Two menu scenarios that fail on master pass here.\n- **Residuals on the record:**\n  - `palette/Shortcuts.tsx` modal still ignores Escape (missing affordance, Sessions' old class — both reviewers concurred it is its own item).\n  - SlashMenu's capture handler taking Enter aimed elsewhere (pre-existing, judged against the new rule during review).\n  - Mobile scrims' one-tap-two-things — both reviewers walked it: the picker rides inside the sheet's dismissal because it is IN the sheet (lawful).\n  - No unit test for `topmost.ts` — Solid's server build does not propagate signal→memo; held by e2e and two `claims.test.ts` sweeps, `arriving.ts`'s precedent, Grok-endorsed.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:53-04:00"}
{"id":"undo-feature-flaky","parent":"bugs","ord":"aJ","title":"undo.feature races a write against the assertion after it #techdebt","done":"2026-08-14T09:00:48-04:00","desc":"The e2e flake was one mistake in six places: a write goes out through a DRAFT, the draft is the only receipt this tab gives, and no key step waited for it.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-14** (PR #164, the human approved, squashed at 96b1dfb).\n  - \"I press\" / \"I type\" / \"I select all and type\" / \"I click away\" now wait for the caret to be in the line before aiming, and to leave the PLACE (`Row.key`: chain + seat) after — or for the page to say why not.\n  - \"I press … without waiting\" remains for the two scenarios that mean the race.\n  - Two disk assertions fixed: waiting readers go through `world.servedNodesSoFar` (ENOENT and nothing else — a non-JSON line still faults).\n  - The holding-negative \"holds no node titled\" split from its waiting twin (five holding uses remain, listed on the PR).\n- **Proof:** 5/5 undo runs and 3/3 five-feature runs failed under load before; 12/12 green after, 12/12 again post-`/simplify`, 3/3 after the review round.\n  - No timeout raised, no retry added, no claim loosened — red runs now name what they waited for (mutant-proven wording).\n- CI 9/9 required at 96b1dfb.\n- **Two product findings reported, not fixed**, each its own node under Bugs: new-line-blur-caret and client-quiescence (#human).\n- **MERGE-ORDER NOTE for the open PRs:** #159 and #162 each carry their own copies of the two disk fixes.\n  - Whichever lands after this conflicts textually in `editing_steps.ts` — keep THIS reader (`servedNodesSoFar`, ENOENT only) and one copy of the step.\n  - Their local `recordsIn` blanket-catch swallows malformed records and must not survive.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:53-04:00"}
{"id":"client-quiescence","parent":"bugs","ord":"aK","title":"The client publishes no quiescence: a refused key is indistinguishable from the last #human","todo":true,"desc":"FINDING from PR #164 (2026-08-14).\n- Structural re-focuses the row and collapses its selection after a write answers (`RowEditor.tsx`'s `takeCaret`).\n- A refused key redraws nothing — so a second refusal is indistinguishable from the first, and no harness can know a refused key has been answered.\n- Under load this landed inside the next gesture (`keyboard_editing.feature:264`: ⌘A collapsed mid-retype, title prepended instead of replaced — twice in ~30 loaded runs before #164's move-key receipts, not since).\n- #164's receipts cover every key that MOVES the caret; keys that redraw a row without moving it (Control+Enter and the walk beside it) still have no receipt, and the module says so.\n- **The honest fix:** the product publishing its own quiescence — a counter bumped when a key is enqueued, cleared when the queue drains — which covers all keys at once.\n- A product change made for tests: THE HUMAN'S CALL.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:06:53-04:00"}
{"id":"new-line-blur-caret","parent":"bugs","ord":"aL","title":"Clicking away from a brand-new line leaves the caret in the row it just made","done":"2026-08-15T16:47:25-04:00","desc":"FINDING from PR #164's era (2026-08-14): clicking away from a brand-new line left the caret in the row it just made.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-15** (pre-approved on the orchestrator's visual verification): PR #187, squashed at 4d031cb.\n- **Root cause** exactly the node's hypothesis: every caret keeps its address for life EXCEPT a brand-new line's.\n  - The write that lands it mints the row's id, so the blur guard read \"the reader moved\" about a reader who never did.\n- **Fix:** the landed row carries the slot it was typed at (`Editing.was` — one writer, one reader, always-a-row forwards nothing, sabotage-proven); blur asks `stillAt`.\n- Three red-first scenarios across all three anchors.\n  - The disclosed timing window (click inside `IDLE_COMMIT` or the idle timer masks the bug) proven asymmetric by review — a slow runner gets a loud timeout, never a silent pass.\n- **Reviews:** Grok + opencode, zero blocking, zero nits.\n- The orchestrator verified the before/after frames by eye: an open editor where the click should have landed, then nothing being typed.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"multiselect-completion","parent":"editor","ord":"a9","title":"Picking completed: drag-across marquee, edge auto-scroll, touch drag","done":"2026-08-14T16:33:15-04:00","desc":"The deferrals PR #159 named, taken up 2026-08-14 at the human's word. **MERGED 2026-08-14** (PR #169, the human approved, squashed at e9adceb).\n- **Drag-across marquee**: allowlist not preventDefault; band not box; the flat page gains its rail at the ul so depth 0 sweeps like everywhere else.\n- **Edge auto-scroll**: window decides whether, page decides where; still pointer keeps scrolling.\n- **Touch drag**: long-press on the bullet lifts the row; scroll claimed at the deadline with non-passive touchmove, not `touch-action:none`; the mutation-proven fence green with a sister scenario.\n- **Design ruling shipped panel-converged:** the bullet is the one drag handle on all devices (both reviewers independently recommended it).\n- Panel grok 0+2 / opencode 0+3, union addressed; the `userSelect` single-writer premise is a `claims.test.ts` sweep.\n- CI 9/9 at e9adceb; 551 scenarios / 4110 steps.\n- **Still deferred:** the delete key (the human's ruling), tone/role unification, sweep-union modifier, finger-sweep (permanent no).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"reads-on-the-floor","parent":"surface-mcp","ord":"a1","title":"Query-shaped reads move to the format floor","done":"2026-08-14T22:41:42-04:00","desc":"Deferral from PR #167 (2026-08-14), recorded with THREE traps:\n1. The shared read-request vocabulary must go to `@olai/format`, NOT `@olai/ops`.\n2. `Applied` cannot be included — the two sides are deliberately different types.\n3. An Outline schema in `format/searching.ts` would collide with the Outline the package already exports from `set.ts:62` via `index.ts`.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-14** (night slate, autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization): PR #170, squashed at head 95d69fc — a pure refactor by the end.\n  - All three traps respected.\n  - **Drift property** proven by experiment and extended twice by the review round.\n    - The `as SearchHit` cast became an annotation (a SearchHit-only field now fails ops+web+server where it compiled clean before).\n    - `NodeContext` borrows Found's field schemas (dropping `Found.path` now fails `@olai/chat` too).\n- **Review:** Grok + opencode, zero blocking, every nit fixed or answered on the record; all commits verified standalone.\n- CI 9/9 required green at 95d69fc.\n- **One behavior change the branch had carried** — trimming `list_outlines`' torn-file answer — was REVERTED before merge (nothing unratified lands overnight) and became its own #human node.\n- **The three concurred declines** became their own #techdebt nodes: the four-way `{file,line}` spelling, `read()`'s request-half inference, `outlines()`'s O(files × nodes) walk.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"per-face-expose","parent":"agents","ord":"aB","title":"Upstream: serveSurfaceApp cannot scope a verb per face #upstream #human","done":"2026-08-15T09:03:32-04:00","desc":"Deferral from PR #167 (2026-08-14): the 18 write tools have no surface procedure, and giving them one puts the ops request vocabulary on the surface.\n- `serveSurfaceApp` took handlers whole with no expose list, so every open tab could call every verb.\n- **DONE 2026-08-15:** the human approved and kolu PR [#2170](https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2170) is squash-merged at bfb4eb56.\n  - `@kolu/surface/expose` gives every serving face the same ExposeMap grammar (`classifyExpose`), a checked `FaceExposure` at the handler seam, `SurfaceMemberNotExposed` as the per-request refusal.\n  - The night's review round contributed one real fix (`Object.prototype` keys no longer listable as members).\n  - Drishti pair srid/drishti#142 re-pinned to bfb4eb56 (tarball byte-identical to the reviewed tree) and MERGED on the human's word; lane torn down clean.\n- Issue [#2169](https://github.com/juspay/kolu/issues/2169) STAYS OPEN for the writable-primitive-on-gated-face spelling.\n  - The PR's `Closes #2169` auto-closed it at merge and the author reopened it with the landed-vs-open split written out.\n- **LESSON**, worth a HACKING line someday: a multi-slice issue wants \"Part of #n\" in PR bodies, never \"Closes #n\".\n- Two framework-shape questions stay recorded on #2170 for srid (one expose currency across faces; expose-required + exposeEverything), cheapest while a drishti gate is open.\n- **What this unblocked:** mcp-bridge, dispatched the same day.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"mcp-bridge","parent":"agents","ord":"aBV","title":"The bridge shape: an external agent attaches to the RUNNING olai","done":"2026-08-15T11:16:32-04:00","desc":"Deferral from PR #167 (2026-08-14). UNBLOCKED 2026-08-15 by kolu #2170 (bfb4eb56); ratified as ONE PR, three stages.\n- **Now** (2026-08-15):\n  - Kolu terminal: `cd13fd33` (Claude Opus, YOLO), olai repo, branch `mcp-bridge`.\n  - PR: #175 — pin bump.\n    - ALL write verbs (19, not the node's 18 — md-editing postdates it, noted in code) as surface procedures.\n    - MCP face exposed, browser face denied.\n    - The bridge: `olai mcp` attaches to a running server over the unix socket, boots its own store only when none runs.\n    - Design doc: `docs/brainstorming/mcp-bridge.md`.\n  - **Audit correction** carried honestly: the 418 MB two-store price was misread.\n    - An `olai mcp` over an EMPTY directory is already 213.8 MiB (Bun runtime, not corpus); memory does not halve.\n    - The fd story stays with bun-watcher-bump (the bridge's remaining 1048 descriptors are the watcher's).\n  - **Decisions for srid at fielding:**\n    - Writer became a per-FACE binding (`ops.commit` twin deleted — it existed only to carry the field and had drifted on its error channel).\n    - The three READS became procedures too (stage 3 could not leave them behind).\n  - **Deferred on the record:**\n    - `socket.ts:86` realpath vs `directory.ts:16` string-trim — two canonicalisations of \"which directory\" (symlink → same socket, different chat memory), pre-existing, not widened.\n    - chat-agent face's writer has no e2e trailer test (fenced only, same as before).\n    - Socket latency unmeasured, said so in the doc.\n  - **Stage:** #review — Grok (`dc5279c5`) and opencode (`0be27fed`), briefed to run the DRY drift experiment themselves, re-verify the 213.8 MiB baseline, and attack the canonicalisation seam.\n  - **CI:** 8/9 at 47c5d52c with e2e finishing under the author's monitor (10/10 at both preceding heads).\n  - **Then:** FIELDED to the human — the orchestrator merges only on his word.","after":["per-face-expose"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"watcher-fd-cost","parent":"surface-mcp","ord":"a4","title":"The recursive watcher holds one fd per served file, per store, for life #techdebt","done":"2026-08-14T23:32:02-04:00","desc":"FINDING from PR #167's two-store measurement (2026-08-14): the store's recursive watcher holds one open fd per served file, per store, for the process's lifetime.\n- 14 fds with `watch:false` vs 1050 with `watch:true` on a 1020-file vault.\n- **CLOSED 2026-08-14** (night slate) as an investigation, per the human's small-or-stop ruling — NO CODE, one doc: PR #173, squashed at df2a646, `docs/brainstorming/watcher-fd-cost.md`.\n- **The cost is BUN'S:** 1.3.13's `fs.watch` routes through Bun's internal bundler watcher, one `open(2)` per path under the ROOT (.git and node_modules included — the real multiplier).\n  - Bun 1.3.14's rewrite onto inotify/FSEvents/kqueue drops it to ~15 descriptors and closes the post-boot-subdir blind spot.\n- Per-directory watching, the brief's own proposal, measured at identical cost on 1.3.13 — no small fix existed.\n- **Both reviewers reproduced every conclusion independently** (fact-check round: nits only, all re-measured and folded, one honest 13-fd run-divergence explained in the doc).\n  - Grok's intelligence about nixpkgs#519796 being held on a bun-compile SIGSEGV olai wouldn't hit is left in the review record.\n- **Successor nodes:** bun-watcher-bump (#human, the ruling) and watcher-postboot-blind (the bug the bump also fixes).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"someday","ord":"zzVV","title":"Someday/Maybe","desc":"Work deliberately parked — not active, not abandoned. An entry here holds everything needed to resume cold: the PR/branch, the lane, and the obligations that attach at resume time."}
{"id":"semantic-recall-parked","parent":"someday","ord":"a0","title":"Semantic recall — PR #165 drafted and parked","desc":"Parked 2026-08-14 at the human's word (\"I don't want to actively do it now\") with the pipeline COMPLETE.\n- Panel-reviewed (grok 0+5, opencode 0+4, union addressed at b3721c2), CI 9/9 there.\n- Evidence and design doc done (`docs/brainstorming/semantic-recall.md` — llama-cpp + bge-small nix-native, +196 MB, exact-first, ≈ marker, byte-for-byte off-pin).\n  - Measured 0% CPU idle, ~3 ms/warm query, 71–84 MB RSS.\n- **State:** PR #165 converted to DRAFT, open.\n  - Lane `cfad244a` (worktree `.worktrees/semantic-recall`, branch `semantic-recall`) left running at the human's word; reviewer splits killed.\n- **To resume:**\n  1. Merge master and re-fit — the search seam moved twice since (#167's `format/searching.ts` declaration, #168's filter grammar).\n  2. The 2026-08-14 debate ratified two RE-FIT OBLIGATIONS that bind at merge:\n     - `matched: \"meaning\"` declared on the format floor as `optionalKey([...SEARCH_FIELDS, \"meaning\"])` with the PR's local surface schema deleted.\n     - `searchWith` consuming the parsed filter (refused query keeps `refusals` and does not fill; no operator tokens as prose to the embedder; paraphrase hits honor is:/file/under — the recall leg gets the residual text).\n  3. Mark ready, re-run CI, field for approval.\n- **Related but independent:** the ratified `@olai/child` receptacle (debate ledger, local `debates/lowy-electricity-2026-08-14/conclusion.md`) would absorb `embedder.ts:509`'s swallowed exec error.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"child-receptacle","parent":"infra","ord":"aN","title":"One shared owner for starting and stopping subprocesses (@olai/child) — awaiting your go-ahead #human","todo":true,"desc":"The 2026-08-14 debate's ratified yield (three debaters, all-three signatures; the precise ledger is local at `debates/lowy-electricity-2026-08-14/conclusion.md` — the docs/ write-up was deleted at the human's word).\n- AWAITS THE HUMAN'S RATIFICATION before dispatch.\n- **The bundle:**\n  1. **A workspace leaf `@olai/child`** owning the subprocess plumbing spelled three times (`chat/pipes.ts`, `@kolu/detect`'s private copy, `recall/embedder.ts`).\n     - Owns: spawn, the exec-error race as typed `unstartable`, drained stderr with the caller naming the sink, kill-with-scope (SIGTERM → grace → SIGKILL).\n     - Explicitly OUT (unanimous): readiness, transport, restart policy, death-LOOK.\n     - Three deletions ride it: `embedder.ts:509`'s swallowed exec error (a bad `OLAI_EMBED_SERVER` should name the file, not time out on /health); `agent.ts`'s graceless bare `kill()` on clean stop; `pipes.ts`'s stale two-callers claim → claim test.\n  2. **Sidecar build unification**: `scripts/embedder.sh` is `scripts/acp-agent.sh` re-typed (its own comment confesses); one nix helper + one `scripts/sidecar.sh` replace both.\n     - The human's stronger shape from review: `nix/sidecars/<name>/default.nix` per sidecar (fonts spirit), the script shrinking to one generic lazy-loader for the dev loop only — the packaged binary is already fully baked.\n  3. **Two fences**: only recall/ reads the embedder env vars (gripping the read, scoped to packages/); only recall/ spells the cache path/tmp-rename.\n  4. **The kill-9 experiment** (decides whether the orphan sweep joins the leaf): nix-built serve, chat panel open, `kill -9` the olai pid, check ps for the adapter.\n     - Dies → sweep stays llama-own as ratified.\n     - Survives → sweep is shared and a 589 MB orphan is the strongest argument.\n  5. **detect's private unstartable**: ruled leftover-of-a-paid-socket; disposition open (export from `@kolu/detect` / wait for the leaf / leave 15 lines). Nothing filed upstream without the human.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"sidebar-pierre-tree","parent":"viewing","ord":"aV","title":"The directory tree gets file icons: adopt @pierre/trees, Workflowy-exact or fall back to icons-only","done":"2026-08-15T00:22:04-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-14 (the human, from a sidebar screenshot: markdown files, olai outlines and folders indistinguishable).\n- RULED the same night: adopt `@pierre/trees` with a pre-ratified icons-only escape hatch.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-15** (night slate, autonomous merge per the human's overnight authorization): PR #174, squashed at 8ea77c16 — THE HATCH, taken on evidence, not on the expected wall.\n  - Styling pierced the shadow DOM fine; pierre was mounted inside the real sidebar and declined on four measured walls, each reproduced by both reviewers (grok's 62 kB figure a byte-identical rebuild):\n    - Rows are never anchors (this column's every entry is a real `<a>` Link).\n    - Virtualized fixed heights truncate where `fileTree.ts` wraps.\n    - An internal scroller against the one-scroll-region rule.\n    - 252,776 raw / 62,250 brotli of Preact on a first-paint surface.\n  - Fifth, for whoever tries again: expansion has no event and no `getExpandedPaths` — fold persistence would poll.\n- **Delivered:**\n  - `client/file/icons.tsx` — folder + document vendored VERBATIM from pierrecomputer/icons (Apache-2.0, attribution + the when-a-real-NOTICE-is-owed rule in the header).\n  - The olai outline drawn to the set's own metrics; `currentColor` so accent/muted rides the row's ink.\n  - The rail's divergent icons unified (the app had two answers to \"what does an outline look like\" — a sabotage-proven scenario now pins both faces).\n  - +2,009 raw / +776 brotli at the merged head, same-base rule now stated beside the table in `packages/web/README.md`.\n- **Review:** zero blocking, five nits all fixed or answered on the record.\n- CI 9/9 required green at 8ea77c16; e2e 590 scenarios at the merged head.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"input-widgets-escape-flake","parent":"bugs","ord":"aM","title":"input_widgets.feature:209 flakes: Escape sometimes fails to close the editor draft #e2e","done":"2026-08-15T17:39:32-04:00","desc":"Caught loose during PR #171's night run (2026-08-14), grok's attribution; bit at least five separate runs across the week.\n- **HUNTED 2026-08-15** (Grok author, terminal `06697db6`): THE FLAKE WAS REAL, AND DOUBLE.\n  1. Escape could resurrect the draft it had just dismissed (isolated repro red on run 3/200, state captured).\n  2. With that fixed alone, a too-early ⌘Z still tripped it at run 150.\n- Both fixed in PR #190.\n- **Proof discipline:** both-fixes 300/300 on :209, neighbors 100/100, full suite clean, unit `kept(null, held)` red-then-green.\n- CI 9/9 at d3e6a75.\n- **Stage:** #review — opencode SOLE reviewer per the human (`91e57e62`), briefed to re-derive both mechanisms from the captured states and loop the proof at its own timing.\n- FIELDED to srid; merge is his word.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"torn-file-answer-trim","parent":"agents","ord":"aM","title":"list_outlines answers a torn file with dead zeros — trim to {file, unreadable}? #human","todo":true,"desc":"Raised inside PR #170 (2026-08-14 night slate): an unreadable outline currently answers `{file, nodes: 0, roots: [], unreadable}` — the zero fields are noise beside the flag.\n- The PR briefly changed it to `{file, unreadable}`; both reviewers verified both in-tree consumers read `.file` only.\n- The orchestrator had it reverted before the overnight merge because no unratified behavior change lands while the human sleeps.\n- **The case is preserved verbatim** in `reading.ts`'s `OutlineSummary` header, `packages/format/README.md:270`, the reverted commit 525f737a, and the PR comment — nothing needs re-deriving.\n- The human says keep the old shape or re-apply the revert's revert; either is one small commit.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"four-way-site-spelling","parent":"infra","ord":"aO","title":"\"A place in the loaded set\" is spelled four ways in @olai/format #techdebt","done":"2026-08-15T17:30:07-04:00","desc":"Found during PR #170's refactor round (2026-08-14), both reviewers concurring: `{file, line}` spelled four ways in `@olai/format`.\n- **FIELDED FOR THE HUMAN 2026-08-15:** PR #188 at 5f92af7e, CI 9/9 green — and the four turned out to be SIX (the PR found `validate.ts`'s inline return type and a web component literally named Site hand-rolling the pair).\n- One `Site` in `node.ts` now.\n- **Drift property** proven both halves: a field added reddens all seven packages and lands on every carrier at once; before, it named only one of four.\n- Public surface 150→151 with Site deliberately reachable; behavior byte-identical, verified by printing export keys.\n- **Reviews:** Grok + opencode, zero blocking, no seventh spelling found by either.\n  - Two doc nits taken (the index header now carries no number beside an appendable list — it was wrong once before, #170's \"Eight\" — and confesses why).\n- **Declined on the record**, reviewers endorsing: no `Order.Order<Site>` for one-and-a-half consumers of different shapes.\n- Merge is the human's word.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"read-request-inference","parent":"infra","ord":"aP","title":"Read tools: TypeScript cannot infer their argument types, so every one spells them by hand #techdebt","done":"2026-08-17T22:27:25-04:00","desc":"Pre-existing, surfaced during PR #170 (2026-08-14): at ops/tools.ts:188 the request half's union Schema.Codec&lt;A,never,never,never&gt; | Schema.Top defeats inference of A, so every read tool hand-annotates its args. The answer half infers since #170. Either a tighter union or a second signature; small type-level work, no runtime change.","changed":"2026-08-17T22:27:25-04:00","custom":{"pr":"230"}}
{"id":"outlines-quadratic","parent":"infra","ord":"aQ","title":"outlines() walks O(files × nodes), three passes per file #techdebt","done":"2026-08-15T21:57:00-04:00","desc":"Pre-existing, surfaced during PR #170 (2026-08-14): ops/query.ts:333's outlines() is O(files × nodes) with three passes per file. Untouched by #170 (out of its scope, both reviewers concurred). Matters as vaults grow; one pass with per-file accumulation is the obvious shape, measured before/after when taken.","changed":"2026-08-15T21:57:01-04:00","custom":{"pr":"198"}}
{"id":"watcher-postboot-blind","parent":"bugs","ord":"aN","title":"A directory created after boot is invisible to the watcher until the 60s backstop","done":"2026-08-15T21:36:05-04:00","desc":"Found 2026-08-14 by the watcher-fd-cost investigation, in what ships today (bun 1.3.13's watcher, Linux).\n- Create a file in a post-boot subdirectory → NO EVENT; edit it → NO EVENT.\n- Only `store.ts:157`'s 60s poll backstop keeps this from being a correctness bug.\n- Measured shape-by-shape; the method and transcript are in `docs/brainstorming/watcher-fd-cost.md`.\n- Fixed upstream by bun 1.3.14's watcher rewrite (the same bump that drops 1050 fds to 15).\n- This node closes with whichever bump path the human rules on bun-watcher-bump, and exists so the blind spot is not forgotten if that ruling waits.","see":["bun-watcher-bump"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00","custom":{"pr":"196"}}
{"id":"bun-watcher-bump","parent":"infra","ord":"aR","title":"File-watching still costs one file descriptor per file — bun 1.3.14 fixed it; pick how we take the fix #human","todo":true,"desc":"The watcher-fd-cost investigation's ask (2026-08-14 night slate; full pricing in `docs/brainstorming/watcher-fd-cost.md`).\n- The one-fd-per-file cost is bun 1.3.13's watcher, O(every file under the root) — .git and node_modules included (2055 fds on a git-shaped corpus, 1004 of them on files olai never reads).\n- Bun 1.3.14's rewrite (Linux/macOS/FreeBSD together) is per-directory: 1050 → 15 fds, and it also closes the post-boot-subdir blind spot (see watcher-postboot-blind).\n- **Nine mutation shapes verified across the bump:** 1.3.14 delivers all nine, 1.3.13 seven.\n  - The one disagreement (create-by-rename source-vs-destination naming) costs olai nothing since `disk.ts:80-85` drops the payload at the edge.\n- `bun test` 1597/1597 on both binaries.\n- **Options, priced:**\n  1. Wait for nixpkgs — zero risk, unknown date, keeps cost + blind spot ← investigator's recommendation.\n  2. Bun override now — buys the fix, forks the runtime, darwin hashes on faith.\n  3. Hand-rolled per-directory watcher — halves the git case, still O(corpus), obsolete on the next bump, not recommended (and kqueue on Darwin makes it lossy).\n  4. Polling — forbidden by the ruling (changes latency/granularity).\n- The surface-mcp bridge is orthogonal: collapsing two stores halves the count but halving O(corpus) is still O(corpus).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"shortcuts-modal-escape","parent":"viewing","ord":"aW","title":"The shortcuts modal has a scrim but ignores Escape","done":"2026-08-15T17:58:54-04:00","desc":"Found by PR #172's altitude pass and both its reviewers (2026-08-14): `palette/Shortcuts.tsx:22` is a modal with a scrim and no Escape dismissal at all — the same missing-affordance class `chat/Sessions.tsx` was before #172 fixed it.\n- Deliberately not folded into #172 (new affordance, not stack discipline; author + both reviewers concurred it is its own item).\n- The fix joins `topmost.ts`'s stack like every other dismissable.\n- **Closed 2026-08-15:** #172 delivered the fix after all (commit 138c66af touches `Shortcuts.tsx` — it joins `topmostWhileOpen` and answers Escape on the window; the file's own header documents it).\n- Human confirmed Escape dismisses the dialog.\n- The \"kept as its own item\" plan was overtaken before this node was ever picked up.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:08:46-04:00"}
{"id":"tests-stray-debris","parent":"bugs","ord":"aO","title":"Stray probe files committed to packages/tests, one hardcoding a dead worktree path","done":"2026-08-15T17:47:07-04:00","desc":"Found by the sidebar-pierre-tree lane (2026-08-15).\n\n- **Found:** packages/tests/_h.ts and _probe.ts — agents' probe scripts accidentally committed, one hardcoding a dead worktree path.\n- **RESOLVED** the same day by the human's ruling: no CI check, just hygiene.\n  - Both files git-rm'd directly on master (718e312e).\n  - The human's own \"no junk files\" line committed to HACKING.md (aa23635e).\n- The check-that-would-catch-them idea lives on at stray-file-green-ci, unratified.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-model-stale","parent":"bugs","ord":"aP","title":"The chat header's model goes stale after /model","done":"2026-08-15T11:16:32-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15 by the human with a screenshot.\n\n- **Diagnosed** systemic: the picker's values are adapter ALIASES while the live system/init id is CANONICAL.\n- labels.get() missed all five rows, so the stale-model warning fired on every change ever and the header answered raw or stale.\n\n**Now** (2026-08-15):\n- Kolu terminal: `485cd9bb`, branch `chat-model-stale`, PR #176 at head 46db630.\n- **Review round done:**\n  - Grok: 1 BLOCKING — constructed the lie (\"Opus (1M context)\" on a 200k session) — plus nits.\n  - opencode: 2 nits.\n  - **ALL ADDRESSED:**\n    - The lane-borrowing inference is gone: an undated live id resolves, a dated pin shows raw, the opus lie is REFUSED (one scenario drives all three arms; cost paid deliberately: a common alias now shows as a raw id).\n    - The if(running) guard deleted on its own demerits (a refusal fallback re-picks via config_option_update — back to whichever-moved-last-wins, pinned by a reconfig scenario).\n    - Video caption corrected.\n    - docs/chat.md documents the refusal.\n  - **Deferred** (argued on the record): no test for first-live-id-disagrees-at-boot — needs a per-scenario spawn knob for one assertion; no baseline branch left to regress into.\n- **Stage:** CI at 46db630 running under the author's monitor, then FIELDED to the human; PR 2 (chat-token-usage) cuts only after his word on PR 1.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-token-usage","parent":"agents","ord":"aN","title":"Chat shows token usage, so /compact stops being a guess","done":"2026-08-15T12:31:51-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15 by the human: the chat gave no view of context consumption, so /compact was a guess.\n\n- **MERGED** 2026-08-15 (pre-approved by the human): PR #178, squashed at fcbb155f.\n- Header draws the newest usage_update frame as a FRACTION (22k/1M) beside the model.\n  - A percentage was rejected on captured evidence: the adapter corrects the window mid-conversation (1000000 → 200000 on the wire), and a percentage read 2% on both sides of a fivefold drop in real headroom.\n- Read in @olai/acp (any agent may send usage); newest frame wins — pinned MID-TURN with a hold verb after Grok caught the fake agent reproducing only half the correction, sabotage-verified both directions.\n- cost arrives on the wire and is deliberately undrawn, with a unit test asserting the drop.\n- **Reviews:** Grok (2 findings + the deeper recursion of its own fix) and opencode (1 blocking) — all addressed with per-finding replies.\n  - The round also produced the pending-review-draft lesson (a review created without a submit event sits invisible — the orchestrator submitted it by API) and the detached-HEAD reviewer hazard.\n- **Deferred** in the PR body:\n  - No compaction-threshold cue yet (wants the human's eye on a real session).\n  - A loaded conversation shows nothing until its first turn (session/load replays without a usage frame — documented where a person meets it).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"olai-extension","parent":"infra","ord":"aS","title":"Outlines are .olai files: the .jsonl extension retires","done":"2026-08-15T11:35:30-04:00","desc":"Ratified 2026-08-15 (docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md Question 3): PURE RENAME, hard cutover, manual mv; this repo migrates in the same PR.\n\n**Now** (2026-08-15):\n- Kolu terminal: `939eb88c` (Claude Opus, YOLO), branch `olai-extension`, PR #177.\n- **Delivered:**\n  - docs/roadmap.olai + docs/Archive.olai via git mv (byte-identical).\n  - OUTLINE_EXT carries the rule (code that decides reads it, prose that describes spells it out — a two-reviewer argument settled on the record).\n  - THE FENCE: tests/extension.test.ts sweeps every git ls-files path for .jsonl, string and filename, six named exemptions, all sabotage-proven.\n    - Its own review round caught the sweep reading packages/ only and choking on gitignored screenshots (git ls-files fixed both).\n- **Stage:** #review — Grok (`5f4fbcb7`) and opencode (`990a07e9`), briefed to hunt spellings outside the fence's reach and to verify the e2e suite actually exercises .olai fixtures (the silent-no-op failure mode).\n- **Parallel-lane fact:** if #175 lands first, this branch re-runs post-rebase and the fence catches #175's .jsonl spellings — the fence working as designed.\n- **Merge:** AUTONOMOUS once review clean + CI green (the human's ruling).\n  - OPERATIONAL NOTE at merge: every running olai server — the orchestrator's own ledger MCP included — reads .jsonl until restarted; the ledger goes quiet between merge and restart, and the human's other vaults migrate by hand (README carries the mv).\n- **Deferrals filed:** stem-strippers-twins, tree-sweep-fixture (which also carries the RCA-path human call).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"agents-outline","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a4","title":"The agents outline: who, as nodes — the launch command lives in a note","done":"2026-08-15T11:20:54-04:00","desc":"Step 1 toward orchestration-in-olai (docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md).\n\n- One node per agent, the exact launch command in its note.\n- Every launcher reads the node before spawning; a missing node refuses loudly — no machine default can decide the model again (the Fable burn's fix).\n- Zero new olai code.\n- Kolu's structured launch spec remains the later upgrade the notes would migrate into.\n- **DONE** 2026-08-15: docs/agents.olai.\n  - Born agents.jsonl — the create_outline call was handed a repo-shaped path and minted docs/docs, fixed by git mv; then PR #177's fence renamed the extension in flight.\n  - Three agents recorded: claude-opus (author), grok (reviewer, --always-approve), opencode (reviewer).\n  - Grok earned an authoring entry the same day (PR #180, solo, review waived).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"workflow-template","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a5","title":"Author the shared workflow outline: the step DAG every lane clones","todo":true,"desc":"The human's idea, 2026-08-15.\n\n- The pipeline every lane walks (implement → refactor → review ×2 → address → CI → evidence → merge) stops being gist prose and becomes a TEMPLATE subtree.\n  - Each step a todo node, dependencies as after edges, fan-out (both reviews before address) expressed natively.\n- The app draws blocked-vs-ready for free.\n- Existing grammar only: marks, after, add_node, descs — no new olai features.\n- **RULED** 2026-08-15: ONE SHARED PLACE — a single orchestration outline every repo's lanes clone from, so the process is defined once.\n  - Cross-repo progress ruled the same day: the lane's step-marks live in the orchestration outline; repo roadmaps keep their own items.\n  - A worked example is in docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md.","after":["node-properties"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"lane-cloning","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a6","title":"Dispatch clones the DAG: a lane is the template copied, marks carry progress","todo":true,"desc":"The lanes half of the doc's organizing idea.\n\n- Dispatching a task clones the workflow template under the lane's node — real copies via add_node (not mirrors: each lane's steps carry their own marks).\n- The PR's progress is marks flipping todo → doing → done, with terminal id, PR and evidence links in the step descs (props, once node-properties lands).\n- The orchestrator's memory becomes the outline and survives anything.\n- **TEMPLATE RULE**, learned from a live incident (2026-08-15: the orchestrator instructed a rebase while two reviewers were still reading the same worktree).\n  - A step that MUTATES the worktree sits `after` every step that READS it — readers fan out, writers wait.\n  - **Enforcement half:** dispatch IS set_doing on the step, so set_doing REFUSING on a blocked node (today it only nudges) turns that discipline into a mechanism — the machine cannot instruct what the DAG forbids.\n  - That refusal is this node's one candidate code change; everything else is authoring and practice.","after":["agents-outline","workflow-template"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"olai-subscribes","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a7","title":"PR: olai subscribes to kolu's urgency/terminals and flips lane marks itself","todo":true,"desc":"The answer to oic-wake, as architecture rather than workaround.\n\n- A server never sleeps between turns, so olai itself holds a real kolu-MCP subscription/stream and updates lane step-nodes live.\n  - Agent-agnostic by construction, because the listener is not an LLM harness.\n- Retires the terminal orchestrator's detached debrief watchers and the hand-flipped marks of lane-cloning's transition.\n- Depends on the bridge-era plumbing (mcp-bridge) and on kolu's stream verbs behaving (the kolu-watch question noted in git history of the brainstorm).","after":["lane-cloning","mcp-bridge"],"changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"node-properties","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a5V","title":"Org-style properties: facts stop living in desc strings #needs-brainstorm","done":"2026-08-15T17:46:15-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15, the human's observation on the ledger's own habit: every \"**Now** (terminal, stage, PR)\" block is structured data smuggled into desc prose — unqueryable, eyeball-parsed — and lane-cloning is about to make it systemic.\n\n- **RULED** 2026-08-15, in four rounds:\n  - Freeform key→value; brainstorm before code; full web parity in the same PR (quiet drawer under the note, ••• menu edits).\n  - Marks are not special — todo/done/date/see/after are LEGACY PROPERTIES; the record unifies into one props map, olai AUTO-MIGRATING each file's shape at startup.\n    - BUILT-IN KEYS ARE POLICED: set_prop refuses every system key toward its own verb (status→set_done and kin, date→set_date, after→set_after); set_prop owns only the keys olai does not read or write.\n    - A user key is promoted by gaining a READING, never by changing shape.\n  - The stage is NEVER a property: a lane's stage is its cloned DAG's `doing` step.\n  - Workflowy's pair joins as stamps: `created` (at capture) and `changed` (re-stamped by every write op) — no verb at all, nothing else may write them.\n    - Absent on migrated nodes (the ledger does not invent a past); appearing as nodes are touched.\n- **BRAINSTORM:** [docs/brainstorming/properties.md](/doc/docs/brainstorming/properties.md) (example-first; UNCOMMITTED, awaiting the human's review), with the interactive drawer prototype linked inside: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/48a09a59-5079-44fe-b99a-7f3a5fe49c90 (insertion order, not alphabetical — a position on open question 1).\n- **STILL OPEN:** whether search HITS carry props (one query = the lane board); whether the roadmap's existing Now blocks migrate in a sweep or rot away as lanes close.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"stem-strippers-twins","parent":"infra","ord":"aT","title":"Two functions strip an outline filename's extension with opposite rules — unify them #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T16:00:22-04:00","desc":"Found by PR #177 (2026-08-15), pre-existing: message.ts:148 and dates.ts:387 both strip an outline's suffix, with opposite stated arguments (spell the suffix vs find it). Unifying them needs its own argument. Related micro-fact from the same sweep: node.ts:253's isArchived allocates a string per call on a per-file-per-probe path.","changed":"2026-08-17T16:00:23-04:00","custom":{"from":"177","pr":"227"}}
{"id":"tree-sweep-fixture","parent":"infra","ord":"aU","title":"Three tests each walk the whole repo tree their own way — share one walker when a fourth appears #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T16:00:24-04:00","desc":"Counted by PR #177 (2026-08-15).\n\n- acp/manifest.test.ts:76, the claims sweeps, and now tests/extension.test.ts each walk the whole tracked tree their own way.\n- **Rule** (the author's own): a shared fixture is the right move at four, not three — this node exists so the fourth sweep triggers it instead of becoming the fourth spelling.\n- **Also owed a human call**, recorded here rather than lost: docs/RCA/2026-08-11-roadmap-stamp-reverts.md:64 still names docs/roadmap.jsonl inside a dated, explicitly-unbuilt proposal — correct the path or let the dated document stand as written.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00","custom":{"from":"177","pr":"227"}}
{"id":"props-floor","parent":"node-properties","ord":"a0","title":"PR: properties, whole — the props map + migration, set_prop + search + drawer, created/changed stamps","done":"2026-08-15T17:46:07-04:00","desc":"RULED 2026-08-15 through three shapes, final.\n\n- Record unchanged + ONE open top-level key `custom` (string → text-or-list), no migration, top level closed and typo-refusing.\n- set_prop writes only custom.\n- Search: prop:key / prop:key=value.\n- Drawer with read-only system rows (id visible; zoomed always, tree rows once props exist — the human kept that at merge).\n- created/changed stamped flat, excluded from changesOf.\n- **MERGED** 2026-08-15 (the human's manual approval, the day's one reserved read): PR #179, admin-squashed at head 8d0f512e after the conflict merge with #188/#189/#190.\n  - Nix build was the sole gate at that head, a ONE-TIME exception on the human's explicit word (full odu CI stands for everything else).\n- **Journey's receipts:**\n  - Grok's same()-ignores-custom blocking fixed as a no-op guard (a same-value set_prop is a no-op everywhere).\n  - The ⌘Z double-removal on list values caught and fixed.\n  - The fresh double round found nothing further.\n- **Rulings at the gate:** drawer stays only-when-props on tree rows; hits-carry-custom filed as its own PR node.\n- **Evidence:** 1711 unit / 612 e2e / CI green at the reviewed head 5b1933e.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"doing-refuses-blocked","parent":"lane-cloning","ord":"a0","title":"PR: set_doing refuses on a blocked node — the DAG's law becomes a mechanism","done":"2026-08-15T14:22:10-04:00","desc":"Born from the 2026-08-15 incident (a rebase instructed while two reviewers still read the worktree).\n\n- set_doing on a node whose after-targets are unfinished refuses in words instead of allow-with-nudge.\n- **Asymmetry** deliberate and argued in code: only the STARTING verb refuses; set_done keeps its nudge; set_todo untouched.\n- **Deliberate non-gates** argued at plan.ts:876: set_after onto a started node records a true discovery; capture cannot arrive blocked (verified on the schema by review).\n- **Now** (2026-08-15): Kolu terminal `bf2dbd48` (Claude Opus), branch `doing-refuses-blocked`, PR #181.\n  - Built and verified: 1655 unit, 601 e2e.\n  - Stage #review — Grok posted NITS ONLY: pin the two non-gates with planner cases; the click-away note; capture-can't-arrive-blocked verified on the schema.\n  - Sharpest question: the relocated undo scenario — what undo does restoring doing onto a now-blocked node wants its own assertion.\n  - VIDEO EVIDENCE ordered by the human.\n  - **MERGE:** PRE-APPROVED — autonomous once findings addressed + CI green at final head.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"commit-op-staged-rename","parent":"bugs","ord":"aQ","title":"PR: pending and commit learn the index — a staged rename stops reading as a deletion","done":"2026-08-15T14:30:39-04:00","desc":"One hole, two faces, two live reproductions (2026-08-15): the pending/commit machinery reads the working tree against HEAD and never reads the INDEX, so hand-staged work — renames above all — is invisible or misclassified.\n\n- **MCP face** (orchestrator, fixing the docs/docs mint): with `git mv old new` staged, the commit op failed \"pathspec old did not match any files\" instead of committing the rename or refusing in its own words.\n- **WEB face** (the human's vault, post-.olai migration): `git mv`'d Archive.jsonl→Archive.olai and Tasks.jsonl→Tasks.olai staged.\n  - Commit panel showed \"Archive.jsonl deleted\" / \"Tasks.jsonl deleted\" — renames unread, the new .olai files invisible.\n  - Committing died with `fatal: pathspec '/home/srid/Vault/Archive.jsonl' did not match any files` — git's words surfaced raw because the sweep offered a path that exists only in HEAD.\n- **THE HUMAN'S CONSTRAINT**, binding on whoever takes this: REPRODUCE IN A TEST FIRST — a failing test holding a hand-staged rename against both the pending view and the commit path, before any fix lands.\n  - The fix reads the index (staged state) as part of pending, draws a rename as a rename, and never hands git a HEAD-only path.\n- **Related but separate:** create_outline minted docs/docs silently when handed the served root's own name — a refusal wanting a sentence (kept here so the two path-shaped stumbles travel together).","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:41-04:00"}
{"id":"external-links-newtab","parent":"bugs","ord":"aR","title":"An external link opens in a new tab","done":"2026-08-15T12:31:56-04:00","desc":"Filed and fixed 2026-08-15 the same afternoon (the ledger was frozen at filing time — this node is the after-the-fact record, the freeze's one debt).\n\n- **Bug:** an external link rendered in olai navigated the app tab away.\n- **MERGED** as PR #180 (squash, review WAIVED by the human, Grok 4.6 solo author — its first authoring lane here).\n  - Cross-origin http/https anchors gain target=_blank rel=noopener noreferrer at render time.\n  - /doc/ links, node navigation and anchors untouched, pinned in render.test.ts's own style.\n  - CI 9/9 required at fbf49eee.\n- **Grok-TUI quirk** recorded for future dispatches: a paste during boot needs a second Enter once the footer says send-now.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:42-04:00"}
{"id":"regressions","ord":"zzVVV","title":"Regressions","desc":"Behavior that shipped worse than what it replaced, each node naming the offending PR. Ruled into existence 2026-08-15 by the human during the first live one."}
{"id":"stdio-retires","parent":"regressions","ord":"a0","title":"PR: the stdio MCP retires — agents dial the running server over HTTP","done":"2026-08-15T14:54:33-04:00","desc":"RATIFIED 2026-08-15 after the bridge regression's root-cause conversation: one brain, and the door to it is HTTP.\n\n- The `olai mcp` subcommand is DELETED; .mcp.json points at the running server's /mcp route (the user runs `just run`); the ACP chat keeps its self-server MCP unchanged.\n- **Rulings sealed at the door:**\n  - (a) LOOPBACK NEEDS NO TOKEN — requests from 127.0.0.1 skip auth on /mcp, the chat keeps its bearer tokens, same trust stdio had.\n  - (b) The #175 attach/unix-socket machinery goes WITH it — serveOverUnixSocket usage, the dial, OwnedSurfaceConnection wiring, dead code deleted not dormant (the kolu per-face-expose upstream work stays: the web face rides it).\n  - (c) Stable per-repo port so the .mcp.json URL holds — just run binds it.\n- Docs move with it: .mcp.json example, docs/running.md, the charter gains the precondition that unattended agent runs need the server up.\n- This PR obsoleted three nodes filed hours earlier (bridge-no-fallback, socket-litter, mcp-process-leak — all archived with their stories).\n- **ASSIGNED:** Grok, solo, review WAIVED by the human.\n- Fielded to the human at green — merging changes his own session config (.mcp.json → http) and his run habits, so the coordination note rides the fielding.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:42-04:00"}
{"id":"brain-lock","parent":"regressions","ord":"a1","title":"PR: the brain locks its directory — a second olai over the same vault is refused","done":"2026-08-15T16:23:56-04:00","desc":"RATIFIED 2026-08-15, the enforcement half of one-brain.\n\n- **MERGED** the same day (pre-approved on verified evidence): PR #186, packages/server/src/lock.ts.\n  - bun:ffi flock, zero dependencies — the lockfile-family libraries failed the human's own kill-9 requirement (their validity is file-existence plus a staleness window).\n  - Keyed on realpath, pid in the file as DIAGNOSIS only.\n- **Evidence:** the orchestrator verified the transcript by eye.\n  - Second olai refused, naming pid.\n  - Symlinked spelling refused identically.\n  - kill -9 left the lock file on disk and the next boot served anyway — validity is the kernel's.\n- **Review:** Grok + opencode, nothing blocking.\n  - The EINTR disagreement settled IN the docstring with both readings and a bounded retry.\n  - kimi's CodeQL HIGH fixed at the line (0o600).\n- The audit's prediction came true: e2e workers were four olai over one shared fixture vault — per-worker copies now, which also closed a stray-write-into-tracked-fixtures hole.\n- **OPEN FOR THE HUMAN**, reviewers split: LockUnavailable (cannot determine a holder) ships FAIL-CLOSED with no escape.\n  - kimi argued a narrow bypass for only that case (macOS is CI-unproven; a portability miss is a no-dial outage).\n  - grok argued a macOS miss should be a bugfix, not a knob.\n  - Both paths' tests already exist either way.\n- **Cosmetic residue:** the VaultInUse refusal prints inside a raw Effect stack trace rather than as one clean sentence.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:42-04:00"}
{"id":"pr-body-wrap","parent":"infra","ord":"aV","title":"PR: repo markdown unwraps — one line per paragraph, 80 columns stays for source comments","done":"2026-08-15T14:47:49-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15 from the human's root-cause exchange with a lane: agents hard-wrapped PR bodies at ~80 because the repo's own docs/*.md do — the habit inherits from the corpus.\n\n- **Fix** targets the SOURCE: unwrap the repo's markdown prose (README, docs/*.md, brainstorming, package READMEs) to one line per paragraph.\n  - Code blocks, tables, ASCII diagrams untouched, rendered output identical.\n  - Convention written in HACKING.md: markdown prose never hard-wraps; ~80 stays for source comments.\n- PR bodies themselves were explicitly scoped OUT (the human's correction mid-dispatch — the habit dies at the corpus, not by editing history).\n- **Now** (2026-08-15): Grok solo (terminal `3e7619c0`, branch `pr-bodies-unwrapped`), review WAIVED, fielded at green.\n  - A mid-dispatch scope correction was sent and acknowledged-by-conduct; the whitespace-shaped diff rebases trivially under whichever sibling lands second.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:42-04:00"}
{"id":"quote-safe-selectors","parent":"infra","ord":"aW","title":"PR: e2e steps should build their data- attribute selectors through one quote-safe helper #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T16:00:24-04:00","desc":"Filed at PR #182's close (2026-08-15), opencode's nit answered-not-fixed with the receipt on the record.\n\n- Solid sets dynamic attributes via setAttribute so the DOM is escaped by construction — this is a test-selector concern only.\n- data-from was the fourth instance of one house idiom (data-path, data-file, data-node-id).\n- Hardening only the newest made the suite inconsistent for zero coverage.\n- **Fix:** one quote-safe helper across every data- step in packages/tests/step_definitions/.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:42-04:00","custom":{"from":"182","pr":"227"}}
{"id":"chat-diff-wrap","parent":"bugs","ord":"aU","title":"PR: the chat's diffs wrap — no horizontal scrollbar in the panel","done":"2026-08-15T15:32:13-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15 by the human with a screenshot: an agent's file-edit diff in the ACP chat clipped long lines behind a horizontal scrollbar.\n\n- **MERGED** the same day (pre-approved on verified evidence): PR #185, squashed at 61f22f0.\n  - Content wraps inside the box (grid + the min-w-0 chain on Panel/Entry/ToolFrame/Transcript/DropTarget, overflow-x-hidden on the transcript, both halves credited).\n  - Gutter and +/- keep their column across wrapping add, remove and same rows, pinned with 700-character UNBROKEN tokens of each kind.\n- Grok authored; opencode sole reviewer per the human (nothing blocking, 3 nits fixed); CI 9/9 at head.\n- **Evidence:** the orchestrator verified the before/after by eye on laptop and phone before firing — the before shows the token escaping the box, the after wraps mid-token with the gutter intact.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:42-04:00"}
{"id":"html-preview","parent":"viewing","ord":"aX","title":"PR: .html joins the previewable types — through a registry future types register in once","done":"2026-08-15T17:46:07-04:00","desc":"Filed and dispatched 2026-08-15 (srid). FIELDED FOR HIS WORD the same day — PR #189, CI green at the post-Escape-fixes master merge.\n\n- The registry is real: a future type is one entry; suffix-outside sweeps red.\n- The sandbox held every fresh attack from both reviewers.\n- **Best fix from the nit round:** CSP asserted as a parsed DIRECTIVE-SET EQUALITY instead of substrings.\n  - The substring version would have waved `img-src data:` straight through — sabotage-proven by that very example.\n- sandbox=\"\" now carries its warning ON the attribute line, where a diff-only reader lives.\n- **AWAITING SRID** under his deferral rule; four deferrals posted in full on the PR:\n  - (1) no pictures in a .html — img-src 'none'; closing it means parsing foreign markup into /media rewrites, which is where a preview could start serving files nobody meant to serve.\n  - (2) every .html body resident for process lifetime, no cap — memory scales with vault content.\n  - (3) fixed 70dvh frame (sandboxed frames cannot report height).\n  - (4) .htm unclaimed, one line the day somebody has one.\n- **Two judgment calls flagged for his eye:** the kind is `hypertext` in source but \"page\" in the one user-facing sentence; write_document/doc stay .md-only.\n- Terminal `1ae9b6fc` rests until he rules.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:42-04:00"}
{"id":"html-images","parent":"viewing","ord":"aY","title":"PR: pictures inside a previewed .html — /media rewrites under the sealed frame's CSP","done":"2026-08-16T10:43:54-04:00","desc":"Deferral from PR #189 (2026-08-15): the sealed frame ships img-src 'none', so a saved page's pictures do not draw.\n\n- Closing it means parsing foreign markup to rewrite src into /media/… — exactly where a preview could become a way of serving files nobody meant to serve.\n- The rewrite must be allowlist-shaped: vault-relative only, no traversal, no remote fetch.\n- Security review non-negotiable when taken.\n- **Receipt:** docs/format.md:120, sealed.ts:44.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:42-04:00","custom":{"pr":"201"}}
{"id":"html-memory","parent":"infra","ord":"aX","title":"PR: .html bodies stop living whole in the set — big pages want lazy bodies or a cap","done":"2026-08-16T12:55:44-04:00","desc":"Deferral from PR #189 (2026-08-15).\n\n- Every .html body is held in the loaded set for the process lifetime (ops/codec.ts:44, format/set.ts:53).\n- Saved pages are megabytes with assets inlined — resident memory scales with vault content, no eviction, no cap.\n- Named in docs/format.md:122.\n- **Fix direction:** bodies loaded on read (the snapshot-scale precedent — documents already stopped riding the first frame once) or a size-gated claim that refuses in words.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"204"}}
{"id":"html-frame-height","parent":"viewing","ord":"aZ","title":"PR: the sealed frame sizes to its page — 70dvh stops being a guess #techdebt","done":"2026-08-16T08:43:21-04:00","desc":"Deferral from PR #189 (2026-08-15): a script-less sandboxed frame cannot report content height, so Hypertext.tsx fixed it at 70dvh.\n\n- **RESOLVED** by PR #197.\n- The old rule here — \"the empty sandbox attribute is not negotiable\" — is AMENDED by the human's ruling (2026-08-16, \"accepted and approved\").\n  - The frame runs sandbox=\"allow-scripts\" with allow-same-origin forbidden by name and by e2e test.\n  - Execution sealed to one hash-pinned measuring script under default-src 'none'.\n  - A load-count gate re-seals the frame if a previewed page navigates it away (grok's review found that delta; it is closed and probe-tested).\n- **Not negotiable now:** allow-same-origin never joins the token list.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"197"}}
{"id":"hits-carry-custom","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a8","title":"PR: search hits carry custom properties — the lane board becomes one query","done":"2026-08-15T20:19:52-04:00","desc":"Ruled 2026-08-15 at PR #179's merge gate: hits do NOT carry custom yet (read_node does); this node is the future PR.\n\n- **What it buys:** \"every lane with pr=X\" / \"every node with source=Y\" as one search_nodes call — the orchestration board's native query.\n- **Shape:** hits gain a custom field the way they carry see/after.\n- **Open:** the wire cost of big values wants a look — hits are many, values can be long — truncate or key-only?","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","pr":"192","terminal":"48b46d55-9779-4fe7-b206-b89fe61fe87d"}}
{"id":"suite-load-flakes","parent":"bugs","ord":"aV","title":"Under load, the e2e suite drops 1–3 unrelated scenarios — never the same twice #e2e","done":"2026-08-15T23:47:22-04:00","desc":"Named independently by three lanes and two reviewers on 2026-08-15 (props, one-Site, caret, html-preview runs all saw it).\n\n- A full or tag-filtered suite on a box hosting other worktrees' servers intermittently fails 1–3 UNRELATED scenarios: inbox capture, a date pill, server restart, palette, edge editing, ⌘Z pair.\n- 15s timeouts, always green in isolation and on re-run, never twice on the same scenario.\n- Not any PR's diff — parallel workers vs machine load.\n- Distinct from the FIXED Escape flake (#190, a real bug).\n- **Hunt:** starts with worker-count vs load instrumentation; the fix may be as dull as backoff on the 15s step timeout under load — but measured, per the house law.","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"199"}}
{"id":"chat-speaker-discern","parent":"bugs","ord":"aW","title":"PR: the human's chat messages are hard to tell from the agent's","done":"2026-08-15T18:38:28-04:00","desc":"Reported by the human 2026-08-15 with a screenshot (kept at /tmp/olai-dispatch/chat-discern-before.png).\n\n- In the web chat panel, the human's own messages (\"scrim?\", \"I confirm Esc does dismiss…\") render nearly identically to the agent's.\n- A faint box is the only cue, and it does not read as a speaker change.\n- **Fix:** visual differentiation of the human's messages in the chat transcript.\n- Dispatched to grok as AUTHOR at the human's explicit instruction, with no reviewer lane — a deliberate exception to agents.olai's reviewer-only contract for grok.\n- The PR must include before/after visual evidence (screenshots), per the human's dispatch order.","created":"2026-08-15T18:00:51-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"agent":"grok","pr":"191"}}
{"id":"chat-steer-on-send","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"a9","title":"PR: chat sends immediately — mid-turn messages steer the agent, the queue dies","done":"2026-08-15T20:30:07-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15 from a live freeze.\n\n- The orchestrator spawned a babysitter subagent; the ACP adapter holds a turn's settlement open while a spawned subagent lives (claude-agent-acp `turnAwaitingSubagents`/`Turn.deferredSettle`).\n- olai's queue-until-idle branch (`packages/chat/src/chat.ts` send(): `if (turn !== null) { queue.push(prompt) }`) sat on 4 user messages for the turn's whole lifetime.\n- Cancel ran `dropQueue(\"cancelled\")` and destroyed them.\n  - No copy anywhere: the transcript is not persisted, the agent session is the persistence, and a queued message never reached the session.\n- **THE FIX**, learned from how Zed's composer never locks: send the prompt immediately, always.\n  - The adapter already supports a prompt arriving mid-turn — it STEERS: the message is injected into the running turn (`steeredSettle`, the pre-emption lanes) — so a user can talk to the agent while a subagent holds the turn.\n  - The queue and its drop are DELETED, not patched.\n- **CANCEL SEMANTICS** fall out: with steer-on-send everything typed was already delivered, so cancel means stop-the-agent and nothing else.\n  - For a residual undelivered message (steer in flight at cancel), keep the row marked unsent with a resend affordance — the panel never silently destroys user words.","created":"2026-08-15T18:37:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","pr":"194","terminal":"333bf4f1-ed35-48ed-8d27-de46102f1b88"}}
{"id":"chat-subagent-lanes","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"aA","title":"PR: subagent activity renders as its own lane in the chat panel","done":"2026-08-15T20:19:53-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15, the human's ask from the freeze incident (it was one of the 4 dropped queued messages, resurrected).\n\n- In-session subagent activity renders flat and unattributed — a tool call made by a spawned subagent looks exactly like the main agent's own, so subagents are invisible-yet-leaking.\n- The ACP adapter already tags subagent traffic with `_meta.claudeCode.parentToolUseId` (claude-agent-acp, `liveBackgroundTasks`); olai drops the meta on the floor between `packages/chat/src/agent.ts` and the panel.\n- **Fix:** group/attribute subagent tool frames under the Agent call that spawned them.","created":"2026-08-15T18:37:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","pr":"193","terminal":"a5cb10bc-f92d-4659-a02d-c2c2fbb2f9bf"}}
{"id":"instructions-reconcile","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"aB","title":"Update instructions.md to match how we now work #human","todo":true,"desc":"The instructions were written before the orchestrator/ folder existed (2026-08-15). Some sections now say things we no longer do. Each child below is one edit to make.","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-15T19:06:48-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-now-section","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a0","title":"Replace the \"Now\" section — done, two small fixes left","done":"2026-08-15T19:03:40-04:00","desc":"Done: the section now points at lanes.olai.\n\n- **Leftover 1:** it says lane entries are \"mirrors\" — they aren't; each lane is a real copy of the template, and the `item` property links it back to the roadmap.\n- **Leftover 2:** the deleted paragraph \"prose is not a ledger\" (anything worth tracking must be a node, not a sentence) was a good general rule — consider moving it to the Planning section instead of losing it.","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-pipeline-prose","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a1","title":"The step-by-step PR process is written twice — keep it only in dag.olai","todo":true,"desc":"The sections \"Implementation guidelines\", \"Reviewing the PR\" and \"When human approves a PR\" describe the same pipeline that dag.olai now defines as nodes.\n\n- **Shorten** them to: \"the pipeline is the dag-pr template; a dispatched task walks it in lanes.olai\".\n- **Keep only what nodes can't hold:**\n  - How to upload screenshots/videos as evidence.\n  - The footnote about checking CI properly.\n  - Merging approved PRs in an order that avoids conflicts.\n  - Killing the terminal as a separate step after merge.","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-babysit-split","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a2","title":"The watching instructions are wrong for the chat agent — split them","todo":true,"desc":"The doc says: watch every terminal with a background shell loop. Two problems.\n\n- (1) An earlier ruling says the waits should be kolu MCP tool calls, not shell commands.\n- (2) The chat agent must never watch at all: on 2026-08-15 it spawned a helper agent to watch grok, and the chat froze for the whole wait — a chat turn cannot end while a helper it spawned is still running.\n- **Fix:** the doc needs two sets of rules — a terminal orchestrator watches with MCP waits; the chat agent just dispatches and answers when poked.\n- Both become unnecessary once olai itself watches the terminals (the olai-subscribes item).","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-ops-only-rule","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a3","title":"Outline files were hand-written once — ruled: always use the MCP tools","done":"2026-08-15T19:06:07-04:00","desc":"The doc says outlines are only ever written through olai's MCP tools. I broke that: lanes.olai and dag.olai started as hand-written files.\n\n- **Ruled:** no exceptions.\n- dag.olai was deleted and recreated properly through the tools.\n- lanes.olai stays as-is — it was hand-born but every edit since went through the tools, and recreating it would have disturbed lanes mid-work.\n- **Also seen:** a brand-new file isn't noticed by the server until touched, and a deleted one lingers briefly — the first is a real (small) bug.","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-agent-menu","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a4","title":"When asking which agent to use, list them from agents.olai","todo":true,"desc":"The doc hardcodes example names (\"eg: Grok, Codex\"). Instead, the choices should come from agents.olai: nodes with role=author for who writes, role=reviewer for who reviews. Then adding an agent is one node, not a doc edit.","created":"2026-08-15T18:47:08-04:00","changed":"2026-08-15T19:07:11-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-watcher-idle-safe","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a5","title":"The watch command returns instantly on an idle terminal — fix the recipe","todo":true,"desc":"Found live 2026-08-15.\n\n- `kolu debrief` in a loop works while the agent is busy.\n- On an agent already sitting idle it returns the same screen immediately — loop it and it spins forever.\n- **Fix for idle terminals:** first `kolu wait <id> --until working` (the agent started doing something), then the debrief loop.\n- The doc's watching section should give both shapes.","created":"2026-08-15T18:56:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-merge-master-rule","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a6","title":"When to merge master into a PR: \"always, just in case\" or \"only when needed\"?","todo":true,"desc":"Ruled 2026-08-15: never rebase a PR; merge master into it instead (faster). One thing left to pick: instructions.md says merge master before CI \"just in case\" (always), but CLAUDE.md says only when the PR has conflicts or CI needs newer code. The dag-pr template currently follows CLAUDE.md (only when needed). Make the two docs agree.","created":"2026-08-15T19:00:32-04:00","changed":"2026-08-15T19:07:17-04:00"}
{"id":"prop-value-bound","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"aC","title":"PR: property values get a size limit","todo":true,"desc":"Ruled at PR #192's gate (2026-08-15): nothing stops a huge value being stored in a property. The PR argued ops/src/plan.ts is where a write-side bound belongs; nothing has hit this yet. Filed so it isn't folklore.","created":"2026-08-15T20:18:18-04:00"}
{"id":"search-props-ui","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"aD","title":"PR: search results show properties, and say when a property is why a hit came back — with an e2e test","done":"2026-08-15T21:35:10-04:00","desc":"Ruled at PR #192's gate (2026-08-15): three of that PR's leftovers fold into ONE follow-up PR, done by the same agent.\n\n- (1) The web app's search results still draw only title and place — a person can't see the properties the wire now carries.\n- (2) A hit found by prop:agent=X can't say a property is why it matched — growing `matched` an arm changes what that field means, and this PR must rule that design point.\n- (3) With something finally on screen, the e2e scenario that #192 rightly skipped becomes writable.","created":"2026-08-15T20:18:21-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","pr":"195","terminal":"48b46d55-9779-4fe7-b206-b89fe61fe87d"}}
{"id":"chat-subagent-asks","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"aE","title":"PR: a subagent's permission form names who is asking","done":"2026-08-19T10:57:20-04:00","desc":"Ruled at PR #193's gate (2026-08-15): when a subagent triggers a permission question, the form is drawn in the main column and reads as the main agent's.\n\n- The adapter already stamps parentToolUseId on session/request_permission and on a subagent's AskUserQuestion elicitation — ChatEntry.parent is tool-only and transcript.ask is never handed it.\n- **Grok's sharpening**, recorded: the unattributed row also breaks the lane stretch, so the lane re-opens and names itself again (visible, not silent).\n- The plumbing exists; recorded in packages/chat/README.md and docs/architecture.md.","created":"2026-08-15T20:18:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"#255 merged 0fa068bb"}}
{"id":"unsent-discriminate","parent":"orchestrator-in-chat","ord":"aF","title":"PR: an unsent message says timed-out vs refused — AgentGone learns the difference","done":"2026-08-18T10:06:53-04:00","desc":"Ruled at PR #194's gate (2026-08-15): a message marked unsent after a steer timeout cannot be told apart from one refused by a dead agent.\n\n- The timeout arm is an inference; today only the honest comment at the site says so.\n- **Real fix:** discriminates answered-from-unanswered inside AgentGone so a timeout routes like a dead turn (notice, no resend button) while a refusal keeps its button.\n- Redesigns ask, a shared primitive with five call sites — a real project, which is why #194 rightly deferred it.","created":"2026-08-15T20:18:27-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00"}
{"id":"siblings-of-quadratic","parent":"model-indices","ord":"Zz","title":"Slice 1: the index shape — byFile, mirrorsOf, edgesTo in Derived; every scan becomes a lookup #techdebt","done":"2026-08-16T12:30:00-04:00","desc":"Ruled 2026-08-16: docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md commits to direction C — patch the in-memory view when a file changes instead of rebuilding it three times per edit (the emanote shape).\n\n- C lands in four shippable slices; this node is slice 1: give `Derived` real indexes.\n  - `byFile` (file → its nodes), killing every by-file scan: `siblingsOf`, `nodesOf`, the trash page, the per-candidate loops.\n  - Plus the reverse maps the later patcher needs: `mirrorsOf` (target → mirrors resolving to it); `edgesTo` (target → sources whose after/blocks edges land on it).\n  - Built in the same single pass as today's tables, with every scan site converted to index reads.\n  - Still full-rebuild-per-edit at this slice.\n- Slices 2–4 (one computation per edit; the patcher with its oracle property test; patches on the wire) become their own roadmap items when the human says dispatch.\n- **Library scan concluded:** hand-rolled Maps, no dependency — d2ts/TanStack DB are the ideas' productized form but the wrong bite.\n- Grok's #198 warning about a \"blind\" shared grouping helper is answered by putting the grouping inside `Derived`, always paired with its revision.","created":"2026-08-15T21:31:01-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"205"}}
{"id":"ir-evidence-recipe-reach","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a7","title":"Workers can't see the evidence-upload recipe — it lives in the orchestrator's file","todo":true,"desc":"Found live 2026-08-15 (night shift): PR #195's screenshots landed on catbox.moe because the GitHub-CDN upload recipe is written in docs/orchestrator/instructions.md — a file worker agents never read.\n\n- Either the recipe moves to where workers look (HACKING.md or CLAUDE.md), or every dispatch briefing that asks for screenshots must carry the recipe inline.\n- Until ruled, the orchestrator includes it in briefings.","created":"2026-08-15T21:33:15-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00"}
{"id":"viewport-helper-promotion","parent":"infra","ord":"aZ","title":"viewport() joins OlaiWorld — nine step files spell it inline #techdebt","done":"2026-08-16T09:17:25-04:00","desc":"Filed from PR #197's deferral (2026-08-15): the e2e world's own convention says a helper belongs on OlaiWorld once three or four features ask; nine step files spell viewport() inline. Converting them was six files outside #197's diff. Mechanical.","created":"2026-08-15T21:43:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-16T09:17:26-04:00","custom":{"pr":"200"}}
{"id":"drawnorsaid-extra-frame","parent":"infra","ord":"aa","title":"drawnOrSaid waits one extra frame on the happy path — grok's #199 follow-up #techdebt","done":"2026-08-16T09:17:27-04:00","desc":"Filed from grok's #199 review (2026-08-16): the one follow-up it would take — an extra frame on drawnOrSaid's happy path so the pointer and the keys agree about when the tab has the way back. Small, e2e-harness precision.","created":"2026-08-15T23:47:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-16T09:17:27-04:00","custom":{"pr":"200"}}
{"id":"client-draw-crash","parent":"bugs","ord":"aX","title":"The web page crashes while drawing: \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'remove')\"","done":"2026-08-16T11:07:05-04:00","desc":"Seen 2026-08-16, mid-chat, on the production build (myolai.rooster-blues.ts.net). The whole page dies to the \"This page broke\" screen.\n\n- **Window:** the human says it started in the last ~24 hours of PRs — #192 through #200.\n  - Of those, #192 hits-carry-custom, #195 search-props-ui and #197 html-frame-height touched client drawing; #200 was tests-only.\n- The throw is inside the UI framework's own list-reconciliation code, not olai's (frames `qf`/`ft`/`rn` in the minified bundle; `dev.js` in dev).\n- \"reading 'remove'\" during reconciliation usually means the framework tried to take a DOM node out of a list it no longer holds — the classic causes are two rows sharing a key, or a keyed list being mutated while it draws.\n- **Stack** (prod bundle main-hesa85kj.js):\n\n```\nTypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'remove')\n    at qf (main-hesa85kj.js:1:22637)\n    at ft (main-hesa85kj.js:2:3293)\n    at Object.fn (main-hesa85kj.js:2:3019)\n    at rn (main-hesa85kj.js:1:7545)\n    at y (main-hesa85kj.js:1:7326)\n    at U (main-hesa85kj.js:1:1596)\n    at ft (main-hesa85kj.js:2:3011)\n    at Object.fn (main-hesa85kj.js:1:25143)\n    at rn (main-hesa85kj.js:1:7545)\n    at y (main-hesa85kj.js:1:7326)\n```\n\n- Not yet reproduced on demand.\n- **Next:** a fix PR should first find a reproduction (what was on screen: the chat page, while messages streamed), then bisect the #192–#200 window if the reproduction doesn't point straight at the cause.","created":"2026-08-16T09:33:17-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"202"}}
{"id":"html-preview-relative-links","parent":"bugs","ord":"aY","title":"HTML preview: clicking a relative link to another .html doc does not navigate there #deferral","done":"2026-08-16T17:55:15-04:00","desc":"RULED by the human at #206's gate (2026-08-16), with the example that settles it: folder A holds foo.html and bar.html; foo links to bar; clicking that link must open **bar.html in Olai**.\n\n- The app navigates to bar's own page (URL, sidebar selection, everything) — the same place clicking bar.html in the sidebar lands.\n- What #206 shipped is NOT this: the click swaps the bytes inside the preview frame (the sibling renders sealed, in-frame) while Olai's own page still says foo.html.\n- That in-frame behavior was #206's honest scope; this node is the remaining distance.\n- **Shape of the fix:** the frame's navigation (or a click intercept) tells the host page which vault file it moved to, and the host navigates the app to that document.\n  - Likely a postMessage from the injected prefix script, or intercepting same-vault link clicks before the frame navigates.\n  - Must stay inside the seal's rules: only same-vault .html targets get this treatment; everything else keeps #206's behavior.\n- Needs the e2e scenario the original filing asked for: click a relative link, assert Olai's own page is now bar.html's.\n- **Original filing, for history:** follow-up to #201, whose base made relative links 404 under /media/ — #206 then made them render in-frame; ruled insufficient.","created":"2026-08-16T09:35:51-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"from":"201","pr":"209"}}
{"id":"noderefs-duplicate-target-crash","parent":"bugs","ord":"aZ","title":"NodeRefs: a repeated see/after target crashes the page the same way #202 fixed","done":"2026-08-16T12:05:05-04:00","desc":"Found by #202's author while hunting client-draw-crash, deliberately left out of that PR.\n\n- NodeRefs.tsx draws see/after links with `<Key each={props.refs} by=\"id\">` — but an id names the *target*, not the row.\n- A hand-edited .olai repeating a target (`\"see\":[\"x\",\"x\",\"x\"]`), opened at /n/&lt;node&gt;, dies with the identical reconciler stack on the next store frame.\n- Verified against a real server.\n- **RULED** by the human, 2026-08-16: draw ONE — deduplicate at the read.\n  - Matches the write layer's set semantics (a re-add is a silent no-op in plan.ts): a repeated target means one link.\n  - Fix: a dedupe where the refs are read, keeping `by=\"id\"` honest.\n  - Plus its own scenario: a hand-edited duplicate target draws one pill and the page survives.\n- Reproduction and both options are written on PR #202.","created":"2026-08-16T10:21:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:02:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"203"}}
{"id":"seal-base-uri","parent":"viewing","ord":"aa","title":"Seal hardening: decide whether base-uri joins form-action #techdebt","done":"2026-08-16T14:40:15-04:00","desc":"Answered by #206, found while sweeping deferrals 2026-08-16: the preview rebuild added base-uri 'none' to the network policy — needed once the seal stopped winning by tree order — which is exactly the second bar this node asked to be decided. Originally #201's deferral 1.","created":"2026-08-16T10:35:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-16T14:40:21-04:00","custom":{"pr":"206"}}
{"id":"preview-pictures-coverage-gaps","parent":"viewing","ord":"ab","title":"Preview pictures: the named test-coverage gaps #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T16:00:26-04:00","desc":"#201's own report names these gaps; both reviewers ruled them bounded and correctly deferred. Filed here so they're tracked rather than left in prose.\n- No e2e for `srcset`, `<picture><source>`, or CSS `background: url()` — they work by consequence of the shared base; only unit-level agreement is asserted.\n- A `loading=\"lazy\"` picture arriving after load keeps its pre-load height (clamped by CSS) — named in the seal's comment, untested.\n- No component-level unit test for the two-readings height logic (this client has no harness for Hypertext.tsx) — covered by the held-picture e2e and its negative control.\n- **Not included here:** the relative-links cost — that's its own bug, `html-preview-relative-links`.","created":"2026-08-16T10:35:15-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"201","pr":"227"}}
{"id":"ir-closing-keywords","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a8","title":"Orchestrator commit messages must not spell GitHub's closing keywords","todo":true,"desc":"Learned 2026-08-16 the hard way.\n- **INCIDENT:** the board commit \"grok closes #202's review pair\" landed on master; GitHub read `closes #202` as a closing keyword and auto-closed the PR mid-lane.\n  - Not merged — the author caught it, verified nothing was on master, and reopened it.\n- **Lesson:** any lane can lose its PR to a sentence.\n- **Rule to add to instructions.md:** in commits the orchestrator pushes to the default branch, never put \"close/closes/closed/fix/fixes/fixed/resolve/resolves/resolved\" directly before a PR/issue number.\n  - Write \"grok finishes #202's review pair\" — or put the number first.","created":"2026-08-16T10:48:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00"}
{"id":"model-indices","parent":"infra","ord":"ab","title":"Model indices: patch the view, don't rebuild it (direction C)","desc":"**Plan of record, ruled 2026-08-16:** docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md.\n- Four shippable slices, in order — each a PR with its own evidence.\n- **End state:**\n  - One small edit costs what it touched, not three whole-corpus rebuilds.\n  - The patcher speaks Surface's own collection-delta frame.\n  - from-scratch `derive()` stays as the oracle a property test holds the patcher to.","created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00"}
{"id":"model-indices-2","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a0","title":"Slice 2: compute the view once per edit — validate's Derived flows through to publish","done":"2026-08-16T15:51:51-04:00","desc":"Thread the validated view through to the publish step instead of recomputing it over the whole corpus (today's second rebuild). Old direction B, now C's plumbing. Open question 4 of the doc (serving derived facts through Surface's derived.collection reconciler) is a later refinement, not this slice.","after":["siblings-of-quadratic"],"created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-16T15:51:56-04:00","custom":{"pr":"208"}}
{"id":"model-indices-3","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a1","title":"Slice 3: the patcher — patch(derived, delta) in format/, held to the derive() oracle","done":"2026-08-17T08:45:18-04:00","desc":"One function beside `derive()` in format/, consuming Surface's collection-delta frame (`{upserts, removes}`).\n- Local updates: byFile, children keys owned by the file, byId with duplicate-claimant promotion.\n- A dirty set from the reverse indexes (mirrorsOf, edgesTo) recomputes only touched status/blocked entries.\n- Cycle checks re-run only when edges/mirrors changed.\n- **Copy-on-write:** a patch returns a NEW Derived, sharing untouched maps.\n- **Safety line:** the oracle property test — `patch(derive(before), delta)` deep-equals `derive(after)` over generated edit sequences, duplicate ids on purpose.\n  - The patcher may bail to full `derive()` on hairy cases.\n- Server uses it; the browser still rebuilds in this slice.","after":["model-indices-2"],"created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr":"211"}}
{"id":"model-indices-4","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a2","title":"Slice 4: the browser joins — the derived memo folds delta frames through the same patcher","done":"2026-08-17T12:06:05-04:00","desc":"- Swap `web/src/client/outlines.ts`'s derived memo from flatten-and-derive() to the patcher, over the delta frames the outlines collection already delivers.\n- **No wire change** — outlines-as-collection already paid that cost.\n- State the mixed per-entry revs contract explicitly in the patcher's contract (same as today, not new unsoundness).\n- If the generic fold-a-collection combinator proves itself olai-free here, offer it upstream to kolu Surface as a small PR (the precompress-upstream route) — a consequence of the design, not a prerequisite.","after":["model-indices-3"],"created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr":"223"}}
{"id":"chat-model-reverts-on-restart","parent":"bugs","ord":"aa","title":"Chat: /model choice does not survive an olai restart — the session comes back on sonnet","done":"2026-08-16T22:52:24-04:00","desc":"Reported 2026-08-16: switch the chat to fable with /model, restart olai (new deploy), and the restored chat runs sonnet again.\n\n**ROOT CAUSE — CONFIRMED 2026-08-16.**\n- The deploy container's `~/.claude/settings.json` holds `\"model\": \"sonnet\"` (the human read it out).\n- The pinned adapter (0.66.0, `dist/acp-agent.js` ~5470-5530) picks the model on session/load by priority: (1) `ANTHROPIC_MODEL` env, (2) settings.model, (3) the resumed transcript's live model, (4) default.\n- For a RESUMED session it deliberately RE-ASSERTS an env/settings pin with `query.setModel` (\"a resumed session lands on the transcript's model regardless of env/settings, so the override must be re-asserted\").\n- `/model` is handled inside the wrapped CLI, so the change lives only in the transcript — which the pin then clobbers on every restart.\n\n**IMMEDIATE REMEDY (no code):** delete the `\"model\"` line from the container's `~/.claude/settings.json`.\n- `/model` choices then survive restarts via the transcript, and fresh sessions start on the adapter's default.\n\n**DURABLE FIX (if a settings pin should coexist with /model):**\n- olai remembers the session's chosen model itself and re-applies it after session/load through the model config option.\n- Or upstream: argue the transcript should outrank settings on resume.\n- **Floor either way:** `/model`'s change only becomes visible to olai one turn late (the next turn's init message), because nothing else on the wire carries it.","created":"2026-08-16T11:18:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr":"212"}}
{"id":"chat-subagent-live-face","parent":"bugs","ord":"ab","title":"Chat: a running subagent has no live face — lanes only fill as tool frames arrive","done":"2026-08-17T01:11:57-04:00","desc":"Reported 2026-08-16 with a screenshot: during a fan-out, the panel shows the Agent call as a plain pending dot plus a lane of already-arrived tool rows — nothing says a subagent is running RIGHT NOW.\n\n**It IS possible in ACP:**\n- The pinned adapter streams a subagent's tool calls live, stamped with `parentToolUseId` in `_meta.claudeCode` (exactly what #193's lanes draw), with pending/completed status riding each frame.\n- The e2e suite proves the lane draws them (`the_agent.feature` 82-100).\n\n**What's actually missing**, in the client (`chat/src/agent.ts` ~420-470 and the lane drawing):\n- The Agent frame itself gets no live treatment — a running Task shows the same \"·\" as anything pending: no spinner, no \"running · N calls so far\", no elapsed time.\n- A subagent's TEXT and THINKING are never drawn: `agent_message_chunk` is emitted as \"said\" with the parent meta ignored, so between tool calls a working subagent produces nothing visible.\n  - If the adapter forwards its narration, it would land in the MAIN agent's voice — check whether that interleaving is reachable; that would be its own defect.\n- A subagent spawned but with no first tool call yet has no lane at all — nothing to hang the lane on until a tool frame arrives.\n\n**Fix shape:**\n- Give the Agent frame a running state (derived from its own tool_call status plus the presence of parent-attributed frames since).\n- Decide whether a subagent's narration deserves a collapsed line in its lane (Claude Code's own UI shows \"N tool uses · last: ...\" — a compact live summary, not the full stream).","created":"2026-08-16T11:18:52-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr":"214"}}
{"id":"chat-at-completion","parent":"agents","ord":"aO","title":"Chat: typing @ completes file paths into the message","done":"2026-08-17T00:31:16-04:00","desc":"Requested 2026-08-16.\n- In the chat input, typing `@` should open a completion of the served directory's files (the same set the sidebar knows: outlines and documents), filtered as you type, inserting the path into the message — the way Claude Code's own `@` works in the terminal.\n- **Precedent:** the chat client already has a completion pattern to lean on — the editor's tag autocomplete (input-widgets).\n- **No new server surface needed:** the file list is already on the wire for free — the `outlines` collection's keys plus the `documents` collection's key set.\n- **Decide alongside:** whether a completed `@path` is plain text the agent reads, or carries the same attach semantics the `+` button has.","created":"2026-08-16T11:19:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr":"213"}}
{"id":"html-preview-scripts-dead","parent":"bugs","ord":"ac","title":"HTML preview: the page's own JavaScript does not run — ruled unacceptable; adopt kolu's iframe shape","done":"2026-08-16T13:58:26-04:00","desc":"**Ruled 2026-08-16 by the human:** a previewed .html whose scripts are dead is unacceptable.\n- Today this is by design — the seal (#189, hardened in #197/#201) inlines the document via `srcdoc` with a CSP whose `script-src` allows exactly one hash (the seal's own measure script), so the file's scripts are blocked on purpose.\n- **Overruled:** #189's \"not negotiable\" line — both #197 reviewers had already asked for it to be amended.\n\n**How kolu does it** (the reference, read 2026-08-16): `kolu/packages/solid-fileview/src/renderers/iframe.tsx`.\n- Renders an iframe with `src` pointing at a file-serving route and `sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"` (WITHOUT `allow-same-origin`) — the page's JS runs in an opaque origin: cannot read host cookies/localStorage, CORS-gated fetch from inside is blocked.\n- The route (`kolu/packages/server/src/iframePreviewRoute.ts` + `packages/serve-dir`) serves raw bytes with content-type, guarded per-segment against traversal on the UN-normalized request target.\n- A postMessage bridge is available via ref for host↔frame channels.\n- The sandbox is the boundary; CSP hash-pinning is not part of it.\n\n**The olai shape of that:**\n- Serve the .html body by URL (extend the `/media` route family or a sibling `/preview` route, traversal-guarded like #201's mediaTarget but not picture-only).\n- Switch the frame from `srcdoc` to `src`, keep `sandbox=\"allow-scripts\"` alone.\n\n**Open design points for the PR to argue:**\n- **Privacy promise** (\"a saved page cannot tell anybody else's server what you are reading\"): an opaque origin still loads remote no-cors embeds (img/script src).\n  - If the promise is to survive, the route can send a Content-Security-Policy HEADER permitting inline/own-origin scripts but no remote hosts — JS works, nothing leaves.\n  - If the human would rather drop the promise, that's a deferral to rule.\n- **Measure script** (two-readings height, #197/#201): srcdoc injection dies with srcdoc. Options: inject into the served bytes server-side, a postMessage bridge like kolu's, or read the frame's height another way.\n- **Relative links:** with a real URL base, a relative link navigates INSIDE the frame to the sibling file — this may fix `html-preview-relative-links` for free; say so with a scenario if it does.\n- **Docs:** format.md's seal story and #189's \"not negotiable\" sentence must be rewritten to the new rule.\n\n**Security review non-negotiable on the PR**, as with #197/#201.","created":"2026-08-16T11:22:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr":"206"}}
{"id":"just-e2e-node-leak","parent":"bugs","ord":"ad","title":"just e2e breaks before running a scenario: a system node leaks into the nix e2e shell","done":"2026-08-17T01:51:47-04:00","desc":"Found by #206's author, 2026-08-16, and reproduced on a clean checkout of master — not that PR's doing.\n- `just e2e` fails before a single scenario runs: a system `node` leaks into `nix develop .#e2e` and cannot type-strip @kolu/surface's TypeScript sources under node_modules.\n- **Workaround the author used:** run the suite through `bun ./node_modules/@cucumber/cucumber/bin/cucumber.js` directly.\n- CI's e2e leg is unaffected (green).\n- **Fix direction:** the e2e dev shell should pin/front its own node (or run cucumber under bun) so PATH's node never wins.","created":"2026-08-16T12:15:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr":"216"}}
{"id":"check-targets-index","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a3","title":"checkTargets still walks per node — convert to the reverse index without moving error order #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T02:04:15-04:00","desc":"**Resolved 2026-08-17 overnight:** the conversion turned out already done by #208 (slice 2), held behind three pins two of which fail on the walk.\n- PR #218 records it in model-indices.md with the measurement: walk 4.0ms vs index 0.40ms clean; 144ms vs 3.8ms with 200 unknown namings.\n  - didYouMean per-unknown-id (25 calls vs 200) is the larger factor.\n- **Honest close:** done by #208, measured by #218.","created":"2026-08-16T12:17:29-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"205","pr":"218"}}
{"id":"html-unreadable-refused-state","parent":"infra","ord":"ac","title":"A page olai cannot read should say so on the page, not only in the log #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"#204's deferral 1.\n- Under load-on-read, an unreadable .html (permissions, vanished mid-read) reports only to the server log — the reader sees the page with no body.\n- Telling them needs a `\"refused\"` state on DocumentEntry (a wire change with its own argument) and a face for it.\n- Still quieter than what it replaced, which failed the whole probe and bannered the whole directory.","created":"2026-08-16T12:49:32-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"204"}}
{"id":"watch-set-per-connection","parent":"infra","ord":"ad","title":"Bodies stay live by refcount, not a 16-slot guess — the wire learns when a reader leaves","done":"2026-08-17T20:41:08-04:00","desc":"**Reframed 2026-08-17** after reviewing kolu's watchers (was: \"per-connection LRU?\", #204's deferrals 3–5).\n- The 16-path set in `packages/server/src/bodies.ts` is not file-watching (the store already watches the whole directory) — it decides which OPEN pages get their bodies re-read when a revision touches them.\n- The bound exists only because the wire says when a reader OPENS a key and never says when the last one LEAVES (\"the framework owns subscription lifetime and does not publish it\" — bodies.ts).\n  - So eviction is a guess aged out of an LRU, and sixteen newer opens anywhere silence a still-visible page (stale, never wrong; reopen heals; documented in docs/format.md).\n\n**Kolu's honest shape** (`packages/integrations/io/src/refcounted-dir-watcher.ts`, `packages/integrations/git/src/working-tree-watcher.ts`): refcounted subscription per key.\n- First subscribe installs, every consumer shares, last unsubscribe tears down.\n- No cap, no LRU, no per-connection question, because the leave signal EXISTS.\n\n**The fix:**\n- Expose subscription lifetime on olai's wire (the \"keys-style member for who holds this key\" bodies.ts names as its own replacement), and refcount bodies on it — live for exactly the pages somebody has open, no magic number anywhere.\n- Both documented format.md edges (the silenced page; the birth-announce gap in published.ts) get revisited by the same change.\n- **Superseded:** the original per-connection-LRU idea — it would shrink the blast radius while keeping the guess.","created":"2026-08-16T12:49:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"204","pr":"229"}}
{"id":"done-over-open-work","parent":"bugs","ord":"ae","title":"A done parent must not be able to hide unfinished tasks — gate both doors","done":"2026-08-16T15:26:01-04:00","desc":"Ruled by the human 2026-08-16 after the model-indices slices vanished from the roadmap view.\n\n**Symptom:** the Infrastructure root stored `done`, and done-hiding — correctly, per its own rule that a parent's mark is a claim about the whole branch — hid everything under it, including the four freshly-filed model-indices slices.\n\n**Root cause** (traced through git):\n- Nobody marked it over open children.\n- PR #90 (\"Status is stored, never derived\", 2026-08-11 morning) ended derived parent status and, as its data migration, STAMPED the then-derived rollup into storage — that morning every child under Infrastructure happened to be done, so the derived \"done\" froze onto the root as a stored fact (`\"done\":\"2026-08-11\"`; f69d26d0 reformatted it to an instant the same afternoon).\n- Then five days of new open children accumulated under a root that silently carried done.\n- The mark was true when written and went stale by design: a stored fact over a growing branch, with no constraint at either write.\n- **Sweep of the other roots:** `editor` and `website` also store done but currently hide nothing; `infra`'s mark was cleared in a40583f3.\n\n**The ruling:** this must be a preventable constraint, not a nudge — the history shows one gate is not enough, since the state is reachable through two doors:\n- **set_done over open work**: marking a node done while its SUBTREE holds unfinished tasks (todo/doing — an unmarked bullet is not a task, per #90's own creed, and must not block) is REFUSED, naming the unfinished tasks — the same refusal shape set_doing already has for `after`.\n- **Open work arriving under a done ancestor** — the door this incident actually walked through: add_node with a todo/doing mark, set_todo/set_doing, or a move that lands an unfinished task under a done ancestor. Choose and argue: refuse it, or auto-undo the ancestor's done (louder and kinder to capture flows), but never let it land silently.\n- Web and MCP share the planner, so each gate is written once.\n- Archived subtrees stay exempt as everywhere else.\n- The nudge that set_done currently returns becomes the refusal's message body.","created":"2026-08-16T13:09:12-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr":"207"}}
{"id":"preview-body-not-shipped","parent":"viewing","ord":"ac","title":"A previewed page's body crosses the wire twice — the page only needs to know the file changed #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T03:57:34-04:00","desc":"#206's deferral 4, sharpened by its #204 merge.\n- To preview a .html, the page's subscription makes the server read and ship the whole body over the websocket — and then the frame fetches the same bytes again from the `/media` route, which is the copy actually drawn.\n- The websocket copy is only used to notice the file changed on disk.\n- **Fix:** a head/revision-only member on the documents collection (the page learns \"it changed\" without the bytes) — and #204's own client notes such a change should be measured, not guessed at.","created":"2026-08-16T13:46:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"206","pr":"219"}}
{"id":"preview-postload-growth","parent":"viewing","ord":"ad","title":"A previewed page that grows after loading never gets a taller frame #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"#206's deferral 5 — found by three refactor checks and confirmed by a verifier; predates #206, but running JavaScript is exactly what makes drawing late content common, so #206 makes it matter.\n- **Symptom:** a chart drawn from a fetch, a details element the reader opens, a late web font — the frame keeps its pre-growth height.\n- **Converged fix:** instead of rationing height reports per width, accept reports but REJECT THE ECHO — a report within a pixel or two of the frame's own current height is a vh-page feeding its container back; everything else is honest growth.\n- A behavior change wanting its own scenario.","created":"2026-08-16T13:46:29-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"206"}}
{"id":"chat-rewind","parent":"agents","ord":"aP","title":"Chat: no /rewind yet — the adapter has laid the plumbing but not shipped the verb","desc":"**Asked by the human 2026-08-16.** Investigated:\n- olai's chat has no rewind verb or UI.\n- The pinned adapter (claude-agent-acp 0.66.0) implements none either, but maintains a messageId→SDK-uuid map on every live and replayed message whose own comment says it exists \"so rewind/resume can translate a client-supplied id — Not read yet\" — upstream is preparing rewind but has not shipped it.\n- The CLI's own `/rewind` is an interactive terminal feature (the Esc-Esc checkpoint picker), not an SDK slash command, so nothing passes through the wire.\n\n**Two paths:**\n- **Wait** for the adapter to ship its rewind verb, then surface it in the chat (watch item — check on each adapter pin bump).\n- **Today:** offer \"branch this conversation\" via the adapter's `unstable_forkSession` (ACP `session/fork`) — a new chat continuing from the full current state, covering the try-a-different-direction half of rewind with zero upstream work.\n\nThe human has not asked for the branch button; it becomes a lane on their word.","created":"2026-08-16T14:03:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-create-placement","parent":"infra","ord":"ae","title":"Upstream: kolu's create-terminal endpoint should demand explicit placement — toplevel or child-of #upstream","done":"2026-08-16T21:20:12-04:00","desc":"**Proposed by the human 2026-08-16**, after the orchestrator drifted into spawning reviewers as top-level terminals when the charter said splits — the default absorbed the mistake silently, and the canvas's hierarchy (who works for whom) quietly flattened.\n\n**The design**, simplified on the human's challenge (\"what interactive CLI?\"): humans create terminals through the kolu web canvas, not the CLI — the CLI's real audience is scripts and agents, exactly the callers that drift.\n- No TTY carve-out, no default anywhere.\n- The padi create endpoint takes a REQUIRED placement — `toplevel | childOf(terminalId)`.\n- The CLI requires exactly one of `--toplevel` or `--parent <id>`, erroring otherwise.\n\n**Scope added by the human same day:** the rule also covers kolu's MCP surface.\n- The create-terminal tool `kolu mcp` offers agents takes the same required placement with no default, refusing a call that omits it — agents over MCP are exactly the script-shaped callers the rule exists for.\n- Migration is one word per script.\n\nA kolu PR, dispatched (lane `kolu-create-placement`).","created":"2026-08-16T14:15:53-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"2173"}}
{"id":"quiet-outline","parent":"viewing","ord":"ae","title":"PR: The Quiet Outline — titles first, notes behind a ¶, tags inline but quiet","done":"2026-08-16T17:21:00-04:00","desc":"**The decluttering proposal** the human commissioned 2026-08-16 (artifact \"The Quiet Outline\", rev 2), dispatched with its two rulings baked in:\n- Tags stay INLINE in the title Workflowy-style (quieted by contrast, never boxed, never moved to a column).\n- Nothing table-shaped anywhere.\n\n**Six moves, one PR:**\n- Notes fold behind a small ¶ per row, opened by click/space, with a view-wide density switch Compact/Cozy/Open (Open = today's always-shown behavior, kept).\n- The outline column caps near 80 characters, opened notes wrap near 62.\n- Tags render dim inline, brightening on hover/open; one hot fact may ride inline after the title (pr number on shipped work, fraction on a branch).\n- Top-level sections get a heavier name with the fraction beside it and stick while their branch scrolls.\n- One fixed-width glyph column — bullet, todo, doing, done — with doing the only accented glyph.\n- Done rows dim and a collapsed branch says \"+N done\" instead of hiding silently.\n\n**Open state** has exactly three inline layers:\n- Title line.\n- A properties run (key value pairs, dot-separated, one dim wrapping line — a byline, not a form).\n- The note.\n\n**Pipeline note:** this lane carries an extra #human gate — the human reviews the design (screenshots) after implement, BEFORE any reviewer agent is spawned.","created":"2026-08-16T14:22:55-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"210"}}
{"id":"ir-item-shape","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"a9","title":"Write into instructions.md: a roadmap item describes what to do (a PR), never a category","todo":true,"desc":"**The human's rule, 2026-08-16**, stated over the old \"Search & filter\" node: a bare category name marked todo is meaningless — every roadmap item's title should say what a PR would do.\n- Umbrella/category grouping belongs to parent bullets with no mark; work items are PR-shaped sentences.\n- **First application:** the search umbrella became \"PR: the search grammar's deferred half — …\".","created":"2026-08-16T14:32:58-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00"}
{"id":"search-relative-dates","parent":"search","ord":"a0","title":"PR: date: understands relative words — yesterday, last-week, this-month #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T02:24:41-04:00","desc":"Today date: takes only literal dates and ranges (2026-08, 2026-08-01..2026-08-14). Add the relative vocabulary — yesterday, last-week, this-month — resolved against the server's today, refused verbatim like every other bad operator value.","created":"2026-08-16T14:35:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-17T02:24:42-04:00","custom":{"from":"168","pr":"217"}}
{"id":"search-quoting-or","parent":"search","ord":"a1","title":"PR: quoted phrases and OR join the search grammar #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T03:37:12-04:00","desc":"Today every word is AND-ed and matched alone; \"exact phrase\" quoting and an OR between terms are the two compositions people reach for first. One grammar change, both faces, refused verbatim on bad input like the rest.","created":"2026-08-16T14:35:27-04:00","changed":"2026-08-17T03:37:12-04:00","custom":{"from":"168","pr":"220"}}
{"id":"search-is-blocked","parent":"search","ord":"a2","title":"PR: is:blocked finds what is waiting on something #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T01:31:31-04:00","desc":"The format already derives blockedness (Derived.blocked, drawn on every row) — the operator just reads it. is:blocked = the node is waiting on at least one unfinished task; -is:blocked composes like every operator.","created":"2026-08-16T14:35:29-04:00","changed":"2026-08-17T01:31:32-04:00","custom":{"from":"168","pr":"215"}}
{"id":"search-everywhere","parent":"search","ord":"a3","title":"PR: the day, agenda and trash pages honor the filter box like the outline pages do #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T05:17:24-04:00","desc":"Filter-in-place works on outline pages; the day page, the agenda, and the trash ignore the same box. Same grammar, same ancestors-kept behavior, one filter meaning everywhere.","created":"2026-08-16T14:35:35-04:00","changed":"2026-08-17T05:17:25-04:00","custom":{"from":"168","pr":"221"}}
{"id":"search-saved","parent":"search","ord":"a4","title":"PR: saved searches — name a query, get it back with one click #deferral","done":"2026-08-20T11:53:32-04:00","desc":"A named query the reader can re-run — where it is stored (client preference vs a node in the vault) is the one design question to argue in the PR; the vault-node answer would make saved searches shareable and agent-visible for free.\n- **The storage question was answered by Pins before this lane ran** (format.md §Pins): a pin is a node whose title is an address, and `?q=` on one is how a saved query is a pin at all — one click back, shareable (a file), agent-visible (add_node/move_node/trash_node).\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #282 (Opus, merged fae7a1446; grok + opencode do-not-object).** The missing slice was NAMING where the thought arrives: ⌘⇧P / ⌘K \"Pin this page\" on a page carrying `?q=` asks for a name in the palette's own box (placeholder = the derived name; Enter with nothing pins unnamed as before; Enter with words writes `[name](/…?q=…)` in ONE op; Escape writes nothing; the chord is dead while its own question stands). A shelf row's ✎ asks the same question and resolves to `set_title` — the op an agent sends. `@olai/format` gained `pinTitle` as `linkedTitle`'s inverse (one spelling on both sides of the wire; a `]` in a name is refused, a `(` in the address escaped); the `pin` verb gained an optional `name`; no new record shape, field or client store.\n- A bug the screenshot found and fixed: the shelf's `×` had never appeared on hover (group-hover sat on the `<Link>`, controls were its siblings).\n- The human used it on this vault during the lane: `[created today](/roadmap.olai?q=created%3Atoday)` is on the shelf.\n- Not this slice, by design: a pin's QUERY is not a search operator; no naming door on a node's ••• (a node's name is its live title); no shelf •••.","created":"2026-08-16T14:35:37-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T11:53:32-04:00","custom":{"from":"168"}}
{"id":"search-document-bodies","parent":"search","ord":"a5","title":"Document bodies are invisible to search — decide how the text inside .md and .html gets found #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"Surfaced by the human's 2026-08-16 question (\"what does search NOT search?\") — the biggest answer then: search covered a node's title, id, tags and note, and never the text inside a document file.\n\n**Reconciled 2026-08-19** (verified at e571aef5): **the .md half SHIPPED with #258.**\n- `fcd-pr2-face` claims this node closed, and for markdown it did.\n- Document bodies are in the search haystack (`format/src/filter.ts:2055,2194,2230`).\n- Ranked into one list beside node hits (`ops/src/query.ts:262-277`).\n- Answered by `search_nodes`, the palette, and the header box; pinned by `documents.feature:346,356`.\n- The MiniSearch-vs-rebuild-lazily question this node parked was overtaken by the fold/index work.\n\n**What keeps it open — the .html half:**\n- `filter.ts:2194` fills `body` only for `kind === \"document\"`; the set deliberately keeps a `.html` path WITHOUT its body (architecture.md: a saved page is megabytes nothing in the set reads; `ops/src/tools.ts:547` says so to agents).\n- \"Text inside .html gets found\" is not a missing feature yet — it needs a RULING first: either bless the doctrine (hypertext is opaque to search, close this node) or design an index that reads bodies search-time without re-inflating memory (#204's load-on-read constraint stands).\n- That ruling is the remaining scope; interacts with the parked semantic recall as before.","created":"2026-08-16T14:35:47-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-preview-packages","parent":"viewing","ord":"af","title":"Weigh adopting kolu's solid-browser and solid-fileview where they actually fit #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"**The human's question at #209** (2026-08-16), answered from the packages' own source (kolu/packages/solid-browser, solid-fileview).\n\n**What they are:**\n- solid-browser is a pure history controller — `createBrowser` over an opaque location type (back/forward stack, forward-truncation, reactive) — plus `resolveRelativePath` (GitHub-style relative-ref resolution, framework-free) and back/forward mouse-button wiring.\n- solid-fileview is a FileView dispatching to renderers: iframe (plain sandbox), image, markdown, pdf, video.\n\n**The assessment, piece by piece:**\n- **Do NOT** swap the preview onto fileview's IframeRenderer — olai's is deliberately MORE: the injected measure prefix (auto-height), the network-only CSP header, walk-off custody, and #209's link-to-app bridge. Adopting the plain renderer would be a downgrade.\n- `createBrowser` is UNNECESSARY under the ruled design: #209 routes link clicks into olai's own pages, so the real browser's history gives back/forward for free. Relevant only if an in-pane browse mode (navigating without moving the app) is ever wanted — which the human just ruled against.\n- `resolveRelativePath` IS worth adopting where olai resolves relative refs in rendered MARKDOWN prose (`client/markdown/rewrite.ts`) — one GitHub-rules resolver shared with kolu instead of a private spelling. Small, real.\n- fileview's image/pdf/video renderers are the honest opportunity: olai only gives faces to .md and .html today — a vault png/pdf/mp4 clicked in the sidebar has nowhere to go. If those types deserve pages, these renderers are the cheap way in.\n\n**So:** no wholesale adoption; two targeted candidates (the relative-ref resolver; the media renderers if media files get faces). Awaits the human's pick.","created":"2026-08-16T14:39:30-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00"}
{"id":"ir-deferral-tag","parent":"instructions-reconcile","ord":"aA","title":"Write into instructions.md: a deferral node wears #deferral and carries from=&lt;PR&gt; as a property","todo":true,"desc":"**The human's rule, 2026-08-16:** every roadmap node born as a PR's deferral is tagged `#deferral` in its title, with the deferring PR as the `from` property.\n- So `prop:from=168` lists one PR's leftovers and `#deferral` lists them all.\n- No note begins with \"Deferred on PR #N\" prose.\n- Applied across the open roadmap the same day (twelve nodes).\n- The sweep also found `seal-base-uri` already answered by #206 and closed it.","created":"2026-08-16T14:41:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00"}
{"id":"preview-links-deferrals","parent":"viewing","ord":"ag","title":"What #209 left open, each its own call","done":"2026-08-16T17:55:40-04:00","created":"2026-08-16T15:54:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-16T17:55:40-04:00"}
{"id":"preview-olai-links","parent":"preview-links-deferrals","ord":"a0","title":"A preview's link to a sibling .olai outline should open that outline in Olai #deferral","done":"2026-08-16T17:55:20-04:00","desc":"#209 claimed .html and .md siblings; an .olai link keeps #206's in-frame behavior because an outline is not a bodied kind — its page is /o/, its existence check a different list. A second route and membership question, same navigate-the-app shape as #209.","created":"2026-08-16T15:54:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-16T17:55:24-04:00","custom":{"pr":"209"}}
{"id":"doc-page-anchors","parent":"preview-links-deferrals","ord":"a1","title":"The document page cannot land on an anchor — so fragment links to siblings stay in-frame #deferral","done":"2026-08-16T17:55:24-04:00","desc":"bar.html#section stays the frame's click because /doc/ has no anchor support; #209 backs the kept behavior with a scenario. The honest fix is anchor support on the document page, then fragment links can carry.","created":"2026-08-16T15:54:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-16T17:55:29-04:00","custom":{"pr":"209"}}
{"id":"preview-open-channel-budget","parent":"preview-links-deferrals","ord":"a2","title":"The preview's open channel needs a budget — a page naming itself can spam history #deferral #human","done":"2026-08-16T17:55:34-04:00","desc":"Found by #209's refactor passes, confirmed by a verifier, deliberately not fixed.\n- `router.go` pushes a history entry and scrolls to top per message, unbounded.\n- A page naming itself never re-keys DocumentPage, so the frame survives to send again — the WALK_OFFS hazard class on a new channel.\n- **Three candidate rulings, each a behavior change:** refuse the self-open; a budget that outlives one mount; replace over push.\n- Needs the human's pick, then its own scenario.","created":"2026-08-16T15:54:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"from":"209","pr":"209"}}
{"id":"preview-dropped-click-silent","parent":"preview-links-deferrals","ord":"a3","title":"A dropped preview click tells the reader nothing #deferral","done":"2026-08-16T17:55:29-04:00","desc":"When the host refuses a posted path (not in membership — e.g. a .html under a pruned directory, servable yet unlistable), the click silently does nothing, against HACKING's never-silently-ignore rule. Surfacing it is a behavior change; the odd seam it rides has its own scenario in #209.","created":"2026-08-16T15:54:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-16T17:55:34-04:00","custom":{"pr":"209"}}
{"id":"kolu-watch-next-cli","parent":"infra","ord":"af","title":"Upstream: the ring — padi nags every settled terminal by default until it is worked, snoozed with a reason, or killed #upstream","done":"2026-08-19T10:57:20-04:00","desc":"**Rev 3** of docs/brainstorming/kolu-watch-cli.md — simplified on the human's ruling (rev 2's five-command watchdog was too much; we own both tools, no compat debt).\n\n**The whole design:**\n- **The ring**, default padi behavior — a terminal settled ≥60s is *ringing*, level-triggered, cleared only by work/death/snooze, so missed wakeups are structurally impossible.\n- **One verb:** `kolu snooze <id> --for 2h --reason \"…\"` — the only way to legitimize idleness, reason+expiry mandatory, expiry re-rings.\n- **One face:** `kolu ring --wait` — block until any terminal rings, print, exit; its exit is the orchestrator's wake.\n- Same state via the urgency resource for MCP (lingerIds already half-exists).\n\n**Deletes rev 2's:** subscriptions, ack cursors, expect/park, `--settled-ms`, screenTail-in-events — all of it was delivery machinery for a problem level-triggering doesn't have.","created":"2026-08-16T17:18:14-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"kolu #2181 merged by the human 2026-08-18; dogfooded live (snapshot/transition/nag all observed)"}}
{"id":"kolu-darwin-unit-fsevents","parent":"infra","ord":"aeV","title":"Upstream: darwin's unit lane is structurally red (git FSEvents churn tests), which silently skips every darwin daemon suite and blocks merges #upstream","done":"2026-08-17T00:40:26-04:00","desc":"**Surfaced by #2173's author and ruled DISPATCH by the human 2026-08-16.** Two coupled facts:\n- `ci::unit@aarch64-darwin` has 20+ consecutive reds on ci@petit from the git FSEvents churn tests (packages/integrations/), reproducing byte-identically on unmodified master.\n- `ci/mod.just` declares `daemon: install unit`, so while unit is red on darwin the daemon suites there are SKIPPED — darwin daemon coverage is not exercised at all, and the red required context forced #2173 to merge via `--admin`.\n- **Fix:** the churn tests for real if the failure mode allows (preferred), or skip them properly on darwin with the reasoning pinned — note PR #2172's branch already skips two of them darwin-only, so reconcile rather than collide.\n- **Success** = darwin unit green on master, daemon suites running on darwin again.","created":"2026-08-16T21:21:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"2176"}}
{"id":"slice4-path-order-landmine","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a4","title":"Slice 4 must pick one path order — assemble's plain string compare vs the client's segment-wise sortByPath disagree on where an arriving file goes #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"**Recorded by the slice-3 author (PR #211):** the patcher places an arriving file by assemble's plain string path compare, while the web client's `sortByPath` sorts segment by segment.\n- The two already disagree today — not new unsoundness.\n- But slice 4 (the browser folding delta frames through the same patcher) has to pick one ordering, or the patched browser view will disagree with the assembled one.\n- Filed on the human's overnight draft ruling (\"file roadmap entries for those three\").","created":"2026-08-16T23:15:14-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"from":"211"}}
{"id":"patch-bench-harness","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a5","title":"Commit the 1,000-file patch-vs-rebuild benchmark as a just leg so the order-of-magnitude figure is reproducible #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T22:38:02-04:00","desc":"Open question 5 of docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md.\n- The slice-3 author measured 2–3ms patched vs 25–40ms rebuilt on a 1,000-file / 21,000-record vault as a one-off.\n- The harness is not in the tree, so README/architecture.md deliberately call it an unreproducible laptop sample.\n- **Fix:** commit the harness with a `just` leg.\n- From PR #211; filed on the human's overnight draft ruling.","created":"2026-08-16T23:15:17-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"from":"211"}}
{"id":"patch-byid-overlay","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a6","title":"Replace the patcher's new Map(byId) clone — roughly half of every patch — with an overlay or persistent map #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T22:38:02-04:00","desc":"Open question 1 of docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md, now answered with a measurement by the slice-3 author: the byId clone is the dominant remaining cost (~half a patch). The lever is an overlay map or a persistent structure — take it when a bigger vault asks. From PR #211; filed on the human's overnight draft ruling.","created":"2026-08-16T23:15:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-17T22:38:02-04:00","custom":{"from":"211"}}
{"id":"agenda-shows-trashed","parent":"bugs","ord":"af","title":"Agenda shows trashed nodes — archived dated work keeps its place on a page about what is owed","done":"2026-08-17T15:18:51-04:00","desc":"**Reported by the human 2026-08-17; RULED same day:** archived (trashed) nodes appear ONLY on the trash page — stripped from the agenda, day pages, and every other page.\n- This reverses the three-archived-doors doctrine #221 documented (trash, day, agenda): trash becomes the sole door.\n- **The fix must sweep:** agendaOf's keep and the \"archive keeps its place\" test (inverted, renamed); day-page collection; #221's Scope.archived (collapses to the trash page alone — the filter exception simplifies); docs/search.md and format README prose.\n- `is:archived` in search remains the explicit way to reach archived nodes from anywhere.\n- Dispatched to Opus.","created":"2026-08-17T08:51:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"226"}}
{"id":"second-pane","parent":"infra","ord":"ag","title":"The Second Pane — split views: N panes, each a full page, the layout in the URL","done":"2026-08-17T17:56:34-04:00","desc":"Proposed in the artifact \"The Second Pane\" (claude.ai/code/artifact/980a4438-9c7f-4e1b-b5b7-18a647c6b379), researched against Workflowy's native panes and the MultiFlow extension.\n\n**Principles:**\n- A pane is a route (page + zoom + filter) rendering the full page component — no second-class panes.\n- Focus is explicit with a visible ring and all shortcuts/palette/filter acting on it.\n- Links deterministic (click = this pane, mod-click = open right).\n- The whole layout serializes into the URL (share/restore/back-forward).\n- Drag between panes native (one store, no frames).\n- Saved layouts are outline nodes.\n\nDispatched to grok 2026-08-17 on the human's word — draft PR, NO agent reviewers, the human reviews by running the branch.","created":"2026-08-17T10:39:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"225"}}
{"id":"olai-batch-verbs","parent":"infra","ord":"ah","title":"MCP writes stop costing one round-trip per fact — add_node children carry the whole record, a batch apply runs many ops in one atomic write, and update writes several fields of one node","done":"2026-08-17T12:39:00-04:00","desc":"From the 2026-08-17 orchestration retrospective: a lane spawn cost ~13 olai MCP calls (1 add_node + 9 set_after + 3 set_prop) because each fact is its own round-trip — and the agent's turn latency, not the server, is the cost.\n\n**One PR, three verbs:**\n- `add_node`'s child shape gains `after`, `see`, and `props` so a captured subtree arrives with its edges and facts in the same atomic write.\n- `apply` — a list of ops executed in order, one validation, one write, one rev, all-or-nothing with the failing op named.\n- `update {id, mark?, desc?, props?, after?}` for the done+sha+note trio.\n\n- Every refusal the single verbs make (shadowed keys, unknown ids with closest match, cycles named, done-over-unfinished from #207), the batch forms must make identically.\n- **Ruled:** auto-merge on clean evidence.","created":"2026-08-17T10:44:55-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"224"}}
{"id":"kolu-one-shot-submit","parent":"infra","ord":"ai","title":"Upstream: dispatching a message to an agent terminal becomes one call — sendInput grows submit, and create grows message #upstream","todo":true,"desc":"**PR #2177 CLOSED UNMERGED by the human's ruling 2026-08-18** after three rounds of live field testing (full reason on the PR): the core premise — output-quiet means prompt-ready — is false in the field.\n- Round 1 lost a brief to a boot race.\n- Round 2's recognition fix was circular (recognition is downstream of the first message).\n- Round 3 fixed claude via foreground-process identity, but grok still starved both one-shot paths — its idle TUI repaints on a ~0.8–1.5s cadence, so the 1500ms default settle never holds (settleMs:800 submits instantly; the manual trio works).\n\n**Post-mortem for the successor:**\n- Keep the mid-turn refusal semantics, the 30s wire-pinned bound, the readiness-proof structure, and the commandName/adapter recognition work (branch `one-shot-submit` preserved).\n- Replace the quiet-conjunct with a signal that is agent-state-shaped — the adapter already knows idle; padi should ask it, not the byte stream.\n- **Related:** `kolu-watch-next-cli` (PR #2181 in flight) encodes the same lesson for supervision.","created":"2026-08-17T10:44:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00"}
{"id":"faithful-addresses","parent":"infra","ord":"aj","title":"The address system is not faithful to the directory — a file's URL should be its path, and special pages should be marked as special #needs-brainstorm #human","todo":true,"desc":"Raised by the human 2026-08-17 while designing saved layouts, and parked for its own brainstorm before any dispatch.\n\n**The complaint:** `/o/notes.olai` and `/doc/docs/x.md` invent structure the disk does not have — the file lives at `notes.olai`, so the address should be `/notes.olai`.\n- routes.ts convicts itself: it refuses a `/html/` prefix on the grounds that \"the suffix is what fileKind reads, and it is in the address either way\" — a prefix would be \"the same fact spelled twice, free to disagree with the name it carries\".\n- But `/o/` vs `/doc/` is that same duplication, since `.olai` vs `.md` already says which kind of page it is.\n\n**The human's sketch:** file paths ARE the addresses (`/notes.olai`), and special/computed pages wear a marker that cannot collide with a filename — something like `/:today`, `/:agenda`, `/:trash`.\n- Wanted done properly, as a SYSTEM, from the hickey/lowy standpoint rather than patched address by address.\n- **Hickey:** is the address complecting \"which file\" with \"which kind of page\" and \"which view of it\"?\n- **Lowy:** what volatility does the address layer encapsulate, and would its interface survive the axis it claims to own changing (new page kinds, new view parameters, nesting)?\n\n**Two obstacles a design must answer explicitly:**\n- **Collision:** once file paths sit at the root, a file named `agenda` collides with the view. Hence the human's `:` marker (or another reserved shape) — decide it, don't leave it implicit.\n- **The node permalink:** `/n/<id>` deliberately spells ONLY an id, because ids survive renames and moves across files; a faithful `/notes.olai?id=hinge-notes` re-introduces a file that can disagree with reality after a move.\n  - Either the file is a hint the resolver repairs, or the id stays canonical with the path decorative, or something better. This is the real tension, not a detail.\n\n**Downstream:** saved layouts (and anything else that stores a route) must not be built until this is settled, or they bake in the current spelling.\n- Also: #225 landed the pane-list address (the workspace URL) on top of the current scheme, so a change here touches that bijection and its tests.","created":"2026-08-17T18:02:56-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00"}
{"id":"chat-at-nodes","parent":"infra","ord":"ak","title":"Chat: typing @ completes NODES too, not just file paths — hand the agent a task by name","done":"2026-08-17T21:09:49-04:00","desc":"Chosen by the human 2026-08-17 as the next feature.\n- PR #213 gave the chat composer @-completion over FILE paths (server's own prune + kind registry, WeakMap fold, eight rows, tagOpensAt reused so @person habit does not collide).\n- **This is the other half:** the same @ also completes NODES — type `@hinge` and pick the node, so you can say \"look at @pick the hinges\" instead of pasting a path and hoping the agent finds the row.\n- Reuses the completion machinery just built rather than inventing a second one.","created":"2026-08-17T18:05:22-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"pr":"228"}}
{"id":"mentions-index-one-sigil","parent":"infra","ord":"al","title":"The mention index files only @ — one taggedBy would also free the tag completion from walking the corpus #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-18T21:55:00-04:00","desc":"Filed at PR #237 by the altitude pass; SHIPPED in PR #249.\n\n- **Problem:** mentionedBy filed the @ namespace and dropped the sigil, but the fold it rode (titleParts) already yielded #topic parts and threw them away — so the index was HALF a reverse index of tags written in prose.\n- **Fix:** one taggedBy keyed by the WRITTEN form (@herbs and #herbs are two keys), re-keyed in one change across derive.ts, patch.ts's taggings(), the oracle's readable() and backlinksOf; mayHoldSigil went with it.\n- web/src/client/complete/tags.ts now reads the index instead of scanning every node of the corpus per derivation.\n- **Measured** (the deferral's condition): two new `just bench` legs print both halves.\n  - Completion: 18.5ms walked vs 0.47ms read (12.2ms for the title-only walk that was already there, answering 60 tags against the index's 1,052).\n  - Corpus-wide fold: 6.5ms filing @ alone vs 18.6ms filing both sigils.\n  - End to end, interleaved across two worktrees: a rebuild goes 32.8ms → 46.7ms, a one-file patch 0.67ms → 0.85ms, against ~18ms saved on every derivation while a tag is being typed.\n- **Verdict:** yes, with the cost stated — the saving is per keystroke, the cost is per cold rebuild.\n- **Bonus:** WIDENED the completion — a tag written in a note is now offered, and the count is one vote per record rather than per occurrence.","created":"2026-08-18T06:05:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"237"}}
{"id":"patch-refile-fifth-spelling","parent":"infra","ord":"am","title":"patch.ts spells re-file-a-reverse-index five times — extract it when a sixth index appears #techdebt #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"Counted at PR #237 by the reuse pass.\n\n- **Pattern:** containment, namings, mentions, orderings and blockage each walk the same five steps.\n  - Copy the before-map.\n  - Build arriving.\n  - Gather the keys the edit could have moved from arriving + outgoing.\n  - Per key, take the survivors (filtered by TOUCHED FILE, not by record) plus the arrivals in a promised order.\n  - Drop the key if it ends empty rather than storing an empty list.\n- **#237** added the third of those and designed the extraction rather than skipping it.\n- A generic `refiled<T>` needs the entry `Located` projected back out (the indexes hold different entry shapes), then has to hand back three things: the rewritten map, the keys that VANISHED, and whether a first-namer MOVED.\n- Only `namings` asks for the last two, because only `namedBy` promises key order — two axes behind one contract, with the caller paying for neither unless needed.\n- **Rule invoked:** the repo's existing author rule — a shared fixture is the right move at four occurrences, not three — says the SIXTH index is what should force the extraction.\n- **Why this node exists:** so the sixth becomes the trigger, rather than becoming the sixth silent copy.\n- **Status:** the invariants are re-argued per index today; `patch.test.ts`'s oracle is the only thing holding the copies in step.","created":"2026-08-18T06:05:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"237"}}
{"id":"editor-verbs-2026-08-17","parent":"editor","ord":"aA","title":"Editor: three verbs the keyboard still lacks","done":"2026-08-19T11:02:12-04:00","created":"2026-08-17T21:27:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T11:02:12-04:00"}
{"id":"move-to-picker","parent":"editor-verbs-2026-08-17","ord":"a0","title":"Move-to picker: fuzzy-search a new parent anywhere, from the keyboard","done":"2026-08-19T10:57:19-04:00","desc":"Approved overnight 2026-08-17.\n\n- **Feature:** a keyboard dialog (Workflowy's ctrl-shift-M) — invoke on the current node, fuzzy-search every node across all outlines as a destination, Enter moves the node (with its subtree) under the chosen parent.\n- **Reuse:** the search machinery; the move is the existing move op.\n- **Cross-file moves:** refuse with a clear message if the op layer cannot express them (outlines are independent trees — archiving is what crosses files).\n- Say so in the dialog rather than hiding the limit.","created":"2026-08-17T21:27:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"pr":"#245 merged 7d6706c1a"}}
{"id":"duplicate-subtree","parent":"editor-verbs-2026-08-17","ord":"a1","title":"Duplicate subtree: copy a node and everything under it in one action","done":"2026-08-18T10:06:54-04:00","desc":"Approved overnight 2026-08-17. One keyboard/menu action clones the current node and its whole subtree as a sibling below (fresh ids throughout, marks preserved or reset? — the author decides and documents; Workflowy preserves). Mirrors under the copied subtree: copy the placement, not the identity. For templates and repeated structures.","created":"2026-08-17T21:27:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-18T10:06:54-04:00"}
{"id":"recurring-dates","parent":"editor-verbs-2026-08-17","ord":"a2","title":"Recurring dates: a repeat rule on dated nodes — done spawns the next occurrence","done":"2026-08-18T10:06:54-04:00","desc":"Approved overnight 2026-08-17.\n\n- **Feature:** a dated node gains an optional repeat rule (every day / week on Mon / month / year) — keep the grammar small and spelled in the file.\n- **Completing it:** stamps done AND creates the next occurrence at the next date (a fresh node, so the journal keeps the honest history of each completion).\n- Agenda and daily pages show the next occurrence like any dated node.\n- Web editing of the rule beside the date; MCP parity in the same PR.","created":"2026-08-17T21:27:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00"}
{"id":"viewing-2026-08-17","parent":"viewing","ord":"ah","title":"Viewing: the graph's missing reverse face, and panes learn to hand off","created":"2026-08-17T21:27:09-04:00"}
{"id":"backlinks","parent":"viewing-2026-08-17","ord":"a0","title":"Backlinks: a zoomed node shows what references it","done":"2026-08-18T05:20:00-04:00","desc":"Approved overnight 2026-08-17; SHIPPED in PR #237.\n\n- **Feature:** zoom into a node and see a \"referenced by\" section — every node whose see-edge points here, plus every node whose title/note mentions this node by its `@<id>` spelling (#228).\n- **Implementation:** the reverse index is one new table in the derivation, `mentionedBy`, keyed by the WORD a title or note writes after an `@` rather than by a node.\n  - This is what lets a mint or a delete cost nothing (existence is asked at the READ, `backlinks.ts`).\n  - See-edges needed no new index; `namedBy` already carried them.\n- Patched per changed file like the rest of the view, so the section follows the disk with nothing reloaded.\n- **RULED**, documented in docs/format.md's new References section:\n  - A mirror is NOT a reference (a placement is a view, not a claim — `read_node`'s mirrors already answers where a node is drawn).\n  - An after/blocks is not one either (the ordering graph, already drawn both ways on the page).\n  - An archived referrer is left out (#226).\n- Collapsed by default, each entry navigates, and `read_node` answers the identical reading as `referencedBy` so a person and an agent are told one thing about one id.","created":"2026-08-17T21:27:09-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"pr":"237"}}
{"id":"drag-across-panes","parent":"viewing-2026-08-17","ord":"a1","title":"Drag across panes: pick a node up in one pane, drop it in the other","done":"2026-08-18T09:30:00-04:00","desc":"Approved overnight 2026-08-17, SHIPPED in PR #238.\n\n- **Scope change:** with split panes merged (#225), a drag was still a fact about ONE page; it is now a fact about the WORKSPACE.\n- **Mechanism:** every editable page on screen joins a register as it mounts and leaves with itself (web/src/client/drag/fields.ts).\n  - A lift measures all of them; which pane the pointer is in is decided per move on X alone, because a split is columns (drag/aim.ts, unit-tested).\n- Over a page of the carried file, the arithmetic and affordance are the ones that already shipped — the same `planDrop`, the same drop line with the same `data-parent`/`data-after`/`data-depth` — drawn over whichever pane the pointer is in.\n- **SAME FILE IN BOTH PANES** reconciles for nothing: the write goes to the file and both trees redraw off the one store, so the row leaves one pane and arrives in the other on the same frame.\n- **DIFFERENT FILES is a REFUSAL raised at the AIM, not the write:** the pane fills with the reason before the hand lets go, and the same sentence lands on the selection bar after (drag/Refusal.tsx, one spelling carried on the aim).\n  - Sending the drop and quoting the ops layer would have been wrong twice: the line would have promised a landing the release could not keep.\n  - A drop at the other file's TOP LEVEL names `parent: null` — not a refusable request but a legal move to the top of the row's own file, landing silently in a pane nobody was pointing at.\n- **Two things a second pane broke** (rather than extended), both fixed here:\n  - A `Row.key` is a chain from the roots of ITS page, so `measureLines` now takes the page to read — both row gestures scope to their own pane (unscoped, a drag in the left pane was planned against the right pane's boxes).\n  - \"A branch is never offered a place inside itself\" is asked of the RECORDS in a row's chain plus the page's zoom ancestry, not the key's prefix — across two pages there is no shared path, and the branch a pane is zoomed into is not drawn there at all.\n- No new wire verb, no new op: a drop is still one `place` per row.\n- **Pinned by** features/drag_across_panes.feature (5 scenarios) plus drag/aim.test.ts; the in-pane suite is unchanged and green.\n- **Evidence:** two sections in packages/tests/evidence.ts.","created":"2026-08-17T21:27:09-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"pr":"238"}}
{"id":"agenda-spine","parent":"viewing","ord":"ai","title":"The agenda is a spine of time — now is a place on it, and the future recedes","done":"2026-08-18T11:52:08-04:00","desc":"Ruled by the human 2026-08-18, from a three-way design exploration.\n\n- **Decision:** the `/agenda` page redraws as ONE continuous spine of time — no OVERDUE/TODAY/UPCOMING section boxes.\n- **Why:**\n  - The flat sections gave every item equal claim on attention (an item 73 days out shouted as loudly as one due Monday).\n  - ISO dates demanded mental subtraction to feel urgency.\n  - The repeated chrome (file heading + crumb per day) outweighed content ~4:1.\n- **Spec:** the design canvas at https://claude.ai/code/artifact/3d13d467-18ed-49e2-8c95-64d9287683ef — opens on the chosen **B · Spine** artboard, drawn in the chalk palette with the app's real row anatomy.\n  - A \"Fog\" and C \"Horizon\" on the same canvas are the rejected alternates (A's distance-fade ramp is folded INTO B).\n\n- **The spine:**\n  - A 2px vertical line in the left gutter running the page's height, its ink a gradient down the flow of time — alarm above the today point, accent at it, then ink → muted → rule fading to transparent in the far future.\n  - Each listed day is a 7px dot on the line, the dot's ink fading with distance (ink, muted, rule); overdue days sit ABOVE the today dot with alarm dots.\n  - TODAY is an 11px accent dot with a paper ring, drawn even when nothing is due on it (muted italic \"nothing due today\") — now is a place on the line, not a section that vanishes.\n- **Days say felt distance, not just dates:**\n  - \"Mon, Aug 24\" + muted \"in 6 days\"; overdue \"Yesterday · Mon, Aug 17\" in alarm ink with the pill reading \"1 day late\"; today \"TODAY · Tue, Aug 18\" in small caps accent.\n  - Rounding is fine (19 days → \"in 3 weeks\"); roughly: under two weeks in days, then weeks, past ~2 months in months-and-halves.\n- **Gaps are content:**\n  - The stretch between consecutive listed days draws a small italic muted label beside the spine (\"two quiet weeks\", \"seven quiet weeks\").\n  - The vertical whitespace grows with the wait — log-ish, never linear, so a 52-day silence is visibly longer than a 2-day one without costing a screen.\n- **Rows fade with distance**: whole entries ramp ~1 → 0.78 → 0.74 → 0.5 opacity as they get further out.\n- **Chrome cut:**\n  - No per-day file heading (the \"Tasks.olai\" over every group goes).\n  - The ancestry trail is one muted line UNDER the row.\n  - The per-row date pill is dropped in the future half (the day label already says the date) and kept only where it adds a fact — the \"14:00\" time on a datetime.\n  - Overdue keeps DateBadge's alarm-tone semantics; occurrences still never amber, `done` still nowhere on the page.\n\n**Where the code goes, for whoever implements:**\n- **Date arithmetic lives in @olai/format** (packages/format/src/agenda.ts, beside `isOverdue`/`agendaOf` — the one place already allowed to compare dates): weekday + relative-label phrasing, and the gap sizing between days.\n  - `DateBadge.tsx` stays verbatim-printing and dumb; its header states the verbatim principle and this is its sanctioned extension — keep the parsing out of components.\n- **AgendaPage.tsx** loses its three `Section`s for the spine layout.\n  - `DayGroups.tsx`/`DayNode.tsx` are SHARED with the day pages, which keep their current reading — branch by surface or give the agenda its own entry renderer over the same `situate`d `DayEntry` data.\n- **Tones are tokens, never hex**: alarm/accent/ink/muted/rule via the theme custom properties (color-mix where a fade is needed) so all fifteen palettes follow.\n- **The scenario contract moves**: `data-section`/`agendaSection` testids disappear or change meaning — reshape packages/tests scenarios in the same PR; `data-overdue`, `data-date`, `data-occasion` keep carrying their facts.\n- **The filter keeps working** (`keepingOwed` narrowing): removed rows leave, gap labels recompute from the days still drawn.\n  - A filtered-empty page says the filter's sentence (never \"Nothing is due.\"), and the sidebar's unnarrowed owed count (`agenda/owed.ts`) is untouched.\n- **Empty agenda** still says \"Nothing is due.\" and draws no spine — a lone today-dot on an empty page was not ruled on; default to none.\n- **Keyed rendering rules hold**: the `Key by=\"date\"` / `by=\"file\"` reasoning documented in AgendaPage.tsx and DayGroups.tsx applies to whatever replaces them.","created":"2026-08-18T10:04:21-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00"}
{"id":"menu-said-overlay","parent":"bugs","ord":"ah","title":"MenuSaid still paints under sticky headings — the one overlay #233 left behind #deferral","done":"2026-08-19T20:47:22-04:00","desc":"The findings the human waived when ruling #233 merged without further review (claude reviewer's comment 5322681125, reproduced on the branch).\n\n- **(1)** menu/MenuSaid.tsx — the line carrying the ops layer's refusals — is still `absolute…LAYER.row` in the row, so a sticky section heading paints through it.\n  - The README's stacking table still names it a LAYER.row rider, contradicting overlay.ts's new doctrine.\n- **(2)** the completions half of #233 fixed a second real bug with NO test (fails on master, passes there) and hand-rolls measuring where `@kobalte/core/popper` (already a dep, already anchoring the menu) gives flip/shift/autoUpdate free.\n- **Smaller:** `host.parentElement` fails silently; no claims.test.ts sweep for the new layering rule.","created":"2026-08-18T10:07:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T20:47:22-04:00","custom":{"from":"233","pr":"#268 merged a6bd9970 — all three points closed (MenuSaid on overlay.ts, popper adoption, claims sweep)"}}
{"id":"filter-row-says-why","parent":"search","ord":"a6","title":"A filtered row says WHY it is drawn — highlight the hit, dim kept ancestors, excerpt a note-only match","done":"2026-08-19T10:57:19-04:00","desc":"Ruled with the human 2026-08-18, from one screenshot: a `#deferral` tag-click over roadmap.olai.\n\n- Every number and every row was CORRECT, and the page was still confusing, because a filtered page never says why any given row is in front of the reader.\n- **Three cases, all present in that one screenshot:**\n\n**1. A match does not show its needle.**\n- `ir-deferral-tag`'s title merely *talks about* the tag (\"a deferral node wears #deferral\") yet matched exactly like a row that wears it as a label.\n- The format cannot tell use from mention — a `#word` in a title IS a tag, deliberately — so the UI's job is not to distinguish them but to make the reason visible: show WHERE the query landed and the reader resolves the ambiguity themselves.\n\n**2. A kept ancestor looks like a match.**\n- `instructions-reconcile` (\"Update instructions.md to match how we now work\") carries no `#deferral` anywhere; it was drawn only as the ancestor chain leading to `ir-deferral-tag`.\n- Nothing marks it as context rather than result.\n\n**3. A note-only match shows no reason at all.**\n- A row whose hit lives behind the ¶ (matched on `desc`) draws a title containing nothing the query said.\n\n**THE FIX, three parts, all view-time (nothing is stored):**\n- **Highlight the matching substring in a matched row's title** — the classic search-needle treatment, applied to whichever title text (word, phrase, or tag pill) satisfied the query.\n- **Dim rows that are drawn but did not match** — kept ancestors.\n  - The distinction already exists in the model: membership in the `matched` id-set vs merely surviving `keeping`'s prune (`matchedIn` counts exactly this); the row just never draws it.\n- **For a row matched only in its note: draw a one-line excerpt** of the note around the hit, highlighted, under the title (or at minimum light up the ¶ itself).\n  - Explicitly NOT full auto-expansion of the note — ruled out because notes here run to ~1.5KB paragraphs (see `bun-watcher-bump`'s).\n  - The filter re-evaluates per keystroke, so full notes would reflow the page violently while typing, and it would trample the reader's own open/closed state, which would then need saving and restoring.\n  - A clamped excerpt is the same idea with bounded cost.\n\n**IMPLEMENTATION POINTERS (as of master f35af476):**\n- The matcher already knows which field carried a hit — `@olai/format`'s `filter.ts` scores per `SEARCH_FIELDS` (`title`/`id`/`tag`/`desc`) and `search_nodes` hits report `matched`.\n  - But the browser's filter path throws that away: `web/src/client/filter/narrowing.ts` reduces `matching(...)` to a `Set` of ids.\n  - The field (and the needle's position, or just the query's words for the row to re-find) has to ride along to the row — extend what `matching` hands back or derive per drawn row.\n- Title highlighting must hold on BOTH title paths, which are held to each other by test: the no-markdown fast path (`markdown/plain.ts` / `tags.ts`'s `taggedHtml`) and the HAST walk (`title.ts` / `styleTags`).\n  - `plain.test.ts` renders the same titles both ways; the highlight belongs under that same sweep.\n- Matching is case-folded substring over the folds in `filter.ts`'s `foldOf` — a tag is indexed bare AND as written — so highlight offsets must come from the same fold, not a fresh `indexOf` with different case rules.\n- The note excerpt can be plain text (escape, don't render markdown for one clipped line); `desc` is matched folded, so find the hit the same way.\n- The dim-vs-highlight styling wants the same narrowable-page condition tags already key on (`data-narrowable`, `styles.css`) so pages that take no filter change nothing.\n\n**Out of scope here**, filed separately if wanted: the count line's mixed denominators (\"8 of 57 — 17 more matches hidden as done\" reads as 8+17≠57; the 57 is page rows, the 17 is matches).","created":"2026-08-18T11:03:50-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"pr":"#240 merged 9ba1c6b5"}}
{"id":"md-live-preview-editor","parent":"editor","ord":"aB","title":"Markdown editing stops being a dumb text box — live-preview editing faithful to the bytes, autosave, vim mode in prefs","doing":true,"desc":"Ruled with the human 2026-08-18.\n\n- The note editor and the document editor are plain textareas today; they become rich markdown editors — WITHOUT betraying the format's one law, \"the text on disk stays verbatim\" (docs/editing.md, `markdown/render.ts`'s header).\n\n**THE FAITHFULNESS RULING, which decides the whole architecture:**\n- The markdown SOURCE stays the document model, and rich text is a *rendering layered onto it* — the Obsidian/Typora shape, where syntax markers (`**`, `#`, `[]()`) hide except around the caret and bold just looks bold until touched.\n- Editors that parse markdown into their own document model and serialize back (ProseMirror, TipTap, Lexical, Milkdown) are RULED OUT by name.\n  - A round-trip serializer normalizes bytes the user never touched (`_em_`→`*em*`, escapes, list reflow), and under autosave that churn lands on every pause.\n  - Result: phantom git diffs in the audit trail, spurious conflicts with concurrent agent edits, verbatim storage broken by construction.\n- With source-as-model there is no serializer, so fidelity is perfect by construction and needs no tests to hold it.\n\n**THE STACK, and the human's rule about cost:** dependencies are not cost; handrolled code is. The live-preview behavior itself comes from a package, not from decoration rules we write:\n- First choice: **`ink-mde`** — prebuilt CodeMirror 6 markdown editor with Obsidian-style live preview (marker-hiding, checkboxes, images), dark-appearance aware, written in Solid with a first-class `ink-mde/solid` component.\n  - Usage shape agreed:\n    ```tsx\n    <InkMde options={{ doc: node.desc, interface: { appearance: \"dark\", attribution: false }, hooks: { afterUpdate: (doc) => scheduleSave(doc) } }} />\n    ```\n- Fallback if ink-mde's rendering can't be lived with: raw `@codemirror/lang-markdown` + **`@retronav/ixora`** (à-la-carte CM6 live-preview extensions). Same document model either way, so switching later loses nothing.\n- Verify at implementation time how the chosen version accepts extra CM6 extensions (needed for the tag widget and vim below); the API detail is the implementer's, the intent is not.\n\n- **Our handrolled surface is glue only:** a CM6 widget for `#tag` pills that delegates boundaries to `@olai/format`'s `titleParts` (the editor and the view must agree on what a tag is, same rule `markdown/tags.ts` follows).\n  - Plus the autosave wiring, theming to match the panel, and the prefs toggle.\n\n**AUTOSAVE — no save button, no dirty flag:**\n- Debounced write on ~500ms idle plus a flush on blur.\n- Every write is CONDITIONAL — `was` set to the text this editor last saved — so a concurrent agent edit refuses in the ops layer's own words and surfaces as a `SaidLine`, never a silent clobber; the drift-said-before-refusal machinery `DocEditor.tsx` already has stays.\n- For documents this SUPERSEDES the standing ruling in `DocEditor.tsx`'s header (entered-by-verb, Save/Cancel, \"no idle commit\"): the human ruled autosave on 2026-08-18.\n- Its half-a-sentence concern is answered by the debounce being idle-keyed, and its OVERWRITE second verb survives as the door out of a refused write.\n- Rewrite that header to the new ruling rather than leaving the two to disagree.\n\n**Two surfaces, shipped incrementally in this order:**\n1. The NOTE editor (`edit/RowEditor.tsx`'s desc textarea — already commits on blur, so autosave is the smaller step there).\n2. The DOCUMENT editor (`document/DocEditor.tsx` — where the header rewrite above happens).\n- Incremental richness is fine: markers-hidden for bold/italic/headings first, tables and nested lists can lag.\n\n**VIM MODE, enabled in prefs:**\n- `@replit/codemirror-vim` as a CM6 extension, OFF by default, toggled by a stored preference following `layout/prefs.ts` / `preference.ts`'s `boolCodec` pattern (an `olai.editor.vim` key; surface the toggle wherever the done-preference lives in Prefs).\n- One key conflict to settle deliberately: inside a vim-enabled editor, Esc belongs to vim (mode switch), not to the app's dismiss chord — the registry in `keys.ts` is where that gets said, not an ad-hoc guard.","created":"2026-08-18T11:16:47-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"parked":"2026-08-18 by the human's ruling (\"unhappy with markdown editor, revisit in distant future\") — draft PR #241 holds the work, branch + both reviews preserved, ten evidence images on the attachments CDN"}}
{"id":"md-second-class","ord":"a4","title":"Markdown is the second format everywhere content is reasoned about — the .olai/.md parity table #needs-brainstorm","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-18 from the human's ask: sweep the repo and table where `.md` trails `.olai`.\n\n- Three sweeps (format/store/ops/server/git; web/surface/chat/acp; docs/website) agree: markdown is first-class exactly where a file is treated AS A FILE.\n  - That means: the kind registry (`format/src/kinds.ts:101-102`), load/watch/publish, sidebar + new-file affordance, the one shared render pipeline, daily notes, `/media/`.\n  - And second-class in layers that reason about CONTENT.\n- **Re-verified 2026-08-19 against HEAD e571aef5** (after #251 read tools, #253 palette rows, #256 addresses, #258 the face): four rows moved NO→PARTIAL, one flipped for a different reason, six held.\n\n| Capability | `.olai` | `.md` | Parity? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Search | full grammar over title/id/tags/note | body IS indexed now (`format/src/filter.ts:2055,2194,2230`; `ops/src/query.ts:262-277`) — one ranked list from `search_nodes`, the palette and the header box; but a document address still may not carry `?q=` (`web/src/client/routes.ts:519-523`, pinned `routes.test.ts:113`), and `.html` bodies stay invisible (the set keeps a hypertext path without its body) | PARTIAL — was NO |\n| MCP tools | 29 of 33 | 4 + search: `list_documents`, `read_document`, `create_document`, `write_document` (`ops/src/tools.ts:545,553,697,704`), `search_nodes` finds documents, and documents serve as MCP resources (`server/src/mcp/face.test.ts:283,300`); still excluded from `apply` (`ops/src/batch.test.ts:748`) | PARTIAL — was NO |\n| `node.doc` | declared (`node.ts:130`), validated, filterable (`has:doc`), copied by duplicate | writable by NOBODY (`CAPTURE`/`UpdateRequest` lack it, no `set_doc`), no read tool reports it (`Found` omits it, `reading.ts:94-158`) — and `node.ts:199` documents a capture door that does not exist | NO — broken in both directions, and the doc lies |\n| Identity & edges | every node an id; see/after/mirrors/backlinks | a document (and a heading in one) has an Address now (`format/src/address.ts:1-46`); a pin may be one (`tools.ts:507`); body `#tags` reach search (`document.ts:138,320`, `filter.ts:2187`) — but still not a `see`/`after` target (`writing.ts:851-866`), and `taggedBy`/tag-click backlinks stay node-only (`backlinks.ts:148,165`) | PARTIAL — was NO |\n| Links | node→doc renders inline (`DocRef.tsx`) | doc→doc rewrites in-pane (`markdown/rewrite.ts:167-178` + `router.tsx:274-292`); a doc page SHOWS backlinks (`document/Referrers.tsx` over `backlinks.ts:233`); residue: a bare `#id` in a body counts as a backlink (`documents.ts:494-497`) yet a click doesn't navigate (`documents.ts:123-127`) | PARTIAL — index and click disagree on `#id` |\n| Editing | full outliner: drafts, undo stack, tag completion | `textarea` in declared mode, no idle commit (`DocEditor.tsx:111-120`; drift banner `:100-110`); the live-preview fix is PARKED (draft #241), not in flight | NO |\n| ⌘K palette | node hits stream; `+` captures to Inbox | document rows as ordinary search hits (`Palette.tsx:266-281`, `palette/items.ts:214-226`); no create/capture row — ARGUED (outlines get none either, #253); `file/matching.ts` now serves only chat's `@` | PARTIAL — was NO |\n| Structure verbs | move/split/merge/duplicate + archive/inbox/trash | none — only `create-doc` and whole-text `doc` (`writing.ts:830,801`); `empty` names Archive.olai files only (the trash-olai lane is about to reshape this verb) | NO |\n| Git panel | node-level rows, verb-ful subjects | path + status letter (`committing.ts:172-198`); subject `olai: 1 file — x.md` (`message.ts:132-139`) | PARTIAL — surveyed, path-only, defended |\n| Chat | `@` completes doc paths; node ids pressable; nodes armable | doc paths in prose inert (`chat/refs.ts:38-45`); tool-frame paths unpressable though `.md` hunks draw as diffs (`ToolFrame.tsx:231-244`); not armable (`armed.ts:13-42`); a doc Wrote row has nothing to press (`surface/chat.ts:186-193`) | PARTIAL |\n| Daily-note minting | — | `docDay` web-only (`surface/edit.ts:853`, `server/edit.ts:242`, `Calendar.tsx:96`); MCP's `create_document` narrates the convention instead of owning it (`tools.ts:697-699`) | PARTIAL — web face only |\n| Tests | ≈1544 backend tests; `the_agent.feature` 82 | ≈79 md-titled tests (48 backend + 31 web); `store` 0 (kind-agnostic by design), `git` 0 titled but exercises `.md` paths (`git.test.ts:143-168`); features: `documents.feature` 29, `document_editing` 10, `daily_notes` 11, `markdown_arrives` 5, `html_previews` 41, `an_external_agent` 3 of 24 | PARTIAL — was NO |\n| Docs | — | face charter fixed (\"nodes and whole FILES, never bytes\", `mcp/face.ts:167-170`, pinned `mcp/tools.test.ts:415-421`); `docs/chat.md:89` names the four verbs; README still never says markdown (`README.md:1-27`) | PARTIAL — README is the last holdout |\n\n- **Where `.md` is AHEAD**, for fairness — all four still true, one wider: table of contents (`Toc.tsx`), heading anchors in URLs (`address.ts:14-16`), daily notes (a date-named `.md` IS the day), asset serving (now with `.html` subresources, `documents.ts:229-237`).\n\n**READING IT (2026-08-19):**\n- The structural root the 08-18 sweep named — no addressable identity below the file — is half-dissolved: #256/#258 gave documents addresses, search, palette rows and backlinks.\n- What remains is argued NOWHERE and still open: the unwritable/unreported `node.doc` (plus `node.ts:199`'s false sentence), documents as edge targets, structure verbs (move/rename/trash for a `.md`), chat armability and pressable doc references, and the README.\n- The brainstorm the tag asked for happened for the document arc (`brainstorming/first-class-documents.md`, ruled with the human 2026-08-19); the leftover rows above still need their own rulings before PR-shaped children split off.\n- The two open items it overlaps ride as see-edges.","see":["search-document-bodies","md-live-preview-editor"],"created":"2026-08-18T18:51:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"brainstorm":"brainstorming/first-class-documents.md — the hierarchy (Document ⊃ OutlineDocument/MarkdownDocument), the [document]#[element] address grammar, derived md face now, frontmatter later (ruled with the human 2026-08-19)"}}
{"id":"filter-count-honesty","parent":"search","ord":"a7","title":"PR: the count line says what the page holds, and what is hidden as done #deferral","done":"2026-08-18T00:00:00-04:00","desc":"The deferral `filter-row-says-why` filed, taken.\n\n- **Problem:** the count line's mixed denominators (\"8 of 57 — 17 more matches hidden as done\" read as 8+17≠57) — the 57 was page rows LEFT after the done preference, the 17 was matches it had taken away.\n- **Fix:** the line now says three truths, each only where it applies — how many rows MATCHED and are drawn, of how many the page HOLDS, and how many matched rows are NOT drawn and WHY.\n- The denominator moved from what the preference left (`visible()`) to what the page holds (`all()`), so every part is counted inside one set and a reader who adds them up is not lied to.\n- A part that is zero is not said; \"more\" is dropped when nothing is drawn — because `is:done` under a done-hiding reader draws nothing and \"no matches of 57 — 3 more matches hidden\" contradicts itself.\n- The wording is a function of three numbers (`web/src/client/filter/count.ts`) rather than a JSX binding, so it is unit-tested.\n- The numbers stay `narrowing.ts`'s, off the same three readings the page is drawn from, never a recount that could disagree with the prune it counts.\n- **Still deferred**, named on the PR: the ⌘K palette and the header box draw eight hits of however many matched and say nothing about the rest — `SearchAnswer.total` has been on the wire, uncounted, since the matcher was split out.","created":"2026-08-18T00:00:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00"}
{"id":"count-line-honesty","parent":"search","ord":"a8","title":"The count line says what the page holds, and what is hidden as done","done":"2026-08-19T10:57:56-04:00","desc":"Filed and shipped in one overnight lane (2026-08-19, run #3).\n\n- **Feature:** under a filter the count line now says all three truths — matched-of-held (\"2 of 10\", the denominator measured before the done preference takes rows off) plus \"— N more matches hidden as done (Prefs)\".\n- The wording is a pure function (web/src/client/filter/count.ts); the numbers come off the same sets the renderer draws from (filter/drawn.ts), never a recount.\n- **Findings round** made all 31 count-line assertions exact reads (a substring pin would have passed with a spurious hidden clause — both reviewers caught it independently, fix sabotage-proven).\n- **Deferral filed at merge:** the ⌘K palette and header search box draw at most 8 hits and say nothing about a ninth — SearchAnswer.total is on the wire and uncounted (see palette-count-cap).","created":"2026-08-19T10:57:56-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"overnight-3 (brief-born; captured retroactively)","pr":"#248 merged e419c67f"}}
{"id":"has-repeat-search","parent":"search","ord":"a9","title":"has:repeat joins the filter grammar","done":"2026-08-19T11:00:38-04:00","desc":"Shipped 2026-08-19 (overnight run #3).\n\n- **Feature:** one row in HAS_FIELDS (format/src/filter.ts) — parsed, taught in the refusal, evaluated, negated with the grammar's own dash — reaching all five doors through the single matcher, costing what `has:desc` costs.\n- Both reviewers do-not-object; grok's close: \"Ship it.\"\n- docs/search.md carries the row and the `has:date` containment note.","created":"2026-08-19T11:00:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"overnight-3 (brief-born; captured retroactively)","pr":"#252 merged a38b0640"}}
{"id":"empty-trash","parent":"viewing","ord":"aj","title":"Empty the trash — the one write in olai that deletes","done":"2026-08-19T11:00:42-04:00","desc":"Shipped 2026-08-19 (overnight run #3).\n\n- **Feature:** a new ops op `empty` naming EVERY archive the request empties in one op — the union holder-set holds by construction, list order means nothing.\n- A cross-pile cycle is not a special case (grok's objection, probe-verified, fixed at the root and withdrawn on re-verdict after he re-ran his own topology).\n- **Both faces in one change:** MCP `empty_trash` + the web's Empty trash verb, behind a confirmation counting over the SET and saying plainly that only git remembers.\n- Optional count-shaped `was` checked per planning attempt.\n- Refused while anything outside the Trash still names something in it.","created":"2026-08-19T11:00:42-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"overnight-3 (brief-born; captured retroactively)","pr":"#250 merged 557a268e"}}
{"id":"filter-highlight-cross-piece","parent":"search","ord":"aA","title":"A phrase across rendered markdown lights neither piece #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"The surviving half of #240's filter-highlight deferral.\n\n- **Closed half:** a needle inside a code span or link lit nothing — closed by #254 (a848677d): the highlight walk now enters those subtrees while the tag SPLIT stays off (NO_TAGS_IN).\n- **What remains:** a phrase spanning two rendered pieces of a title (across a **bold**, across a code-span boundary) selects the row but lights neither piece, because HAST text nodes carry no source offsets.\n- The fix is offset-preserving rendering — a different change.\n- #254 added a `not.toContain` pin so a later change cannot half-light it silently; docs/search.md names this as the one remaining corner.","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"#240, narrowed by #254"}}
{"id":"palette-count-cap","parent":"search","ord":"aB","title":"The palette and header search draw at most 8 hits and say nothing about a ninth #deferral","todo":true,"desc":"Filed at #248's merge (the count-line honesty PR).\n\n- The filtered page's count line now tells all three truths, but the ⌘K palette and the header search box still cap at 8 drawn hits with no denominator — `SearchAnswer.total` is already on the wire and uncounted.\n- Different surface, denominator and hider than the page's count line; also noted in docs/brainstorming/filter-in-place.md.","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:09-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"#248"}}
{"id":"parity-read-documents","parent":"md-second-class","ord":"a0","title":"MCP reads documents: list_documents + read_document","done":"2026-08-19T11:01:25-04:00","desc":"Closes the table's \"2 of 30 tools, no read, no list\" row's read half.\n\n- An agent can now list the documents the directory serves and read one whole.\n- A missing path refuses in the tools' own voice.\n- `face.ts`'s charter says the honest thing (\"nodes and whole documents, never bytes\") with a test pinning the retired \"no file access\" sentence.\n- **Flag argued in surface/ops.ts:** `read_document` and the documents collection resource answer differently on purpose (request-shaped vs render-shaped).","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:25-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"overnight-3 (parity pick a)","pr":"#251 merged 191d7677"}}
{"id":"parity-palette-documents","parent":"md-second-class","ord":"a1","title":"A document is a row in the ⌘K box, matched by its name","done":"2026-08-19T11:01:28-04:00","desc":"Closes the table's \"zero document rows in the palette\" row.\n\n- The palette and the header search box share one module: a served `.md`/`.html` matches by title/filename and opens its page.\n- The served-path matcher moved to `file/matching.ts` beside the `@` completion.\n- **The create row went NO** — the palette has no create row for outlines either, so offering one to documents alone would invert the imbalance, not remove it (argued on the PR and in docs/search.md).\n- **Doctrine held:** the node grammar reads no `.md` body.","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:28-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"overnight-3 (parity pick b)","pr":"#253 merged 4a9ae71b"}}
{"id":"pin-to-sidebar","parent":"viewing","ord":"ak","title":"Pin to sidebar: any node, document, or saved query, one click away","done":"2026-08-19T11:06:26-04:00","desc":"Approved 2026-08-18 evening; PR #246.\n\n- **Shelf:** `_olai/Pins.olai` — the third by-name convention (`pinsIn`, same walk as `inboxIn`) — holding ordinary nodes whose titles are addresses.\n  - A bare address draws the live resolved face; a markdown link `[label](address)` draws the human's own words (ruled 2026-08-19; chip yes, pills no).\n- **No new op and no agent tool:** `read_subtree`/`add_node`/`move_node`/`archive_node` ARE the agent face; the browser's one pin verb resolves to the same add.\n- Shelf sits below the calendar, beside the tree (ruled).\n- **Grok's two objection defects fixed with proven-red tests:**\n  - URIError on `/n/%` killing the sidebar — fixed at `routeOf` where the address bar hits it too.\n  - Reorder in list-local coordinates.\n- **Future:** Archive/Inbox minting into `_olai/` (see olai-convention-dir).","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:44-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"pr":"#246 merged e44e8ae3 (approved by the human 2026-08-19)"}}
{"id":"graph-view","parent":"viewing","ord":"al","title":"Graph view: the reference graph drawn as a navigable map","todo":true,"desc":"Approved 2026-08-18 evening; PR #247.\n\n- **Feature:** `/graph/<id>` is a node's neighbourhood (1 hop, 2 on `?hops=`); `/graph` is the whole reference graph.\n- Derived live from the same indexes Referenced-by reads (`referencesOf` beside `backlinksOf`, whole-corpus consistency test between them, re-verified against #249's re-keyed written-form index).\n- Both edge kinds in written direction, files as spatial groupings, click navigates, hover names ancestry.\n- **Hand-test rounds:**\n  - d3-zoom camera with +/−/Fit.\n  - Labels declutter at every scale.\n  - Canvas fills the viewport (the fixed ~550px box died).\n  - Done nodes hidden by the app-wide done preference, while the filter box still answers `-is:done` as a page question.\n- **Deliberate cost**, argued in `graph.ts`: the corpus page re-walks prose per store revision while open.","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:49-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"pr":"#247 parked as draft 2026-08-19 — the human ruled it unsatisfying: no .md/.olai parity, and bolting parity on would make a ball of mud; waits on the nodes/docs unification architecture (brainstorming doc)","unblocked-by":"brainstorming/first-class-documents.md — rebuilt on addresses at step 4 of its path"}}
{"id":"olai-convention-dir","parent":"infra","ord":"an","title":"_olai/Trash.olai is the one trash — the archive name dies; Inbox.olai stays top-level","done":"2026-08-19T21:52:16-04:00","desc":"Ruled with #246: minted convention files land in `_olai/` (underscore, not dot — the store prunes dot-directories); `Pins.olai` already mints there.\n\n- **CORRECTED AND EXTENDED by the human 2026-08-19** (supersedes the earlier \"Archive.olai and Inbox.olai follow Pins.olai\" spelling):\n\n1. **There is ONE trash: `_olai/Trash.olai`.**\n   - The per-directory Archive.olai convention dies.\n   - Trashing a node from any outline writes into that one file (an entry must therefore record which outline it came from, so untrashing can put it back).\n2. **Inbox.olai stays top-level** — it does not move into `_olai/`; its by-name resolution and root minting are untouched.\n3. **Full rename, the human's word**: the file, the verbs and the operator all say trash.\n   - `archive_node`/`unarchive_node` become `trash_node`/`untrash_node`; `empty_trash` empties `_olai/Trash.olai`; `is:archived` becomes `is:trashed`.\n   - \"archive\" as a word leaves the product (tools, search grammar, web faces, docs).\n   - BREAKING for agents; blessed.\n4. **Existing per-directory Archive.olai files are left on disk and STOP being read**: no longer trash, not drawn on the trash page, invisible to `is:trashed` — orphaned until a human hand-moves them.\n   - No migration in this PR.\n\n- **Docs to sweep:** format.md, architecture.md wherever Archive.olai is named, the MCP face/charter text, search grammar docs.\n- **Dispatch shape:** Grok authors, opencode is the single review seat, and the debate happens as PR-comment back-and-forth until both settle (the human's ruling on all three points, 2026-08-19).","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T21:52:16-04:00","custom":{"from":"#246 (the human's ruling 2026-08-19)","pr":"#266 merged 3f70317c"}}
{"id":"dev-server-random-port","parent":"infra","ord":"ao","title":"A dev server never squats the production port — port 0 by default, fixed ports are a deploy's explicit word","done":"2026-08-19T19:28:23-04:00","desc":"Two field incidents in one night, same defect class.\n\n- **(1)** a dev instance bound `127.0.0.1:7714` — the production port — so the orchestrator's olai MCP answered with the dev vault's outlines all evening and the ledger was wrongly believed unreachable.\n- **(2)** the empty-trash lane's e2e dialed ANOTHER worktree's server through the shared `/tmp/olai-dev` convention and failed against a foreign bundle.\n- **Fix:** dev and e2e servers bind port 0 (OS-assigned), print the port at startup and write it to a per-worktree file the harness reads back; a fixed `--port` is something only a deploy passes explicitly.\n- Then a dev instance cannot squat production and two worktrees cannot dial each other.","created":"2026-08-19T11:02:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:28:23-04:00","custom":{"from":"2026-08-19 incident (the human's diagnosis)","pr":"#264 merged 82b1c543"}}
{"id":"fcd-pr1-addresses","parent":"md-second-class","ord":"a2","title":"Addresses: the [document]#[element] grammar, URL = / + address — PR 1 of first-class documents","done":"2026-08-19T14:38:19-04:00","desc":"Dispatched 2026-08-19 on the human's word, to Opus.\n\n- **Scope:** the brainstorm's \"PR 1 — addresses\", self-contained.\n  - The branded primitives and the Address sum with `parseAddress`/`printAddress` and the bijection test.\n  - `routes.ts` rebuilt so a content URL is `/` + address.\n  - `/o/` `/doc/` `/n/` deleted in the same diff.\n  - `Pins.olai` titles swept to the new spelling.\n- Compat break blessed by the human.","created":"2026-08-19T12:43:48-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:09:19-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","branch":"fcd-addresses","from":"brainstorming/first-class-documents.md","pr":"#256 merged 675886e0 (approved by the human 2026-08-19; 874/874 e2e, evidence visually verified)","terminal":"6079d86f-0a99-44ae-b591-5c2d7f0a4a25"}}
{"id":"private-dir-export","parent":"infra","ord":"ap","title":"isPrivateOwnedDir exports from kolu; olai deletes its copy — debate #3 finding 3, both-side PRs","done":"2026-08-19T16:55:36-04:00","desc":"Dispatched 2026-08-19 on the human's word while they read the debate conclusion (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md, finding 3).\n\n- **Two PRs by one Grok lane:**\n  - **(1) kolu** — export the `isPrivateOwnedDir` predicate from `@kolu/surface`'s unix-socket module.\n  - **(2) olai** — bump the kolu pin and delete `notPrivatelyOurs` (packages/server/src/lock.ts:318-334, which carries its own death-note: \"if upstream ever exports it, this function is the thing to delete\").\n- Signed by all three debaters across three rounds; sized as a fix, not a vault.","created":"2026-08-19T13:49:45-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:10:00-04:00","custom":{"agent":"grok","from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 3","kolu-pr":"#2186 merged 1b3c20b5 (approved by the human 2026-08-19); olai-side PR B in flight","olai-pr":"#259 merged 0f551b2f — merged by the pipeline's own law (dag-pr-deferrals: a no-deferrals report skips the human gate), after the orchestrator wrongly parked it on an invented approval; both reviews do-not-object, CI green at a1d29c02. Finding 3 closed whole.","terminal":"0b26abe6-7c68-428a-ac42-d1a91019f734"}}
{"id":"fcd-pr2-face","parent":"md-second-class","ord":"a3","title":"The face: Document = Outline | Markdown, the set serves one collection — PR 2 of first-class documents","done":"2026-08-19T17:09:45-04:00","desc":"Dispatched 2026-08-19 on the human's word, to Opus, immediately after PR 1 (#256) merged.\n\n- **Scope:** the brainstorm's \"PR 2 — the face\", self-contained.\n  - The `Outline | Markdown` sum with the derived markdown face.\n  - The set serves it as THE collection, with the parallel nodes/documents exports deleted and every importer migrated.\n  - Search walks Document and hits carry addresses (closes search-document-bodies).\n  - Palette and backlinks ride the same index.\n- **Carries PR 1's two named deferrals that belong here:**\n  - Route's three content arms collapse toward one Address-carrying arm.\n  - `DocumentPath`'s constructor rule moves into a schema filter the day an Address is decoded off a wire.","created":"2026-08-19T14:38:27-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:10:00-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","branch":"fcd-face","from":"brainstorming/first-class-documents.md","pr":"#258 merged 29f4ec38 (approved by the human 2026-08-19; grok + opencode both do-not-object; evidence visually verified; final head df2b94a6 was the conflict-free master merge with #257)"}}
{"id":"surface-deltas-frame","parent":"infra","ord":"aq","title":"The deltas frame is the unit of update — kolu hands \"what changed\" through; deriving.ts dies #upstream","done":"2026-08-19T18:12:02-04:00","desc":"Debate #3's headline (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md finding 1), ratified by the human 2026-08-19.\n\n- **Change:** ONE socket in `@kolu/surface`'s client half, two faces shipping together.\n  - The named-key in-place merge (no whole-dict copy, no N-walk — the measured biggest cost of typing into a big vault).\n  - The `fold({init, step})` member on deltas-verb handles, type-gated.\n- **Amendment from the kolu-benefit survey:** export `useCollectionDeltas` from the solid barrel.\n- `rev` stays (wire contract); `@olai/format`'s patch stays.\n- **Spec** with signatures, semantics and edge cases: docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md §Finding 1.\n- **Beneficiaries proven:**\n  - olai deletes `deriving.ts` whole (`outlines.ts` hands frames straight to patch).\n  - drishti deletes its hand-rolled `foldProcessDeltas` (the drishti pair-PR is the adoption vehicle, not a re-green).\n  - Four more drishti collections stop paying the silent copy.\n- **Ships** as a kolu PR under the drishti pair-PR gate + odu-impact check (additive; expected verdict adoption-opportunity, to be confirmed by the mandated grep), then olai bumps the pin and the deletion is the installation.","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:10:00-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus, terminal f08e17da-421c-47bc-8ff1-05146cda854a, kolu worktree surface-deltas-frame (one lane, two PRs, drishti+odu along the way — dispatched 2026-08-19)","drishti":"#143 merged 185efde4 — foldProcessDeltas deleted, the process table adopts the exported hook; olai's deletion PR in flight (lane vaults-installed)","from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 1","kolu-pr":"#2187 merged b4694c28 (approved by the human; both reviews do-not-object; --admin merge since kolu's base policy refuses self-approval). Remaining: drishti #143 re-pin + merge, then olai deletes deriving.ts at the pin bump","olai-pr":"#263 merged b33fea13 (approved by the human, pipeline waived for the deletion shape) — deriving.ts died whole; kolu's own e2e bench carries the kill: up to 937× by frame shape; deferrals filed as vaults-installed-deferrals","spec":"docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md"}}
{"id":"surface-holders","parent":"infra","ord":"ar","title":"CollectionHandlerDeps.holders — the framework says when the last reader leaves; holding.ts dies #upstream","done":"2026-08-19T18:12:03-04:00","desc":"Debate #3 finding 2 (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md), ratified by the human 2026-08-19.\n\n- **Change:** one OPTIONAL member on kolu's `CollectionHandlerDeps`: `holders?: (key) => Effect<unknown, never, Scope>`.\n  - Run via `Stream.unwrap` in the per-reader get stream's own scope, BEFORE `readOne` (the pull order is contract; `holding.ts`'s test moves upstream as the framework's pin).\n  - Scope close is the release; never error channel (a defect crashes that subscription loudly, no unheld degrade).\n  - Absent → byte-identical path.\n- **Spec:** docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md §Finding 2.\n- **Grenade already went off here:** the #229 sixteen-path LRU.\n- olai deletes `holding.ts` + its test whole; `runtime.ts` says `holders: bodies.held`; `bodies.ts` stays entirely; the client-side askers map stays out (separate axis, ruled).\n- odu's logs store is a proven second consumer (adoption-opportunity on its ledger at next bump).\n- Same shipping gates as surface-deltas-frame; ranked under it by the debate (younger plug, one consumer).","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:26-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:10:00-04:00","custom":{"agent":"same lane as surface-deltas-frame (terminal f08e17da) — second PR from a second branch after the first opens","drishti":"#144 closed as a no-op — #143 landed first carrying the same pin; nothing to adopt (drishti impact was nil, as the review proved by grep)","from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 2","kolu-pr":"#2188 merged f648f0a2 (approved by the human; both reviews do-not-object; one conflict round after #2187 landed, resolved by master merge at 59cc7dcd). Remaining: drishti #144 merge, then olai deletes holding.ts at the pin bump","olai-pr":"#263 merged b33fea13 — holding.ts and its test died whole; runtime.ts says holders: bodies.held; the pull-order pin verified living upstream before deletion","spec":"docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md"}}
{"id":"debate3-claim-tests","parent":"infra","ord":"as","title":"Three claim tests from debate #3 — promises pinned as tests, not comments","todo":true,"desc":"Ratified 2026-08-19 (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md finding 4). One small PR.\n\n- **(a)** address recognition has one door — `addressIn` delegates to `routeIn`, no module outside `routes.ts` implements recognition, the bijection comparison belongs to `routes.test.ts`.\n  - Was meant to ride the fcd-addresses PR; #256 merged without it, so it lands here — or rides fcd-pr2-face if that diff touches routes anyway.\n- **(b)** `createArrival` call sites keep literal `import()` specifiers (the bundler reads them statically).\n  - Today the rule is a comment at arriving.ts:38-42; the third chunk, ink-mde, is already on the roadmap.\n- **(c) interim** — nothing outside `holding.ts`, its test, and `runtime.ts` spells the get-tag wrap / `Stream.unwrap` hold; this one dies with surface-holders and should say so in its test name.\n- The debate caught two records rotting mid-sitting (the package-survey sentence and the roadmap's store stillness stamp) — that is the argument for these, demonstrated on the debate's own inputs.","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:35-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:10:00-04:00","custom":{"from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 4"}}
{"id":"web-testlib-face","parent":"infra","ord":"at","title":"@olai/web gains ./testlib — sixteen wireless doors into src become one declared face","todo":true,"desc":"Ratified 2026-08-19 (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md finding 5) — boundary hygiene, explicitly NOT counted as a receptacle.\n\n- **Problem:** `packages/tests` imports sixteen distinct `@olai/web/src/client/…` files by package name into `src/`, under a manifest that declares `\"exports\": \"None.\"` — both statements cannot be true.\n- **Fix:** a narrow published test-face (`./testlib`, the convention format/git/log/ops already carry) covering the handles the suite actually needs.\n  - The manifest sentence is rewritten in the same diff — a socket must not be installed against a header that still denies it exists.\n- The one-line `./testids` export was proposed and killed in-debate (a bandage leaving fifteen doors wireless).\n- The room recorded the honest alternatives (rewrite the comment to name reality, or tests stop reaching src) if the human prefers either.","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:43-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:10:00-04:00","custom":{"from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 5"}}
{"id":"search-stamp-operators","parent":"search","ord":"aC","title":"created: and changed: read the stamps — plus a sweep for every other field the grammar cannot ask about","done":"2026-08-19T16:13:24-04:00","desc":"Filed and dispatched 2026-08-19 from the human's ask (\"how do I search for newly added roadmap items? like added in last 30 mins?\").\n\n- **Today:** the answer is `git diff` on the ledger, because the record carries created/changed stamps (ops writes them; node.ts:134-148) but `filter.ts` never reads them.\n- **The feature:** `created:` and `changed:` operators sharing `date:`'s exact value grammar (`created:today`, `created:2026-08-19`, `created:last-week..`).\n- Absence of a stamp selects nothing — a node written before the stamps existed has no past to invent.\n- **Plus, ruled by the human:** an honest survey of every other record field no operator reads, implementing the ones with a real use in the same PR and recording the declined ones with reasons.","created":"2026-08-19T14:45:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:10:00-04:00","custom":{"agent":"claude-opus","branch":"search-stamp-operators","from":"human 2026-08-19","pr":"#257 merged 224e05c2 (approved by the human 2026-08-19; grok objected and re-verdicted do-not-object on 1a5df1b6, opencode do-not-object, evidence visually verified). Shipped: created:/changed: with date:'s grammar, is:mirrored from the sweep, has:blocks declined (needs a reverse of Derived.blocked), has:children/has:tag deferred","terminal":"a44f2fe4-7edd-4d75-ac5d-437e49b733c4"}}
{"id":"performance","ord":"zzVVVV","title":"Performance","desc":"Opened 2026-08-19 on the human's ruling, from the PR #258 search-complexity question.\n\n- **Ruling:** when olai supports large vaults, the hot paths must not be LINEAR in vault size — indices are maintained iteratively (pay O(change) per edit), never recomputed per event.\n- Children are the known O(n)-per-event costs, each filed with what event pays and what it scales with.","created":"2026-08-19T16:46:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:10:00-04:00"}
{"id":"search-index","parent":"performance","ord":"a0","title":"An iteratively-maintained search index — a query stops costing O(corpus)","todo":true,"desc":"Ruled by the human: search must not be linear when vaults are large.\n\n- **Today:** a query is a case-folded substring scan over every node's folded fields and (after #258) every document body — O(total corpus bytes) per keystroke.\n  - Two memoization layers exist (face at decode; folded text per value in a WeakMap) that amortize the FOLD but not the SCAN.\n- **The index this buys:** maintained iteratively at the same seam the folds live (an edit updates the index for what changed, O(change)).\n  - Serves the existing grammar (substring semantics — so trigram or suffix-automaton class, not a tokenizer that would change what matches).\n- The WeakMap fold seam in `filter.ts` is the slot.\n- **Trigger honesty:** file with a bench arm measuring body-scan cost at realistic vault sizes, so adoption is a number, not a feeling.","after":["search-server-side"],"created":"2026-08-19T16:46:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T20:04:37-04:00","custom":{"brainstorm":"brainstorming/search-index.md","from":"human 2026-08-19 (PR #258 question)"}}
{"id":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","parent":"performance","ord":"a1","title":"The O(n) sweep — every per-event corpus cost still standing, verified against the tree","desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 on the human's ruling, from a whole-tree sweep at 1b7bac88.\n\n- Only UN-mitigated costs are here — the sweep's already-fixed list (the matcher fold, taggedBy, byFile/namedBy, the patcher, the browser fold, the byId overlay, bucket caps, debounces) is long and stays fixed.\n- **Measured anchors:**\n  - `filter.bench` 9.61ms/keystroke warm at 20k nodes.\n  - composer ~10ms/keystroke at 20k.\n  - `deriving.bench` 51.4ms/frame at 980 files, of which 28ms is the framework merge (dying upstream via surface-deltas-frame).","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:10:00-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-dates-index","parent":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","ord":"a0","title":"Dates are derived at view time over every node, stored nowhere — agenda/calendar/day pay a full walk per edit anywhere","done":"2026-08-20T04:34:18-04:00","desc":"- `dates.ts:231` `datedNodes` flatMaps every record, no memo, no WeakMap; `agenda.ts:6` says it in so many words.\n- `App.tsx:99`'s agenda memo re-runs on every derivation change (= every edit in the vault).\n- `datedDays` (`dates.ts:275`) is a second independent full walk per month navigated.\n- `datedOn` → full walk per day-page resolution.\n- **The fix** shape the house already owns: a dated index on `Derived`, maintained by the patcher like `taggedBy`.","after":["search-server-side"],"created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T04:34:18-04:00","custom":{"pr":"#278 merged 563c6d3d"}}
{"id":"perf-validate-incremental","parent":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","ord":"a1","title":"Five of six validation rules walk every record, per write and per probe tick","todo":true,"desc":"validate.ts:105-110: reportDuplicateIds, checkParents, checkAfterAcyclic, checkMirrorContainment, checkDocs all iterate set.nodes whole; only checkTargets reads an index. model-indices.md:139 names the narrowing (re-run the cycle check only when the edge set changed) and records it unbuilt. Every write and every publishing probe pays it.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-patch-residue","parent":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","ord":"a2","title":"The patcher's residue: a fresh flat array of every record per patch, and nine index clones","todo":true,"desc":"- `patch.ts:283` allocates `[...ordered.values()].flat()` — every record in the directory, per patch, both sides of the wire.\n- `patch.ts:257` `new Map(byFile)` is O(files).\n- `patch.bench.ts:419-443` names the nine clones the overlay did not absorb: children, status, after, blocked, byFile, mirrorsOf, edgesTo, namedBy, taggedBy.\n- `model-indices.md:136` ranks the clones #2 of what a keystroke costs a tab, right after the framework merge that surface-deltas-frame is deleting.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:10:01-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-published-maps","parent":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","ord":"a3","title":"Publishing rebuilds ~3× O(files) of Maps per revision","todo":true,"desc":"published.ts:190 changeOf builds a fresh entries Map over every file, called three times per revision (outlines, documents, heads — published.ts:141,155,228-241), plus new Map(set.broken) and the O(documents) upserts/unread split. Unchanged entries carried by reference (correctness), but the Map shells are re-minted every revision.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-list-documents-bytes","parent":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","ord":"a4","title":"list_documents is O(bytes of every served .md) — the cheaper form is named in the code","todo":true,"desc":"documents.ts:387-396 admits the cost class and names the fix: @olai/store decodes each file and throws away the byte count the read already had; carrying it onto Document makes the listing O(documents) and deletes the question. Paid at query.ts:536 per list_documents call.","created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00"}
{"id":"perf-filter-scope","parent":"perf-sweep-2026-08-19","ord":"a5","title":"file:/under: narrowing does not narrow the walk — and under: costs O(nodes × depth)","todo":true,"desc":"filter.ts:1841-1855: scoping is a predicate applied INSIDE the full walk, so a query scoped to one outline still visits every node in the vault; under: additionally calls ancestorsOf per node. Rides behind search-index (see-edge): an index that serves the grammar should serve the scopes too — byFile already exists for the file: half.","after":["search-index"],"created":"2026-08-19T16:58:59-04:00"}
{"id":"vaults-installed-deferrals","parent":"performance","ord":"a5","title":"What PR #263 left, in so many words — the fold's reconnect cold-start, the missing composition bench, chat's fold adoption, one unpinned patch claim","done":"2026-08-19T19:39:56-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 from #263's deferrals section (the dag gate: a deferral becomes a roadmap node before the merge).\n\n- **(1)** a reconnect re-initialises the fold with freshly decoded entries while the store value-diffs and keeps identity — so after a link flap the per-record WeakMap search fold goes cold corpus-wide; design-ruled, worth its own look.\n- **(2)** no browser-side benchmark measures the composition a tab actually pays any more (kolu benches the merge, patch.bench the patch) — outlines.ts carries this note in its own text.\n- **(3)** `chat/state.ts`'s rows re-reads `seq` off every key and re-sorts the transcript per frame; transcript declares deltas so it gained fold too — an adoption opportunity the design never ruled on.\n- **(4)** `patch.test.ts` has no case for an upsert carrying no records — the file-arrives-empty-fills-empties-goes life was pinned only by the deleted `deriving.test.ts`; one format-suite case closes it.\n- (Deferral 6 of the PR — patch's flat-list allocation — is already filed as perf-patch-residue; 3 and 7 were deliberate and reasoned.)","created":"2026-08-19T18:11:31-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:57:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #263 deferrals","pr":"#265 merged 1cc4cd65"}}
{"id":"reconnect-seed-upstream","parent":"performance","ord":"a3","title":"The reconnect seed's real home is upstream — kolu's syntheticSnapshot on the wire-snapshot path deletes olai's stopgap","done":"2026-08-20T10:28:07-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 at #265's merge (the dag gate: a deferral becomes a roadmap node before the merge).\n- olai #265 fixed the post-flap fold cold-start by seeding from the store (seedOf) and calls itself a stopgap in so many words.\n- kolu already has syntheticSnapshot and already uses it to seed a mid-stream registration; one line upstream on the wire-snapshot path makes init hand back the store's own objects.\n- When that lands: olai deletes seedOf, its test, and the bench's wire arm.\n- Author's bench for scale: one post-flap search 29.9ms wire-seeded vs 16.3ms store-held (980 files / 21,552 records).\n- **DONE 2026-08-20.** The olai half went first, for another reason: #279 (the flip) deleted seedOf, its test and the bench arm with the rest of the browser-held vault. The kolu half is kolu#2189 (merged 2d72179a5, Opus; grok do-not-object with an out-of-tree mutation check): the wire-snapshot arm seeds every fold from `syntheticSnapshot()` after `applySnapshot`, so a fold gets the store's own objects whether it registered before or after the snapshot — one answer, pinned by a reconnect-identity test. Downstream checked: drishti and odu register no folds; no pair PR.","created":"2026-08-19T19:39:07-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T10:28:07-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #265 deferral 1","repo":"kolu"}}
{"id":"perf-faces-broken-walk","parent":"performance","ord":"a4","title":"faces/broken walks every key per frame — +0.1 to +0.3ms of a ~4.5ms frame","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-19 at #265's merge (rode #263 as deferral 3; #265 numbered it without touching it).\n- faces/broken walks every key per frame; measured +0.1 to +0.3ms of a ~4.5ms frame (spread stated where the numbers live, packages/web/README.md).\n- /simplify in #265 found the cheaper form for whoever picks it up (see the PR's refactor commits for the note).\n- Deliberately untouched by #265 — not one of its four items.","created":"2026-08-19T19:39:07-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #263 deferral 3, requantified by #265"}}
{"id":"vault-in-browser","parent":"performance","ord":"Zz","title":"The browser holds the whole vault — stops scaling at thousands of documents","done":"2026-08-20T07:26:38-04:00","desc":"The human's ruling, 2026-08-19, in their words: this is not a 'good' thing — when we have 1000s of .md files it will start to suck. To resolve.\n\n- **The target, ruled**: the browser can at most only have the CURRENT PAGE's data in memory — never the whole vault.\n- **Design**: brainstorming/vault-in-browser.md (Fable, 2026-08-19; iterated with the human in the designer's terminal). The wire goes page-scoped; the format layer does not move; the browser's half of the fold dies.\n- **Staging law, the human's words**: \"I won't accept 'The ugly coexistence'. Every PR must be self-contained, leaving no legacy code.\"\n- **The settled sequence — ten PRs**: (1) search-server-side [first; already its own node] · (2) tag vocabulary · (3) transcript id-marking · (4) calendar dots + agenda count · (5) pins · (6) fold re-filing · (7) read_node gains blocked-status · (8) the date index · (9) the offline overlay — 2–9 in any order, each complete on its own merits with its local walk deleted in the same diff · (10) LAST: the big one — the new wire member, all seven routes flipping to it, the whole-set machinery deleted, one diff, with the parity test and the before/after byte measurement riding it. PR 10 cannot be split: the law forbids both shipping the member unused and flipping routes one at a time; PRs 1–9 exist to shrink it.\n- **Both UX decisions RULED** (doc §5): (a) navigation may round-trip, cache nothing; (b) a dead wire freezes the app under an offline overlay.\n- #204 deflated one part; this replaces the model itself. Lanes dispatch on the human's word.","created":"2026-08-19T19:56:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T07:26:38-04:00","custom":{"done-story":"ALL TEN merged in one night (2026-08-19→20): #270 search, #271 transcript ids, #272 tags, #273 calendar, #274 pins, #275 blocked-status, #276 refile, #277 the offline overlay, #278 the date index, #279 THE FLIP (7e208f77) — the browser holds only the current page's data; first frame 1,679→135 kB (12×); the whole-set fold, DerivedProvider and seedOf are gone; parity property-tested per route before the old path died","from":"the human's ruling 2026-08-19","overnight":"APPROVED by the human 2026-08-19 via question tool: after the e2e cleanup merges, all TEN PRs run overnight on Opus, 3 lanes at a time (PR 1 first alone since 2–9 wait on it; PR 10 last, gated on 2–9) — every one auto-merges on its own green pipeline, none held for morning; deferrals fold into the same PR unless a strong reason is argued"}}
{"id":"search-server-side","parent":"performance","ord":"ZzV","title":"Search goes entirely server-side — the first step out of vault-in-browser","done":"2026-08-20T00:52:43-04:00","desc":"Ruled by the human 2026-08-19: the browser's search boxes (⌘K palette, header box, filter bar) stop scanning the local copy and query the server instead.\n- Engineering that comes with it: per-keystroke round-trips need debounce + stale-response cancellation; results arrive async where they were sync; offline/flap behavior changes and must be decided, not inherited.\n- What it unlocks: the search index no longer needs to run in the browser — server-only shapes (bun:sqlite FTS5 trigram) become first-class candidates instead of a compromise. brainstorming/search-index.md rewrites on this premise.\n- The one-matcher rule bends, not breaks: whatever engine answers, ranking and the grammar stay defined in one place, and an oracle test pins server answers to the reference matcher.","see":["vault-in-browser"],"created":"2026-08-19T19:56:02-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T00:52:43-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human's ruling 2026-08-19","pr":"#270 merged 1954f3c3"}}
