{"id":"e2e-earn-browser","parent":"infra","ord":"au","title":"The e2e suite sheds what a browser doesn't earn — ~150 of 875 scenarios cut on the audit","done":"2026-08-19T22:34:25-04:00","desc":"The human's principle, distilled: an e2e scenario must EARN the browser.\n- Cut categories from the audit: (a) ~67 unit-test-shaped (a unit test already pins the law — filter grammar ×15, move_to_picker ×7, an_external_agent ×14…); (b) ~36 trivial/static render assertions; (c) ~34 one-law-many-doors permutations (keep one representative door); (d) ~14 pixel/geometry pins; (e) a few obsolete (the connection scenarios the offline-overlay ruling replaces are left for THAT PR to rewrite).\n- Every cut must verify its claimed unit-test overlap first; an unpinned claim gets its unit test in the same commit, never a bare delete.\n- The PR also writes the principle into packages/tests/README.md so it binds future authors, and records e2e wall time before/after.\n- KEEP class (earns the browser): stacking via elementFromPoint, real drag/touch, live-wire (watcher edits, reconnects, server death), multi-tab races, CSP/iframe sealing.","created":"2026-08-19T20:50:58-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T22:34:25-04:00","custom":{"agent":"grok","from":"the human 2026-08-19 (audit commissioned in chat; dispatch + merge pre-approved)","pr":"#269 merged c7806133; suite 875→717 scenarios, e2e ~3m32s→~3m7s; principle written into packages/tests/README.md"}}
{"id":"e2e-scratch-sharing","parent":"performance","ord":"a0V","title":"63% of e2e scenarios spawn a private server — share one scratch corpus per feature where files are disjoint","done":"2026-08-20T11:12:01-04:00","desc":"555 of 875 scenarios are @scratch: — each a corpus copy plus an olai process spawned and killed. Families like the_agent (82) and html_previews (32) write disjoint files and could share one scratch corpus per FEATURE instead of per scenario.\n- Worth more wall time than all 150 audit cuts combined; also where the flake census (underload.sh) says the port/lock failures come from.\n- Deliberately out of the e2e-earn-browser cut lane's scope — an infra change with its own risk profile.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #281 (Grok, merged 232c1f8b7), with the premise revised by its own census.** The mechanism: `@share-scratch` on a feature → one corpus copy + one server per feature PER WORKER; collisions OBSERVED by content-hashing the scratch tree after each scenario and failing loudly naming both scenarios and the file; `@own-scratch` opts a scenario out (refused without the feature tag); a shared scenario that restarts its server is refused (`restartGate`, pinned). Census after the cut: 59 features, 724 scenarios, 490 `@scratch`.\n- **What did not hold:** the_agent (76) is NOT file-disjoint — the agent writes the same outlines and conversation state lives in the server and XDG; the UI-edit families all mutate one outline; it_stays_live/backlinks read the original corpus that later scenarios mutate (a write-only observer cannot catch that). Converted: html_previews (19 share / 9 own) and documents (2 / 1) — 16 of 502 spawns saved; converted-file underload 3 runs / 0 drops.\n- What is left is filed: `e2e-scratch-restore-between` (restore files under a live server so overlapping writers could share) and `e2e-underload-full-census` (the full-scale flake census).","created":"2026-08-19T20:50:58-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T11:12:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"the e2e audit 2026-08-19"}}
{"id":"olai-service-sigterm","parent":"infra","ord":"av","title":"olai.service dies by outside SIGTERM after hours up — twice in one night, the ledger goes dark each time","done":"2026-08-20T10:34:15-04:00","desc":"Observed twice while the service ran the pinned binary /nix/store/ylxg…-olai:\n- 23:06 EDT: exit 130 after 2h17m up (journal: received SIGTERM); ledger dark 105 min until the orchestrator restarted it.\n- 06:01 EDT: exit 130 after 5h09m up (journal: received SIGTERM); restarted within the hour.\n- **Mechanism (corrected 2026-08-20 from the live unit):** the unit DID carry `Restart=on-failure` — beside `SuccessExitStatus=130`, which declares the SIGTERM exit a success, so on-failure never fired. At both deaths the journal shows `received SIGTERM` with NO systemd `Stopping`/`Stopped` (the deliberate 20:49 / 08:12 restarts log `Stopped`): something signalled the process directly, in nix-daemon-heavy windows while overnight lanes ran e2e/CI.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #280 (Grok, merged aef63ec76):** `Restart=always` + `RestartSec=1s`, `SuccessExitStatus=130` kept (systemd never restarts a `systemctl stop`, so deliberate stops stay deliberate; a stray SIGTERM now costs ~1s). Proven on transient units without touching the live service; check.nix asserts it; running.md describes it; RCA at docs/RCA/2026-08-20-olai-service-sigterm.md. Darwin already restarted a 130 (`SuccessfulExit=false`).\n- **Sender: unknown.** Every kill path in this repo and in the odu/kolu tooling was read and ruled out in the RCA's table (the e2e harness SIGKILLs its own child; wire/evidence scripts kill `$!`; `just serve` kills its own group; kolu dev-clean checks a state-root manifest; nix builds are PID-namespaced). If it recurs, the unit comes back and the journal's `received SIGTERM` without `Stopped` still names an outside signal.\n- **Third death, 11:54:18 EDT, before the deploy:** same shape (received SIGTERM, `Consumed … over 3h 42min`, no Stopping/Stopped, exit 130 = success, NRestarts=0) under the still-old unit started 08:12. Timing note for the sender hunt: within a minute of the orchestrator spawning reactivity PR 3's Kolu terminal and its Claude Code session booting (11:53–11:54); the earlier two also fell in lane-spawn/CI windows. Ledger dark 4 min — the human deployed at 11:58.\n- **Deployed 2026-08-20 11:58** (home-manager switch by the human): the live unit now reads Restart=always / RestartSec=1s / SuccessExitStatus=130 on /nix/store/i2v7hgc1…-olai. The next outside SIGTERM is the proof; `NRestarts` will say.","created":"2026-08-20T06:51:51-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T11:58:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"the orchestrator's overnight observations 2026-08-19→20"}}
{"id":"chat-links-reload","parent":"bugs","ord":"ai","title":"Chat: a link in the agent's answer full-reloads the app — the transcript answers node chips, not anchors","done":"2026-08-20T11:29:34-04:00","desc":"FOUND by the human after `vault-in-browser` landed (2026-08-20): click a `.md` link in an ACP chat answer and the page reloads from scratch; the same file clicked in the sidebar does not. An audit of every link surface in `packages/web/src/client` found this is the ONE instance — the only internal anchors drawn outside a pane and outside a `<Link>`.\n\n**Why.** The app has exactly two ways an internal link stays in-app: it is a `<Link>` (`router.tsx`), or it is a plain `<a>` inside a pane's `<main>`, whose click bubbles to the pane's delegated listener. The chat panel is mounted BESIDE the panes, and its transcript's only click listener asked one question — `nodeRefIn`, the backtick node-id chips — so every anchor the agent's rendered markdown carried fell through to the browser's default.\n\n**DONE 2026-08-20 — #284 (Opus, merged 1c87295d1; grok do-not-object).** `router.tsx` gained `useFollow`, the one shared tail (`followedSplit` → `openRight`, else `followed` → `go`), called by PageView's listener and the transcript's after its chip check; `useHere` falls back to the focused pane, so a link pressed in the drawer lands where the palette and sidebar land. The fake ACP agent grew a `links` verb; two e2e scenarios click a `.md` link and a `/n/<id>` link (`the page has not reloaded`, the pane shows the target; Alt+click opens to the right). Refactor passes collapsed four wait/click/settle copies in test support onto `world.press(…, modifiers)`. docs/chat.md says it in one sentence.\n- Left for later, filed: `follow-one-unit` — fold `Link` and `Tree.tsx`'s own handler into `useFollow` (every navigation in the app, so not on a bug-fix PR).","see":["external-links-newtab","vault-in-browser"],"created":"2026-08-20T10:30:33-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T11:29:34-04:00"}
{"id":"prefs-git-autopush","parent":"viewing","ord":"am","title":"Prefs gain a Git section with Auto-push — a commit from this browser is followed by a push","done":"2026-08-20T11:50:23-04:00","desc":"The human's ask, 2026-08-20 10:37: add 'Git' to prefs, with an 'Auto-push' setting — when enabled, olai auto-pushes after committing. Reviewer opencode; merge pre-approved by the human.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #283 (Grok, merged b1fb7efdd).** Prefs has a **Git** row with **Auto-push** (default off; browser-local like every other pref, \"sent nowhere\" stays true). When on, a commit from THIS browser's Commit button is followed by the same push the panel's Push button runs (current branch to its upstream, never a force); a failed push shows git's own words in the panel and the commit stands; the `· N unpushed` count stays honest. Agent `commit` ops and `--commit=auto` are untouched — a server-wide policy would be a `--push` flag beside `--commit`, not a pref (stated in the PR body; the human did not redirect).\n- opencode's one finding closed before the merge: the Commit button and `commit()` wait on the same `pushing()` gate as the Push button (`canRecord` in record.ts, pinned), so a commit answered during an in-flight push can no longer silently skip its auto-push.\n- Tests: autopush.test.ts, record.test.ts (mocked push), one Auto-push scenario in committing.feature. Docs: git.md, running.md, web README, website.","created":"2026-08-20T10:41:09-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T11:50:23-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-20","merge":"pre-approved"}}
{"id":"reactivity-after-the-flip","parent":"regressions","ord":"a2","title":"PR #279: the client stops respecting fine-grained reactivity — the sidebar folds and relights on every click, and nine other remount sites","doing":true,"desc":"REPORTED by the human, 2026-08-20: a click on a sidebar entry opens the page in the pane (good) but the whole sidebar re-renders and flickers — which says the flip disrespected Solid's fine-grained reactivity. The ask was every such violation, not just this one.\n\n**The audit is `brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md`** — read it in full before touching anything; it is written so an agent can finish this autonomously: §1 the symptom measured in a browser (16 of 178 sidebar elements destroyed navigating within one folder; 0 across top-level files; the pane remounts with a `Reading…` beat every time), §2 the two framework facts (a kolu stream blanks to `undefined` on every input change; kolu's `reconcile(next, {key:null})` without `merge` replaces every array element per frame — verified against Solid 1.9.14), §3 every finding with `file:line`, severity and a one-line fix, §4 what is already right and must not be touched, §5 the six PRs, §6 the reproduction and the probe that becomes the test.\n\n**The root of the reported symptom**, in one line: `App.tsx:118-212` derives the sidebar's active file, the calendar's open day, the palette's names and undo's file from the focused pane's READING — which blanks for a round trip on every navigation — instead of from the ROUTE, which already knows. Pre-flip it read the route.\n\nThe children are the PRs, in §5's order. PR 1 first (it is the symptom); the rest are independent. The law is `vault-in-browser.md` §6's and HACKING.md's: self-contained PRs, a test per fix, CI green through odu.","see":["vault-in-browser"],"created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T11:10:03-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-route-not-reading","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a0","title":"PR 1: the chrome reads the route, and a navigation swaps the page instead of tearing it down","done":"2026-08-20T12:19:09-04:00","desc":"`brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §3.1 (findings 1.1–1.8) and §5 PR 1.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #285 (Opus, merged e52955f4f; grok do-not-object after re-running the probe itself).** `reading.tsx` holds the last answer across the next question, so `undefined` means only \"this pane was never answered\" and a navigation SWAPS the page instead of tearing it down; `App.tsx` reads `openFile` off `fileNamed(route)` and `openDay` through `requestFor` — the page consulted only for what an address cannot say; `PageView.tsx` gates the FilterBar on `narrowable(route())`; `filter/asking.ts` stops gating its question on the page having rows and asks at once for a query that arrived with an address.\n- Measured (the §6 probe, two client builds, one corpus): sidebar elements destroyed on a within-folder click 11 → 0, three folders deep 37 → 0, a second day of a non-current month 60 → 0 with 144 → 6 sidebar mutations and the month no longer flipping, `aria-current` moving in one observer batch, a `?q=` page drawing one row instead of six-then-one.\n- Tests: four scenarios in `the_chrome_holds_still.feature`, one in `undo.feature`, one line in `pin_to_sidebar.feature` — all six red against master's bundle first. The probe is `packages/tests/support/probe.ts` with reusable steps (`the sidebar did not remount`, `the folder \"…\" stayed open`, `the current mark moved in one frame`, `the month never changed from \"…\"`, `the node \"…\" was never drawn`) for PRs 2–5.\n- Named cost of route-only: a `/#id` that names nothing, and an outline that will not parse, now draw a filter box where they drew none.","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T12:19:09-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-for-by-reference","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a1","title":"PR 2: nine `<For>`s over wire arrays learn their key — crumbs, referrers, edge chips, prop chips, pins, palette hits, @ rows, header search, refusal lines","doing":true,"desc":"`brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §3.2 (2.1–2.10) and §5 PR 2.\n- Fact B (§2): kolu writes frames with `reconcile(next, {key:null})` and no `merge`, so every array ELEMENT is a new object every frame; a `<For>` keyed by reference tears its DOM down per frame (Breadcrumbs, Referrers, EdgePanel, PropsDrawer), per pins frame (Shelf — every `<Pin>` on any rename anywhere), per keystroke (Palette hits, chat CompletionMenu, FilterBar refusal `role=alert` lines — re-announced), per answer (HeaderSearch).\n- Fix: `<Key by=…>` on the stable key the table names, or `<Index>` where positional — the way Shortlist / Completions / NodeRefs / TrashPage already do. Plus an `equals` on `reading.tsx`'s `namesIn` (2.10), which today re-runs every NodeTitle / EdgeRefs on every frame.\n- **Tests:** a browsertest per site (style of `fold/refiling.browsertest.ts`): render, replay an identical frame through the store, assert element identities survived; or the DOM-identity step over a live edit.\n- Mechanical; one PR, or one per area.","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T11:30:08-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-equals-guards","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a2","title":"PR 3: three `equals` and a reset — the HTML preview reloads on the other pane's navigation, the composer re-asks per keystroke, the move-to stream never closes","doing":true,"desc":"`brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §3.3 (3.1–3.4, 4.7) and §5 PR 3.\n- `document/Hypertext.tsx:623` `on(() => [rev(), landingAt()], show)` — `router.landing()` notifies with a fresh object on every push to a heading in ANY pane → the iframe reloads when the other pane navigates. Drive `on` from a string memo.\n- `chat/Composer.tsx:198-204` `subjects` without `equals` reads `draft()` → one `nodes.named` wire call per keystroke while a chip is armed. `equals: sameIds`.\n- `move/moving.tsx:303-307` `standing` is never reset after a landed move → the `moving` stream stays open forever and the page is flattened per frame; `:241-244` the request is rebuilt when another writer moves the row → teardown → every dimmed row un-dims for a round trip. Reset on `saying.said()` expiry; memo the request on `(record, to)`.\n- **Tests:** two-pane preview scenario (iframe `src` set once while the other pane navigates to a heading); composer scenario counting `nodes.named` calls over a typed word; move scenario that lands, waits out the said-line, asserts no `moving` subscription open (`packages/tests/wire.ts` counts).","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T11:53:44-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-per-frame-tax","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a3","title":"PR 4: the per-frame tax — a whole-vault search per frame, two structuredClones of the page per frame for a counter, and six memos without equals","doing":true,"desc":"`brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §3.3 (3.5–3.7), §3.4 (4.1–4.6, 4.8) and §5 PR 4.\n- `filter/asking.ts:293-300`: the frame counter sits outside the debounce → one `search.matching` RPC per page frame while a filter is on, uncoalesced; then a fresh `Map` per answer forces a second full prune. Coalesce; `equals` on `matched`.\n- `reading.tsx:21`: registering `answer.updated` makes kolu deep-compare AND `structuredClone` the whole page twice per frame, to bump an integer. Count frames without clones (may need the upstream item first — if so, a store version on this side, noted).\n- `documents.tsx` `wanted`, `Offline.tsx` `frozen`, `directory.ts` `broken`, `completing.tsx` `trigger`, `Palette.tsx` items-while-closed and per-row `active` (→ `createSelector`), `chat/last.ts` effect-as-derivation over every row's `text` per token, `editing.tsx` flattening the tree three times per frame while a draft is open.\n- **Tests:** `packages/tests/wire.ts` counts calls per frame before/after; unit tests for each `equals`.","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00","changed":"2026-08-20T12:19:23-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-small-c","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a4","title":"PR 5: the C's — landing re-scroll on a rewritten file, indent jumps the caret to the end, Enter picks the previous query's row, a sticky `settling`, a last-wins failure slot","todo":true,"desc":"`brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §3.4 (4.9–4.13) and §5 PR 5. Five small, independent stale-UI items, each with the scenario its row describes. Two of them (4.10 indent/outdent caret, 4.11 `settling`) were reasoned from code and not run — reproduce first; if one does not reproduce, say so in the PR and drop it.","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00"}
{"id":"reactivity-kolu-upstream","parent":"reactivity-after-the-flip","ord":"a5","title":"Upstream (kolu): reconcile without a key replaces every array element per frame; the frame tracker clones the whole page twice","todo":true,"desc":"`brainstorming/reactivity-after-the-flip.md` §2 Fact B and §3.5; in the kolu repo, then an npins bump here.\n- `@kolu/surface/src/solid/writeValue.ts`: `reconcile(next, {key:null})` with no `merge` — let a stream/collection declare its array key (`key` for rows, `id` for names/crumbs/refs) and `merge: true` for keyless arrays. This is the root of every §3.2 site and of the O(rows)-per-frame binding re-evaluation in `Tree.tsx` (2.11), which has no client-side fix.\n- `createSubscription.ts:306+` `createUpdatedTracker.noteFrame`: two `structuredClone`s + a deep `framesEqual` per frame once any `updated` handler exists — a counting mode that does not clone.\n- Verified against Solid 1.9.14 with the replay in §6 (identical frame → `rows[$TRACK]` and `rows[0].node.title` each notify once today; 0 is the target).\n- After it lands: bump the pin, delete whatever 2.10 / 3.6 had to work around on this side.","created":"2026-08-20T10:51:13-04:00"}
{"id":"e2e-scratch-restore-between","parent":"performance","ord":"a6","title":"e2e: restore files between scenarios under a live shared server, so overlapping writers could share a scratch too","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #281's merge (the dag gate: a deferral becomes a roadmap node first; opencode classified this one as real work left, not a finding).\n- #281 shares one scratch + one server per feature per worker only where scenarios' writes are DISJOINT, observed by content hash; a feature whose scenarios rewrite the same file keeps per-scenario copies.\n- Restoring the corpus between scenarios under the still-running server would let overlapping writers share as well — but the store is entitled not to notice a same-length rewrite (the evidence README already says so), so a restore needs a signal the server honours, not just bytes put back. That is the design question.\n- Payoff ceiling: the UI-edit families (keyboard_editing, undo, dragdrop_multiselect, palette_actions, split_and_merge, trash, edge_editing — ~150 scenarios) are the ones this would reach; chat features stay private regardless (server/XDG conversation state).","created":"2026-08-20T11:06:19-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #281 deferral"}}
{"id":"e2e-underload-full-census","parent":"performance","ord":"a7","title":"e2e: run the full-suite flake census at scale (underload.sh RUNS=20 BUSY=48 / SUITES=5) after the scratch-sharing change","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #281's merge (opencode: verification work not yet run — a deferral, not a finding).\n- #281 ran underload.sh on the two converted files only (RUNS=3: 3 runs, 0 drops). The full-suite run at the census's own settings takes hours and the spawn saving was 16 of 502, so the lane did not pay for it.\n- Worth running once, unattended, to learn whether the port/lock failure class moved at all and to re-baseline the census after the ~150-scenario cut and the sharing change. Output is a number in the README's census paragraph, not a code change.","created":"2026-08-20T11:06:24-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #281 deferral"}}
{"id":"follow-one-unit","parent":"infra","ord":"aw","title":"Link and Tree.tsx's own link handler fold into the shared useFollow — one structural spelling of \"route off the event, open it\" #techdebt","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #284's merge from its Deferrals (the dag gate: a thing left \"for the human\" becomes a roadmap node).\n- #284 gave router.tsx a `useFollow` — the one tail (`followedSplit` → `openRight`, else `followed` → `go`) — called by PageView's delegated listener and the chat transcript's. Its altitude pass argued that `Link` and `Tree.tsx:396` carry the same two halves (route-off-the-event + open-it) and could be rewired onto it, deleting two exported functions and making the \"one spelling\" claim structural rather than documentary.\n- Not taken there because it is `Link` — every navigation in the app — changed for zero behaviour on a bug-fix PR whose node said do not widen scope. What WAS taken: the two now spell the force bit identically and the Link docstring no longer overclaims.\n- A behaviour-preserving refactor with the whole navigation e2e surface as its net; worth its own small PR when someone is next in router.tsx.","created":"2026-08-20T11:29:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #284 deferral"}}
{"id":"names-table-once","parent":"infra","ord":"ax","title":"App.tsx and each pane build a names table over the same reading — the focused pane's names are scanned twice per frame #techdebt","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #287's merge from its \"Seen, not touched\" (raised by the efficiency pass).\n- After #287 the names table lives in `names.ts` and holds by value, but `App.tsx` (for the chrome) and each pane (for its own rows) each build one over the focused pane's reading — the same scan twice per frame.\n- The fix is a field on `createReading` and a change to the readings register so the table is derived once beside the reading and read by both — not #287's shape (a `<For>` keying PR).\n- Retired or shrunk by the kolu upstream item (`reactivity-kolu-upstream`) if keyed reconcile lands first, since the per-frame re-derivation is what makes the double scan cost anything.","created":"2026-08-20T13:07:01-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #287 seen-not-touched"}}
{"id":"one-alert-row","parent":"infra","ord":"ay","title":"The palette and the header box hand-roll the role=\"alert\" row the filter bar gets from SaidLine — one list, one sentence, three markups #techdebt","todo":true,"desc":"Filed 2026-08-20 at #287's merge from its \"Seen, not touched\".\n- #287's `refusals.ts` unified the refusal SENTENCE across the filter bar, the palette and the header search box, and keyed their lines so a refusal is no longer re-announced per keystroke.\n- What is still three-fold is the MARKUP: the filter bar draws its row through `SaidLine`, the palette and the header box hand-roll theirs. Unifying it is a change to what three surfaces draw — its own small PR, with the live-region behaviour (one announcement per new refusal) pinned.","created":"2026-08-20T13:07:05-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #287 seen-not-touched"}}
{"id":"archive-migrate-vault","parent":"infra","ord":"az","title":"Migrate this vault's two leftover Archive.olai files into _olai/Trash.olai — the one trash holds what the archives held","doing":true,"desc":"The human's ask, 2026-08-20 13:08: \"did we migrate the old file to new file path? if not do it.\" #266 (olai-convention-dir) shipped the one trash with the 2026-08-19 ruling \"leave-and-stop-reading, no migration\" — so `docs/Archive.olai` (25 records, 6 top-level scaffolds: the roadmap's section titles) and `docs/orchestrator/Archive.olai` (13 records, 1 scaffold \"Lanes\") are still on disk, dormant, and no `_olai/Trash.olai` exists yet.\n- Why a PR and not an op: `trash_node` records the outline a node LEFT as the outermost scaffold — it would write `Archive.olai` where the truth is `roadmap.olai` / `orchestrator/lanes.olai`, and `untrash_node` reads that scaffold to put a node back. A raw edit of the served directory is not the orchestrator's to make. So: a one-off migration PR (Grok, reviewer opencode), merge on the human's word above.\n- Shape: one `_olai/Trash.olai` whose outermost scaffolds are `roadmap.olai` and `orchestrator/lanes.olai`, then the archives' existing ancestor-title chains, then the records with their ids and fields untouched; the two Archive.olai files deleted; the set validates; the trash page draws them; `is:trashed` reaches them; `untrash_node` resolves a sample back into its outline.\n- The product's \"leftover archives stay dormant, no migration\" statement in format.md stays true — this is this vault's own cleanup, not a product feature; whether olai should migrate a user's archives for them is a separate question for the human.","created":"2026-08-20T13:08:58-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-20","merge":"on the human's 'do it'"}}
